1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,560
I know you're tired.

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:07,540
You don't have to do anything here — you
don't even have to stay awake.

3
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:13,700
In a moment I'll begin reading through the
Psalms, slowly, from the beginning.

4
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:18,860
Let them run under your thoughts until
your thoughts go quiet.

5
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:22,620
Get comfortable, and let your eyes close.

6
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:28,520
If there's something you'd like prayed for
tonight, leave it in the comments — I read

7
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:31,380
them, and others here pray through them
too.

8
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:38,280
If this becomes part of how you fall
asleep, subscribing helps you find the next one.

9
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:44,960
Father, I come to you at the end of a
long day, and I don't have much left to bring you.

10
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:47,380
You know how this day went.

11
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:52,420
You know what it asked of me, and you know
the part I couldn't manage.

12
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:57,340
I'm not going to explain it to you — you
were there for all of it.

13
00:00:57,980 --> 00:00:59,580
So I'm setting it down now.

14
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:01,340
Not solving it.

15
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:08,280
Just setting it down, the way a person
sets down something heavy at the door before coming

16
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:09,220
inside.

17
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:12,760
Thank you that you don't ask me to be
strong here.

18
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:18,620
Thank you that the psalms I'm about to
hear were written by people who were tired too

19
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:24,040
— who said so plainly, out loud, and were
not turned away for it.

20
00:01:24,780 --> 00:01:28,580
Quiet the part of me that keeps working
after the work is done.

21
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:30,540
Loosen my shoulders.

22
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:32,180
Slow my breathing.

23
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:38,740
Let your word do what my own thoughts
can't do tonight, which is to make me still.

24
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:41,860
Watch over this house while I sleep.

25
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:46,060
Watch over the people I love, wherever
they are.

26
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:47,680
I'm yours.

27
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:49,080
Amen.

28
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:50,840
Psalm one.

29
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:56,700
Blessed is the man who doesn’t walk in the
counsel of the wicked, nor stand on the path

30
00:01:56,740 --> 00:02:03,100
of sinners, nor sit in the seat of
scoffers; but his delight is in the LORD’s law.

31
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:06,420
On his law he meditates day and night.

32
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:12,660
He will be like a tree planted by the
streams of water, that produces its fruit in its

33
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:15,880
season, whose leaf also does not wither.

34
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:18,620
Whatever he does shall prosper.

35
00:02:19,166 --> 00:02:24,606
The wicked are not so, but are like the
chaff which the wind drives away.

36
00:02:25,786 --> 00:02:31,146
Therefore the wicked shall not stand in
the judgement, nor sinners in the congregation

37
00:02:31,186 --> 00:02:32,266
of the righteous.

38
00:02:32,906 --> 00:02:38,006
For the LORD knows the way of the
righteous, but the way of the wicked shall perish.

39
00:02:39,526 --> 00:02:40,666
Psalm two.

40
00:02:40,706 --> 00:02:45,246
Why do the nations rage, and the peoples
plot a vain thing?

41
00:02:45,786 --> 00:02:52,366
The kings of the earth take a stand,
and the rulers take counsel together, against the

42
00:02:52,406 --> 00:02:58,906
LORD, and against his Anointed, saying, “Let’s
break their bonds apart, and cast their

43
00:02:58,946 --> 00:02:59,946
cords from us.”

44
00:03:00,906 --> 00:03:03,206
He who sits in the heavens will laugh.

45
00:03:03,726 --> 00:03:05,626
The Lord will have them in derision.

46
00:03:06,606 --> 00:03:12,626
Then he will speak to them in his anger,
and terrify them in his wrath: “Yet I have set

47
00:03:12,666 --> 00:03:14,926
my King on my holy hill of Zion.”

48
00:03:16,066 --> 00:03:21,026
I will tell of the decree: The LORD said
to me, “You are my son.

49
00:03:21,746 --> 00:03:23,506
Today I have become your father.

50
00:03:24,146 --> 00:03:30,586
Ask of me, and I will give the
nations for your inheritance, the uttermost parts of the

51
00:03:30,626 --> 00:03:31,846
earth for your possession.

52
00:03:32,686 --> 00:03:35,126
You shall break them with a rod of iron.

53
00:03:35,746 --> 00:03:38,926
You shall dash them in pieces like a
potter’s vessel.”

54
00:03:39,306 --> 00:03:41,626
Now therefore be wise, you kings.

55
00:03:42,426 --> 00:03:44,686
Be instructed, you judges of the earth.

56
00:03:45,166 --> 00:03:48,546
Serve the LORD with fear, and rejoice with
trembling.

57
00:03:49,546 --> 00:03:56,206
Give sincere homage to the Son, lest he be
angry, and you perish on the way, for

58
00:03:56,246 --> 00:03:58,246
his wrath will soon be kindled.

59
00:03:59,066 --> 00:04:01,926
Blessed are all those who take refuge in
him.

60
00:04:02,346 --> 00:04:03,826
Psalm three.

61
00:04:03,866 --> 00:04:07,026
LORD, how my adversaries have increased!

62
00:04:07,786 --> 00:04:10,286
Many are those who rise up against me.

63
00:04:11,146 --> 00:04:16,026
Many there are who say of my soul, “There
is no help for him in God.”

64
00:04:16,066 --> 00:04:17,146
Selah.

65
00:04:17,186 --> 00:04:23,766
But you, LORD, are a shield around me, my
glory, and the one

66
00:04:23,806 --> 00:04:25,266
who lifts up my head.

67
00:04:26,386 --> 00:04:31,806
I cry to the LORD with my voice, and he
answers me out of his holy hill.

68
00:04:31,846 --> 00:04:33,766
Selah.

69
00:04:33,806 --> 00:04:35,886
I laid myself down and slept.

70
00:04:37,206 --> 00:04:40,086
I awakened, for the LORD sustains me.

71
00:04:40,357 --> 00:04:46,397
I will not be afraid of tens of
thousands of people who have set themselves against me

72
00:04:46,437 --> 00:04:47,377
on every side.

73
00:04:48,537 --> 00:04:49,437
Arise, LORD!

74
00:04:50,317 --> 00:04:51,657
Save me, my God!

75
00:04:52,137 --> 00:04:56,377
For you have struck all of my enemies on
the cheek bone.

76
00:04:56,417 --> 00:04:58,797
You have broken the teeth of the wicked.

77
00:04:59,317 --> 00:05:01,217
Salvation belongs to the LORD.

78
00:05:02,137 --> 00:05:03,817
May your blessing be on your people.

79
00:05:03,857 --> 00:05:05,837
Selah.

80
00:05:05,877 --> 00:05:07,837
Psalm four.

81
00:05:07,877 --> 00:05:11,037
Answer me when I call, God of my
righteousness.

82
00:05:12,037 --> 00:05:13,997
Give me relief from my distress.

83
00:05:15,177 --> 00:05:17,617
Have mercy on me, and hear my prayer.

84
00:05:18,797 --> 00:05:23,937
You sons of men, how long shall my glory
be turned into dishonour?

85
00:05:23,977 --> 00:05:26,397
Will you love vanity and seek after
falsehood?

86
00:05:26,437 --> 00:05:28,617
Selah.

87
00:05:28,657 --> 00:05:35,077
But know that the LORD has set apart for
himself him who is godly; The LORD will hear

88
00:05:35,117 --> 00:05:36,297
when I call to him.

89
00:05:37,257 --> 00:05:39,697
Stand in awe, and don’t sin.

90
00:05:40,537 --> 00:05:43,557
Search your own heart on your bed, and be
still.

91
00:05:43,597 --> 00:05:45,437
Selah.

92
00:05:45,477 --> 00:05:47,017
Offer the sacrifices of righteousness.

93
00:05:48,217 --> 00:05:49,537
Put your trust in the LORD.

94
00:05:50,477 --> 00:05:53,217
Many say, “Who will show us any good?”

95
00:05:53,977 --> 00:05:57,237
LORD, let the light of your face shine on
us.

96
00:05:57,917 --> 00:06:03,437
You have put gladness in my heart, more
than when their grain and their new wine are

97
00:06:03,477 --> 00:06:04,377
increased.

98
00:06:05,337 --> 00:06:11,957
In peace I will both lay myself down and
sleep, for you alone, the LORD, make me live

99
00:06:11,997 --> 00:06:12,897
in safety.

100
00:06:13,197 --> 00:06:14,917
Psalm five.

101
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:16,637
Give ear to my words, LORD.

102
00:06:17,317 --> 00:06:18,297
Consider my meditation.

103
00:06:19,737 --> 00:06:24,837
Listen to the voice of my cry, my King and
my God, for I pray to you.

104
00:06:25,697 --> 00:06:28,677
LORD, in the morning you will hear my
voice.

105
00:06:29,617 --> 00:06:34,557
In the morning I will lay my requests
before you, and will watch expectantly.

106
00:06:34,997 --> 00:06:37,977
For you are not a God who has pleasure in
wickedness.

107
00:06:38,797 --> 00:06:40,317
Evil can’t live with you.

108
00:06:40,837 --> 00:06:43,257
The arrogant will not stand in your sight.

109
00:06:44,197 --> 00:06:46,277
You hate all workers of iniquity.

110
00:06:46,937 --> 00:06:49,237
You will destroy those who speak lies.

111
00:06:50,397 --> 00:06:53,477
The LORD abhors the bloodthirsty and
deceitful man.

112
00:06:54,457 --> 00:06:59,657
But as for me, in the abundance of
your loving kindness I will come into your house.

113
00:07:00,337 --> 00:07:03,477
I will bow towards your holy temple in
reverence of you.

114
00:07:04,477 --> 00:07:08,137
Lead me, LORD, in your righteousness
because of my enemies.

115
00:07:08,658 --> 00:07:11,138
Make your way straight before my face.

116
00:07:12,278 --> 00:07:14,498
For there is no faithfulness in their
mouth.

117
00:07:15,358 --> 00:07:16,638
Their heart is destruction.

118
00:07:17,858 --> 00:07:20,398
Their throat is an open tomb.

119
00:07:20,438 --> 00:07:21,918
They flatter with their tongue.

120
00:07:23,258 --> 00:07:24,478
Hold them guilty, God.

121
00:07:25,398 --> 00:07:28,078
Let them fall by their own counsels.

122
00:07:28,118 --> 00:07:32,818
Thrust them out in the multitude of
their transgressions, for they have rebelled against

123
00:07:32,858 --> 00:07:33,758
you.

124
00:07:34,118 --> 00:07:37,038
But let all those who take refuge in you
rejoice.

125
00:07:37,698 --> 00:07:42,058
Let them always shout for joy, because you
defend them.

126
00:07:42,478 --> 00:07:45,678
Let them also who love your name be joyful
in you.

127
00:07:46,378 --> 00:07:47,958
For you will bless the righteous.

128
00:07:48,798 --> 00:07:52,818
LORD, you will surround him with favour as
with a shield.

129
00:07:53,778 --> 00:07:55,398
Psalm six.

130
00:07:55,438 --> 00:08:00,718
LORD, don’t rebuke me in your anger,
neither discipline me in your wrath.

131
00:08:01,658 --> 00:08:04,238
Have mercy on me, LORD, for I am faint.

132
00:08:04,658 --> 00:08:07,958
LORD, heal me, for my bones are troubled.

133
00:08:08,878 --> 00:08:11,078
My soul is also in great anguish.

134
00:08:11,978 --> 00:08:14,038
But you, LORD—how long?

135
00:08:14,838 --> 00:08:15,738
Return, LORD.

136
00:08:16,478 --> 00:08:20,618
Deliver my soul, and save me for your
loving kindness’ sake.

137
00:08:21,598 --> 00:08:24,138
For in death there is no memory of you.

138
00:08:25,058 --> 00:08:27,398
In Sheol, who shall give you thanks?

139
00:08:28,398 --> 00:08:30,178
I am weary with my groaning.

140
00:08:30,618 --> 00:08:32,118
Every night I flood my bed.

141
00:08:33,058 --> 00:08:35,038
I drench my couch with my tears.

142
00:08:35,638 --> 00:08:38,378
My eye wastes away because of grief.

143
00:08:39,118 --> 00:08:41,498
It grows old because of all my
adversaries.

144
00:08:42,698 --> 00:08:48,898
Depart from me, all you workers of iniquity, for
the LORD has heard the voice of my weeping.

145
00:08:49,938 --> 00:08:51,798
The LORD has heard my supplication.

146
00:08:52,798 --> 00:08:54,218
The LORD accepts my prayer.

147
00:08:54,798 --> 00:08:57,778
May all my enemies be ashamed and
dismayed.

148
00:08:58,298 --> 00:09:01,898
They shall turn back, they shall be
disgraced suddenly.

149
00:09:03,158 --> 00:09:04,998
Psalm seven.

150
00:09:05,038 --> 00:09:08,498
LORD, my God, I take refuge in you.

151
00:09:09,298 --> 00:09:15,838
Save me from all those who pursue me, and
deliver me, lest they tear apart my soul like

152
00:09:15,878 --> 00:09:20,258
a lion, ripping it in pieces, while there
is no one to deliver.

153
00:09:20,670 --> 00:09:27,250
LORD, my God, if I have done this, if
there is iniquity in my hands, if I have

154
00:09:27,290 --> 00:09:33,750
rewarded evil to him who was at peace with
me (yes, I have delivered him who without

155
00:09:33,790 --> 00:09:41,170
cause was my adversary), let the enemy
pursue my soul, and overtake it; yes,

156
00:09:41,650 --> 00:09:46,450
let him tread my life down to the earth,
and lay my glory in the dust.

157
00:09:46,490 --> 00:09:48,650
Selah.

158
00:09:48,690 --> 00:09:50,050
Arise, LORD, in your anger.

159
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:53,850
Lift up yourself against the rage of my
adversaries.

160
00:09:54,870 --> 00:09:55,830
Awake for me.

161
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:59,010
You have commanded judgement.

162
00:09:59,050 --> 00:10:01,810
Let the congregation of the peoples
surround you.

163
00:10:02,610 --> 00:10:04,090
Rule over them on high.

164
00:10:05,090 --> 00:10:07,450
The LORD administers judgement to the
peoples.

165
00:10:08,050 --> 00:10:13,410
Judge me, LORD, according to my righteousness,
and to my integrity that is in me.

166
00:10:13,450 --> 00:10:20,030
Oh let the wickedness of the wicked come
to an end, but establish the righteous; their

167
00:10:20,070 --> 00:10:23,010
minds and hearts are searched by the
righteous God.

168
00:10:23,930 --> 00:10:27,650
My shield is with God, who saves the
upright in heart.

169
00:10:28,570 --> 00:10:33,910
God is a righteous judge, yes, a God who
has indignation every day.

170
00:10:34,490 --> 00:10:40,470
If a man doesn’t repent, he will sharpen
his sword; he has bent and strung his bow.

171
00:10:40,510 --> 00:10:44,970
He has also prepared for himself the
instruments of death.

172
00:10:45,930 --> 00:10:47,810
He makes ready his flaming arrows.

173
00:10:48,570 --> 00:10:51,210
Behold, he travails with iniquity.

174
00:10:51,550 --> 00:10:55,230
Yes, he has conceived mischief, and
brought out falsehood.

175
00:10:56,170 --> 00:10:59,850
He has dug a hole, and has fallen into the
pit which he made.

176
00:11:00,770 --> 00:11:03,910
The trouble he causes shall return to his
own head.

177
00:11:04,810 --> 00:11:08,130
His violence shall come down on the crown
of his own head.

178
00:11:08,750 --> 00:11:14,330
I will give thanks to the LORD according
to his righteousness, and will sing praise to

179
00:11:14,370 --> 00:11:15,970
the name of the LORD Most High.

180
00:11:16,690 --> 00:11:18,170
Psalm eight.

181
00:11:18,210 --> 00:11:22,410
LORD, our Lord, how majestic is your name
in all the earth!

182
00:11:23,410 --> 00:11:25,590
You have set your glory above the heavens!

183
00:11:26,550 --> 00:11:32,010
From the lips of babes and infants
you have established strength, because of your adversaries,

184
00:11:33,010 --> 00:11:35,750
that you might silence the enemy and the
avenger.

185
00:11:36,004 --> 00:11:42,604
When I consider your heavens, the work of
your fingers, the moon and the stars, which

186
00:11:42,644 --> 00:11:47,084
you have ordained, what is man, that you
think of him?

187
00:11:48,044 --> 00:11:51,424
What is the son of man, that you care for
him?

188
00:11:51,844 --> 00:11:57,044
For you have made him a little lower than
the angels, and crowned him with glory and

189
00:11:57,084 --> 00:11:58,004
honour.

190
00:11:58,044 --> 00:12:00,724
You make him ruler over the works of your
hands.

191
00:12:01,564 --> 00:12:08,064
You have put all things under his feet:
All sheep and cattle, yes, and

192
00:12:08,104 --> 00:12:15,024
the animals of the field, the birds of the
sky, the fish of the sea, and whatever passes

193
00:12:15,064 --> 00:12:16,684
through the paths of the seas.

194
00:12:17,344 --> 00:12:22,344
LORD, our Lord, how majestic is your name
in all the earth!

195
00:12:23,144 --> 00:12:24,664
Psalm nine.

196
00:12:24,704 --> 00:12:27,664
I will give thanks to the LORD with my
whole heart.

197
00:12:28,544 --> 00:12:30,824
I will tell of all your marvellous works.

198
00:12:31,704 --> 00:12:33,964
I will be glad and rejoice in you.

199
00:12:34,744 --> 00:12:37,724
I will sing praise to your name, O Most
High.

200
00:12:38,104 --> 00:12:42,264
When my enemies turn back, they stumble
and perish in your presence.

201
00:12:43,204 --> 00:12:45,324
For you have maintained my just cause.

202
00:12:46,164 --> 00:12:48,624
You sit on the throne judging righteously.

203
00:12:49,224 --> 00:12:50,884
You have rebuked the nations.

204
00:12:51,884 --> 00:12:53,284
You have destroyed the wicked.

205
00:12:54,084 --> 00:12:57,164
You have blotted out their name forever
and ever.

206
00:12:58,204 --> 00:13:00,824
The enemy is overtaken by endless ruin.

207
00:13:01,744 --> 00:13:05,504
The very memory of the cities which you
have overthrown has perished.

208
00:13:05,544 --> 00:13:07,384
But the LORD reigns forever.

209
00:13:08,164 --> 00:13:11,224
He has prepared his throne for judgement.

210
00:13:11,264 --> 00:13:13,064
He will judge the world in righteousness.

211
00:13:14,244 --> 00:13:17,484
He will administer judgement to the
peoples in uprightness.

212
00:13:18,444 --> 00:13:24,524
The LORD will also be a high tower for
the oppressed; a high tower in times of trouble.

213
00:13:25,074 --> 00:13:31,784
Those who know your name will put their
trust in you, for you, LORD, have not forsaken

214
00:13:31,824 --> 00:13:32,924
those who seek you.

215
00:13:33,964 --> 00:13:40,204
Sing praises to the LORD, who dwells in
Zion, and declare amongst the people what he

216
00:13:40,244 --> 00:13:41,144
has done.

217
00:13:41,204 --> 00:13:43,844
For he who avenges blood remembers them.

218
00:13:44,764 --> 00:13:46,984
He doesn’t forget the cry of the
afflicted.

219
00:13:47,024 --> 00:13:49,164
Have mercy on me, LORD.

220
00:13:49,591 --> 00:13:56,131
See my affliction by those who hate me, and
lift me up from the gates of death, that

221
00:13:56,171 --> 00:13:57,991
I may show all of your praise.

222
00:13:58,811 --> 00:14:03,211
I will rejoice in your salvation in the
gates of the daughter of Zion.

223
00:14:04,051 --> 00:14:07,311
The nations have sunk down in the pit that
they made.

224
00:14:07,871 --> 00:14:11,311
In the net which they hid, their own foot
is taken.

225
00:14:12,051 --> 00:14:13,791
The LORD has made himself known.

226
00:14:14,591 --> 00:14:16,931
He has executed judgement.

227
00:14:16,971 --> 00:14:20,011
The wicked is snared by the work of his
own hands.

228
00:14:20,731 --> 00:14:21,331
Meditation.

229
00:14:21,371 --> 00:14:23,291
Selah.

230
00:14:23,331 --> 00:14:28,691
The wicked shall be turned back to Sheol,
even all the nations that forget God.

231
00:14:29,611 --> 00:14:35,311
For the needy shall not always be forgotten,
nor the hope of the poor perish forever.

232
00:14:36,031 --> 00:14:36,931
Arise, LORD!

233
00:14:37,671 --> 00:14:38,811
Don’t let man prevail.

234
00:14:39,891 --> 00:14:42,011
Let the nations be judged in your sight.

235
00:14:42,731 --> 00:14:44,051
Put them in fear, LORD.

236
00:14:44,791 --> 00:14:47,411
Let the nations know that they are only
men.

237
00:14:47,451 --> 00:14:49,231
Selah.

238
00:14:49,271 --> 00:14:51,231
Psalm ten.

239
00:14:51,271 --> 00:14:53,011
Why do you stand far off, LORD?

240
00:14:53,671 --> 00:14:56,171
Why do you hide yourself in times of
trouble?

241
00:14:57,091 --> 00:14:59,951
In arrogance, the wicked hunt down the
weak.

242
00:15:00,551 --> 00:15:02,851
They are caught in the schemes that they
devise.

243
00:15:04,011 --> 00:15:06,371
For the wicked boasts of his heart’s
cravings.

244
00:15:07,291 --> 00:15:09,971
He blesses the greedy and condemns the
LORD.

245
00:15:10,751 --> 00:15:15,691
The wicked, in the pride of his face, has
no room in his thoughts for God.

246
00:15:16,551 --> 00:15:19,031
His ways are prosperous at all times.

247
00:15:19,671 --> 00:15:23,151
He is arrogant, and your laws are far from
his sight.

248
00:15:24,111 --> 00:15:27,171
As for all his adversaries, he sneers at
them.

249
00:15:27,951 --> 00:15:31,071
He says in his heart, “I shall not be
shaken.

250
00:15:31,791 --> 00:15:34,031
For generations I shall have no trouble.”

251
00:15:34,571 --> 00:15:38,571
His mouth is full of cursing, deceit, and
oppression.

252
00:15:38,611 --> 00:15:41,191
Under his tongue is mischief and iniquity.

253
00:15:41,751 --> 00:15:43,571
He lies in wait near the villages.

254
00:15:44,571 --> 00:15:46,911
From ambushes, he murders the innocent.

255
00:15:48,091 --> 00:15:50,711
His eyes are secretly set against the
helpless.

256
00:15:51,691 --> 00:15:54,871
He lurks in secret as a lion in his
ambush.

257
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:57,471
He lies in wait to catch the helpless.

258
00:15:58,191 --> 00:16:01,571
He catches the helpless when he draws him
in his net.

259
00:16:02,511 --> 00:16:03,611
The helpless are crushed.

260
00:16:04,471 --> 00:16:04,811
They collapse.

261
00:16:04,851 --> 00:16:07,171
They fall under his strength.

262
00:16:08,191 --> 00:16:10,891
He says in his heart, “God has forgotten.

263
00:16:11,409 --> 00:16:12,469
He hides his face.

264
00:16:13,309 --> 00:16:14,529
He will never see it.”

265
00:16:15,449 --> 00:16:16,349
Arise, LORD!

266
00:16:17,089 --> 00:16:18,869
God, lift up your hand!

267
00:16:19,669 --> 00:16:20,869
Don’t forget the helpless.

268
00:16:21,949 --> 00:16:28,129
Why does the wicked person condemn God, and
say in his heart, “God won’t call me into

269
00:16:28,169 --> 00:16:28,969
account?”

270
00:16:29,009 --> 00:16:30,809
But you do see trouble and grief.

271
00:16:31,889 --> 00:16:34,189
You consider it to take it into your hand.

272
00:16:34,689 --> 00:16:36,809
You help the victim and the fatherless.

273
00:16:37,809 --> 00:16:39,169
Break the arm of the wicked.

274
00:16:39,829 --> 00:16:44,969
As for the evil man, seek out his
wickedness until you find none.

275
00:16:45,989 --> 00:16:48,309
The LORD is King forever and ever!

276
00:16:48,689 --> 00:16:50,789
The nations will perish out of his land.

277
00:16:51,929 --> 00:16:54,749
LORD, you have heard the desire of the
humble.

278
00:16:55,609 --> 00:16:56,829
You will prepare their heart.

279
00:16:57,489 --> 00:17:03,249
You will cause your ear to hear, to judge
the fatherless and the oppressed, that man

280
00:17:03,289 --> 00:17:06,429
who is of the earth may terrify no more.

281
00:17:06,469 --> 00:17:07,969
Psalm eleven.

282
00:17:08,009 --> 00:17:09,529
In the LORD, I take refuge.

283
00:17:10,749 --> 00:17:14,669
How can you say to my soul, “Flee as a
bird to your mountain”?

284
00:17:15,709 --> 00:17:18,669
For, behold, the wicked bend their bows.

285
00:17:19,429 --> 00:17:24,429
They set their arrows on the strings, that
they may shoot in darkness at the upright

286
00:17:24,469 --> 00:17:25,369
in heart.

287
00:17:25,989 --> 00:17:29,909
If the foundations are destroyed, what can
the righteous do?

288
00:17:30,749 --> 00:17:32,489
The LORD is in his holy temple.

289
00:17:33,349 --> 00:17:35,269
The LORD is on his throne in heaven.

290
00:17:35,309 --> 00:17:37,109
His eyes observe.

291
00:17:37,749 --> 00:17:39,989
His eyes examine the children of men.

292
00:17:40,729 --> 00:17:46,649
The LORD examines the righteous, but his soul
hates the wicked and him who loves violence.

293
00:17:47,629 --> 00:17:53,889
On the wicked he will rain blazing coals;
fire, sulphur, and scorching wind shall be

294
00:17:53,929 --> 00:17:55,109
the portion of their cup.

295
00:17:56,069 --> 00:17:56,969
For the LORD is righteous.

296
00:17:57,709 --> 00:17:58,609
He loves righteousness.

297
00:17:59,709 --> 00:18:01,529
The upright shall see his face.

298
00:18:02,709 --> 00:18:04,249
Psalm twelve.

299
00:18:04,289 --> 00:18:06,689
Help, LORD; for the godly man ceases.

300
00:18:07,749 --> 00:18:11,089
For the faithful fail from amongst the
children of men.

301
00:18:11,889 --> 00:18:14,569
Everyone lies to his neighbour.

302
00:18:14,609 --> 00:18:18,089
They speak with flattering lips, and with
a double heart.

303
00:18:18,789 --> 00:18:24,409
May the LORD cut off all flattering lips,
and the tongue that boasts, who have said,

304
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:26,609
“With our tongue we will prevail.

305
00:18:27,529 --> 00:18:28,689
Our lips are our own.

306
00:18:29,229 --> 00:18:30,529
Who is lord over us?”

307
00:18:30,872 --> 00:18:36,112
“Because of the oppression of the weak and
because of the groaning of the needy, I will

308
00:18:36,152 --> 00:18:42,172
now arise,” says the LORD; “I will set him
in safety from those who malign him.”

309
00:18:42,972 --> 00:18:50,032
The LORD’s words are flawless words, as
silver refined in a clay furnace, purified seven

310
00:18:50,072 --> 00:18:50,972
times.

311
00:18:51,532 --> 00:18:52,632
You will keep them, LORD.

312
00:18:53,152 --> 00:18:55,852
You will preserve them from this
generation forever.

313
00:18:56,572 --> 00:19:02,972
The wicked walk on every side, when what
is vile is exalted amongst the sons of men.

314
00:19:04,132 --> 00:19:06,072
Psalm thirteen.

315
00:19:06,112 --> 00:19:07,012
How long, LORD?

316
00:19:07,712 --> 00:19:09,012
Will you forget me forever?

317
00:19:10,112 --> 00:19:12,412
How long will you hide your face from me?

318
00:19:13,052 --> 00:19:18,232
How long shall I take counsel in my soul,
having sorrow in my heart every day?

319
00:19:19,012 --> 00:19:21,612
How long shall my enemy triumph over me?

320
00:19:22,492 --> 00:19:25,412
Behold, and answer me, LORD, my God.

321
00:19:25,872 --> 00:19:32,772
Give light to my eyes, lest I sleep in
death; lest my enemy say, “I have prevailed against

322
00:19:32,812 --> 00:19:36,492
him;” lest my adversaries rejoice when I
fall.

323
00:19:37,172 --> 00:19:38,832
But I trust in your loving kindness.

324
00:19:39,552 --> 00:19:41,652
My heart rejoices in your salvation.

325
00:19:42,872 --> 00:19:46,352
I will sing to the LORD, because he has
been good to me.

326
00:19:47,372 --> 00:19:48,952
Psalm fourteen.

327
00:19:48,992 --> 00:19:52,812
The fool has said in his heart, “There is
no God.”

328
00:19:53,232 --> 00:19:54,132
They are corrupt.

329
00:19:54,712 --> 00:19:56,392
They have done abominable deeds.

330
00:19:57,292 --> 00:19:58,992
There is no one who does good.

331
00:19:59,632 --> 00:20:04,532
The LORD looked down from heaven on the children
of men, to see if there were any who

332
00:20:04,572 --> 00:20:06,912
understood, who sought after God.

333
00:20:07,852 --> 00:20:09,192
They have all gone aside.

334
00:20:09,992 --> 00:20:11,632
They have together become corrupt.

335
00:20:12,372 --> 00:20:16,032
There is no one who does good, no, not
one.

336
00:20:16,672 --> 00:20:22,172
Have all the workers of iniquity no knowledge,
who eat up my people as they eat bread,

337
00:20:22,772 --> 00:20:23,992
and don’t call on the LORD?

338
00:20:24,952 --> 00:20:29,672
There they were in great fear, for God is
in the generation of the righteous.

339
00:20:30,692 --> 00:20:34,792
You frustrate the plan of the poor,
because the LORD is his refuge.

340
00:20:35,732 --> 00:20:38,472
Oh that the salvation of Israel would come
out of Zion!

341
00:20:39,612 --> 00:20:45,472
When the LORD restores the fortunes of
his people, then Jacob shall rejoice, and Israel

342
00:20:45,512 --> 00:20:46,412
shall be glad.

343
00:20:47,792 --> 00:20:48,692
Psalm fifteen.

344
00:20:49,079 --> 00:20:51,659
LORD, who shall dwell in your sanctuary?

345
00:20:53,159 --> 00:20:55,099
Who shall live on your holy hill?

346
00:20:56,179 --> 00:21:03,059
He who walks blamelessly and does what is
right, and speaks truth in his heart; he

347
00:21:03,099 --> 00:21:09,979
who doesn’t slander with his tongue, nor does
evil to his friend, nor casts slurs against

348
00:21:10,019 --> 00:21:16,659
his fellow man; in whose eyes a vile
man is despised, but who honours those who fear

349
00:21:16,699 --> 00:21:24,039
the LORD; he who keeps an oath even when
it hurts, and doesn’t change; he

350
00:21:24,079 --> 00:21:29,139
who doesn’t lend out his money for usury,
nor take a bribe against the innocent.

351
00:21:29,679 --> 00:21:32,619
He who does these things shall never be
shaken.

352
00:21:34,059 --> 00:21:35,699
Psalm sixteen.

353
00:21:35,739 --> 00:21:38,819
Preserve me, God, for I take refuge in
you.

354
00:21:39,779 --> 00:21:43,759
My soul, you have said to the LORD, “You
are my Lord.

355
00:21:44,479 --> 00:21:46,839
Apart from you I have no good thing.”

356
00:21:47,859 --> 00:21:52,939
As for the saints who are in the earth,
they are the excellent ones in whom is all my

357
00:21:52,979 --> 00:21:53,879
delight.

358
00:21:54,339 --> 00:21:58,519
Their sorrows shall be multiplied who give
gifts to another god.

359
00:21:59,299 --> 00:22:04,819
Their drink offerings of blood I will not
offer, nor take their names on my lips.

360
00:22:05,959 --> 00:22:08,439
The LORD assigned my portion and my cup.

361
00:22:09,039 --> 00:22:10,779
You made my lot secure.

362
00:22:11,639 --> 00:22:14,619
The lines have fallen to me in pleasant
places.

363
00:22:15,339 --> 00:22:17,459
Yes, I have a good inheritance.

364
00:22:18,559 --> 00:22:21,419
I will bless the LORD, who has given me
counsel.

365
00:22:22,159 --> 00:22:25,459
Yes, my heart instructs me in the night
seasons.

366
00:22:26,439 --> 00:22:28,719
I have set the LORD always before me.

367
00:22:29,399 --> 00:22:33,019
Because he is at my right hand, I shall
not be moved.

368
00:22:33,859 --> 00:22:37,299
Therefore my heart is glad, and my tongue
rejoices.

369
00:22:37,339 --> 00:22:40,459
My body shall also dwell in safety.

370
00:22:41,039 --> 00:22:46,899
For you will not leave my soul in Sheol,
neither will you allow your holy one to see

371
00:22:46,939 --> 00:22:47,839
corruption.

372
00:22:48,459 --> 00:22:50,299
You will show me the path of life.

373
00:22:50,339 --> 00:22:52,879
In your presence is fullness of joy.

374
00:22:54,059 --> 00:22:58,119
In your right hand there are pleasures
forever more.

375
00:22:58,159 --> 00:22:59,829
Psalm seventeen.

376
00:22:59,869 --> 00:23:02,699
Hear, LORD, my righteous plea.

377
00:23:03,499 --> 00:23:07,239
Give ear to my prayer that doesn’t go out
of deceitful lips.

378
00:23:08,279 --> 00:23:10,339
Let my sentence come out of your presence.

379
00:23:11,239 --> 00:23:12,899
Let your eyes look on equity.

380
00:23:13,779 --> 00:23:15,199
You have proved my heart.

381
00:23:15,498 --> 00:23:17,258
You have visited me in the night.

382
00:23:18,018 --> 00:23:20,618
You have tried me, and found nothing.

383
00:23:21,778 --> 00:23:25,118
I have resolved that my mouth shall not
disobey.

384
00:23:25,158 --> 00:23:31,858
As for the deeds of men, by the word of
your lips, I have kept myself from the ways of

385
00:23:31,898 --> 00:23:32,798
the violent.

386
00:23:33,398 --> 00:23:36,398
My steps have held fast to your paths.

387
00:23:37,578 --> 00:23:38,978
My feet have not slipped.

388
00:23:39,798 --> 00:23:43,098
I have called on you, for you will answer
me, God.

389
00:23:44,238 --> 00:23:45,578
Turn your ear to me.

390
00:23:46,418 --> 00:23:47,318
Hear my speech.

391
00:23:48,118 --> 00:23:54,198
Show your marvellous loving kindness, you who
save those who take refuge by your right

392
00:23:54,238 --> 00:23:55,718
hand from their enemies.

393
00:23:56,258 --> 00:23:57,998
Keep me as the apple of your eye.

394
00:23:58,678 --> 00:24:04,638
Hide me under the shadow of your wings,
from the wicked who oppress me, my deadly enemies,

395
00:24:04,678 --> 00:24:06,258
who surround me.

396
00:24:06,938 --> 00:24:09,158
They close up their callous hearts.

397
00:24:09,938 --> 00:24:11,738
With their mouth they speak proudly.

398
00:24:13,258 --> 00:24:15,458
They have now surrounded us in our steps.

399
00:24:16,018 --> 00:24:18,838
They set their eyes to cast us down to the
earth.

400
00:24:19,438 --> 00:24:25,658
He is like a lion that is greedy of his
prey, as it were a young lion lurking in secret

401
00:24:25,698 --> 00:24:26,598
places.

402
00:24:27,758 --> 00:24:29,938
Arise, LORD, confront him.

403
00:24:30,538 --> 00:24:31,438
Cast him down.

404
00:24:32,398 --> 00:24:38,678
Deliver my soul from the wicked by your
sword, from men by your hand, LORD, from men

405
00:24:38,718 --> 00:24:41,578
of the world, whose portion is in this
life.

406
00:24:42,278 --> 00:24:44,438
You fill the belly of your cherished ones.

407
00:24:45,538 --> 00:24:49,598
Your sons have plenty, and they store up
wealth for their children.

408
00:24:50,898 --> 00:24:54,318
As for me, I shall see your face in
righteousness.

409
00:24:54,938 --> 00:24:59,018
I shall be satisfied, when I awake, with
seeing your form.

410
00:25:00,398 --> 00:25:02,158
Psalm eighteen.

411
00:25:02,198 --> 00:25:04,518
I love you, LORD, my strength.

412
00:25:05,238 --> 00:25:11,938
The LORD is my rock, my fortress, and my
deliverer; my God, my rock,

413
00:25:12,678 --> 00:25:19,198
in whom I take refuge; my shield, and the
horn of my salvation, my high

414
00:25:19,238 --> 00:25:20,098
tower.

415
00:25:20,138 --> 00:25:25,998
I call on the LORD, who is worthy to be
praised; and I am saved from my enemies.

416
00:25:27,438 --> 00:25:29,438
The cords of death surrounded me.

417
00:25:30,058 --> 00:25:32,438
The floods of ungodliness made me afraid.

418
00:25:33,598 --> 00:25:35,958
The cords of Sheol were around me.

419
00:25:36,858 --> 00:25:38,878
The snares of death came on me.

420
00:25:39,918 --> 00:25:44,078
In my distress I called on the LORD, and
cried to my God.

421
00:25:45,138 --> 00:25:47,218
He heard my voice out of his temple.

422
00:25:47,626 --> 00:25:50,226
My cry before him came into his ears.

423
00:25:51,346 --> 00:25:53,606
Then the earth shook and trembled.

424
00:25:54,346 --> 00:26:00,266
The foundations also of the mountains quaked
and were shaken, because he was angry.

425
00:26:01,206 --> 00:26:03,326
Smoke went out of his nostrils.

426
00:26:04,286 --> 00:26:06,366
Consuming fire came out of his mouth.

427
00:26:06,406 --> 00:26:08,866
Coals were kindled by it.

428
00:26:09,866 --> 00:26:12,566
He bowed the heavens also, and came down.

429
00:26:13,166 --> 00:26:15,246
Thick darkness was under his feet.

430
00:26:16,166 --> 00:26:18,286
He rode on a cherub, and flew.

431
00:26:19,126 --> 00:26:22,206
Yes, he soared on the wings of the wind.

432
00:26:23,106 --> 00:26:30,186
He made darkness his hiding place, his
pavilion around him, darkness of waters, thick

433
00:26:30,226 --> 00:26:31,466
clouds of the skies.

434
00:26:32,246 --> 00:26:38,406
At the brightness before him his thick
clouds passed, hailstones and coals of fire.

435
00:26:38,846 --> 00:26:41,106
The LORD also thundered in the sky.

436
00:26:42,106 --> 00:26:46,586
The Most High uttered his voice:
hailstones and coals of fire.

437
00:26:47,446 --> 00:26:50,086
He sent out his arrows, and scattered
them.

438
00:26:50,786 --> 00:26:53,066
He routed them with great lightning bolts.

439
00:26:54,066 --> 00:26:55,946
Then the channels of waters appeared.

440
00:26:56,766 --> 00:27:02,466
The foundations of the world were laid bare
at your rebuke, LORD, at the blast of the

441
00:27:02,506 --> 00:27:03,806
breath of your nostrils.

442
00:27:04,626 --> 00:27:06,026
He sent from on high.

443
00:27:06,766 --> 00:27:07,666
He took me.

444
00:27:08,066 --> 00:27:09,826
He drew me out of many waters.

445
00:27:10,706 --> 00:27:16,266
He delivered me from my strong enemy, from
those who hated me; for they were too mighty

446
00:27:16,306 --> 00:27:17,206
for me.

447
00:27:17,446 --> 00:27:22,066
They came on me in the day of my calamity,
but the LORD was my support.

448
00:27:22,926 --> 00:27:25,766
He brought me out also into a large place.

449
00:27:26,446 --> 00:27:29,166
He delivered me, because he delighted in
me.

450
00:27:29,946 --> 00:27:32,886
The LORD has rewarded me according to my
righteousness.

451
00:27:33,806 --> 00:27:37,606
According to the cleanness of my hands, he
has recompensed me.

452
00:27:38,166 --> 00:27:43,146
For I have kept the ways of the LORD, and
have not wickedly departed from my God.

453
00:27:43,946 --> 00:27:46,526
For all his ordinances were before me.

454
00:27:47,266 --> 00:27:49,746
I didn’t put away his statutes from me.

455
00:27:50,506 --> 00:27:52,586
I was also blameless with him.

456
00:27:53,366 --> 00:27:55,486
I kept myself from my iniquity.

457
00:27:56,166 --> 00:28:01,566
Therefore the LORD has rewarded me according
to my righteousness, according to the cleanness

458
00:28:01,606 --> 00:28:03,466
of my hands in his eyesight.

459
00:28:04,426 --> 00:28:07,366
With the merciful you will show yourself
merciful.

460
00:28:07,595 --> 00:28:11,015
With the perfect man, you will show
yourself perfect.

461
00:28:12,175 --> 00:28:15,095
With the pure, you will show yourself
pure.

462
00:28:16,275 --> 00:28:19,455
With the crooked you will show yourself
shrewd.

463
00:28:20,295 --> 00:28:25,655
For you will save the afflicted people,
but the arrogant eyes you will bring down.

464
00:28:26,155 --> 00:28:27,935
For you will light my lamp, LORD.

465
00:28:28,855 --> 00:28:30,855
My God will light up my darkness.

466
00:28:31,675 --> 00:28:34,195
For by you, I advance through a troop.

467
00:28:35,015 --> 00:28:37,815
By my God, I leap over a wall.

468
00:28:38,715 --> 00:28:40,935
As for God, his way is perfect.

469
00:28:42,015 --> 00:28:43,455
The LORD’s word is tried.

470
00:28:44,315 --> 00:28:47,755
He is a shield to all those who take
refuge in him.

471
00:28:48,695 --> 00:28:51,075
For who is God, except the LORD?

472
00:28:51,535 --> 00:28:58,135
Who is a rock, besides our God, the God
who arms me with strength, and makes my

473
00:28:58,175 --> 00:28:59,075
way perfect?

474
00:28:59,615 --> 00:29:04,375
He makes my feet like deer’s feet, and
sets me on my high places.

475
00:29:04,875 --> 00:29:09,455
He teaches my hands to war, so that my
arms bend a bow of bronze.

476
00:29:10,555 --> 00:29:13,295
You have also given me the shield of your
salvation.

477
00:29:14,315 --> 00:29:16,155
Your right hand sustains me.

478
00:29:16,935 --> 00:29:19,075
Your gentleness has made me great.

479
00:29:19,995 --> 00:29:24,475
You have enlarged my steps under me, My
feet have not slipped.

480
00:29:25,515 --> 00:29:28,795
I will pursue my enemies, and overtake
them.

481
00:29:29,495 --> 00:29:32,175
I won’t turn away until they are consumed.

482
00:29:33,275 --> 00:29:37,315
I will strike them through, so that they
will not be able to rise.

483
00:29:38,015 --> 00:29:39,675
They shall fall under my feet.

484
00:29:40,555 --> 00:29:43,215
For you have armed me with strength to the
battle.

485
00:29:43,895 --> 00:29:47,495
You have subdued under me those who rose
up against me.

486
00:29:48,115 --> 00:29:53,795
You have also made my enemies turn their backs
to me, that I might cut off those who

487
00:29:53,835 --> 00:29:54,735
hate me.

488
00:29:55,055 --> 00:30:01,535
They cried, but there was no one to save;
even to the LORD, but he didn’t answer them.

489
00:30:02,515 --> 00:30:05,735
Then I beat them small as the dust before
the wind.

490
00:30:06,675 --> 00:30:09,295
I cast them out as the mire of the
streets.

491
00:30:10,355 --> 00:30:13,175
You have delivered me from the strivings
of the people.

492
00:30:13,775 --> 00:30:15,935
You have made me the head of the nations.

493
00:30:16,955 --> 00:30:19,755
A people whom I have not known shall serve
me.

494
00:30:20,395 --> 00:30:22,755
As soon as they hear of me they shall obey
me.

495
00:30:23,655 --> 00:30:26,295
The foreigners shall submit themselves to
me.

496
00:30:26,628 --> 00:30:31,828
The foreigners shall fade away, and shall
come trembling out of their strongholds.

497
00:30:32,628 --> 00:30:33,528
The LORD lives!

498
00:30:34,848 --> 00:30:35,808
Blessed be my rock.

499
00:30:36,768 --> 00:30:43,328
Exalted be the God of my salvation, even
the God who executes vengeance for me, and

500
00:30:43,368 --> 00:30:45,148
subdues peoples under me.

501
00:30:46,028 --> 00:30:47,868
He rescues me from my enemies.

502
00:30:48,768 --> 00:30:52,968
Yes, you lift me up above those who rise
up against me.

503
00:30:53,568 --> 00:30:55,708
You deliver me from the violent man.

504
00:30:56,608 --> 00:31:02,128
Therefore I will give thanks to you, LORD,
amongst the nations, and will sing praises

505
00:31:02,168 --> 00:31:03,068
to your name.

506
00:31:03,628 --> 00:31:09,908
He gives great deliverance to his king,
and shows loving kindness to his anointed, to

507
00:31:09,948 --> 00:31:13,748
David and to his offspring, forever more.

508
00:31:13,788 --> 00:31:15,228
Psalm nineteen.

509
00:31:15,268 --> 00:31:17,948
The heavens declare the glory of God.

510
00:31:18,808 --> 00:31:20,888
The expanse shows his handiwork.

511
00:31:21,688 --> 00:31:27,488
Day after day they pour out speech, and
night after night they display knowledge.

512
00:31:28,248 --> 00:31:31,688
There is no speech nor language where
their voice is not heard.

513
00:31:32,608 --> 00:31:37,628
Their voice has gone out through all the
earth, their words to the end of the world.

514
00:31:38,588 --> 00:31:44,308
In them he has set a tent for the sun,
which is as a bridegroom coming out of his room,

515
00:31:44,988 --> 00:31:47,848
like a strong man rejoicing to run his
course.

516
00:31:48,588 --> 00:31:53,368
His going out is from the end of the
heavens, his circuit to its ends.

517
00:31:54,248 --> 00:31:56,108
There is nothing hidden from its heat.

518
00:31:57,068 --> 00:32:00,128
The LORD’s law is perfect, restoring the
soul.

519
00:32:01,208 --> 00:32:04,828
The LORD’s covenant is sure, making wise
the simple.

520
00:32:05,628 --> 00:32:08,828
The LORD’s precepts are right, rejoicing
the heart.

521
00:32:09,308 --> 00:32:13,288
The LORD’s commandment is pure,
enlightening the eyes.

522
00:32:14,108 --> 00:32:17,288
The fear of the LORD is clean, enduring
forever.

523
00:32:18,508 --> 00:32:22,028
The LORD’s ordinances are true, and
righteous altogether.

524
00:32:23,268 --> 00:32:30,208
They are more to be desired than gold,
yes, than much fine gold, sweeter also than

525
00:32:30,248 --> 00:32:32,768
honey and the extract of the honeycomb.

526
00:32:33,328 --> 00:32:35,808
Moreover your servant is warned by them.

527
00:32:36,448 --> 00:32:38,528
In keeping them there is great reward.

528
00:32:39,528 --> 00:32:40,948
Who can discern his errors?

529
00:32:41,848 --> 00:32:43,288
Forgive me from hidden errors.

530
00:32:44,108 --> 00:32:47,268
Keep back your servant also from
presumptuous sins.

531
00:32:47,726 --> 00:32:49,966
Let them not have dominion over me.

532
00:32:50,786 --> 00:32:51,826
Then I will be upright.

533
00:32:53,106 --> 00:32:56,646
I will be blameless and innocent of great
transgression.

534
00:32:57,806 --> 00:33:03,966
Let the words of my mouth and the
meditation of my heart be acceptable in your sight,

535
00:33:04,766 --> 00:33:07,606
LORD, my rock, and my redeemer.

536
00:33:07,966 --> 00:33:09,866
Psalm twenty.

537
00:33:09,906 --> 00:33:12,426
May the LORD answer you in the day of
trouble.

538
00:33:12,466 --> 00:33:19,146
May the name of the God of Jacob set
you up on high, send you help from the sanctuary,

539
00:33:20,246 --> 00:33:26,466
grant you support from Zion, remember all
your offerings, and accept your burnt sacrifice.

540
00:33:26,506 --> 00:33:28,466
Selah.

541
00:33:28,506 --> 00:33:33,106
May he grant you your heart’s desire, and
fulfil all your counsel.

542
00:33:34,106 --> 00:33:42,406
We will triumph in

543
00:33:42,446 --> 00:33:42,746
your salvation.

544
00:33:42,786 --> 00:33:43,086
In the name of our God, we will set up our
banners.

545
00:33:43,126 --> 00:33:44,026
May the LORD grant all your requests.

546
00:33:44,506 --> 00:33:47,226
Now I know that the LORD saves his
anointed.

547
00:33:48,186 --> 00:33:53,446
He will answer him from his holy heaven,
with the saving strength of his right hand.

548
00:33:54,106 --> 00:34:00,566
Some trust in chariots, and some in horses, but
we trust in the name of the LORD our

549
00:34:00,606 --> 00:34:01,506
God.

550
00:34:01,826 --> 00:34:06,726
They are bowed down and fallen, but we
rise up, and stand upright.

551
00:34:07,966 --> 00:34:08,866
Save, LORD!

552
00:34:09,586 --> 00:34:11,746
Let the King answer us when we call!

553
00:34:11,786 --> 00:34:14,366
Psalm twenty-one.

554
00:34:14,406 --> 00:34:17,026
The king rejoices in your strength, LORD!

555
00:34:17,746 --> 00:34:20,106
How greatly he rejoices in your salvation!

556
00:34:21,526 --> 00:34:26,846
You have given him his heart’s desire, and
have not withheld the request of his lips.

557
00:34:26,886 --> 00:34:28,666
Selah.

558
00:34:28,706 --> 00:34:31,466
For you meet him with the blessings of
goodness.

559
00:34:32,706 --> 00:34:35,326
You set a crown of fine gold on his head.

560
00:34:35,906 --> 00:34:42,526
He asked life of you and you gave it to
him, even length of days forever and ever.

561
00:34:43,466 --> 00:34:45,746
His glory is great in your salvation.

562
00:34:47,066 --> 00:34:49,326
You lay honour and majesty on him.

563
00:34:49,626 --> 00:34:51,966
For you make him most blessed forever.

564
00:34:52,786 --> 00:34:55,866
You make him glad with joy in your
presence.

565
00:34:56,786 --> 00:34:58,626
For the king trusts in the LORD.

566
00:34:58,666 --> 00:35:03,406
Through the loving kindness of the Most
High, he shall not be moved.

567
00:35:04,386 --> 00:35:06,726
Your hand will find out all of your
enemies.

568
00:35:07,866 --> 00:35:10,566
Your right hand will find out those who
hate you.

569
00:35:11,346 --> 00:35:15,246
You will make them as a fiery furnace in
the time of your anger.

570
00:35:15,688 --> 00:35:18,268
The LORD will swallow them up in his
wrath.

571
00:35:19,308 --> 00:35:20,848
The fire shall devour them.

572
00:35:21,788 --> 00:35:27,428
You will destroy their descendants from the
earth, their posterity from amongst the children

573
00:35:27,468 --> 00:35:28,368
of men.

574
00:35:29,208 --> 00:35:31,348
For they intended evil against you.

575
00:35:32,068 --> 00:35:35,248
They plotted evil against you which cannot
succeed.

576
00:35:36,168 --> 00:35:41,368
For you will make them turn their back,
when you aim drawn bows at their face.

577
00:35:42,468 --> 00:35:47,748
Be exalted, LORD, in your strength, so we
will sing and praise your power.

578
00:35:48,248 --> 00:35:49,031
Psalm twenty-two.

579
00:35:49,071 --> 00:35:53,020
My God, my God, why have you forsaken me?

580
00:35:53,060 --> 00:35:59,668
Why are you so far from helping me, and
from the words of my groaning?

581
00:35:59,708 --> 00:36:06,317
My God, I cry in the daytime, but you
don’t answer; in the night season,

582
00:36:06,357 --> 00:36:08,089
and am not silent.

583
00:36:08,129 --> 00:36:12,965
But you are holy, you who inhabit the
praises of Israel.

584
00:36:13,005 --> 00:36:15,181
Our fathers trusted in you.

585
00:36:15,221 --> 00:36:17,840
They trusted, and you delivered them.

586
00:36:17,880 --> 00:36:20,943
They cried to you, and were delivered.

587
00:36:20,983 --> 00:36:24,488
They trusted in you, and were not
disappointed.

588
00:36:24,528 --> 00:36:31,348
But I am a worm, and no man; a reproach of
men, and despised by

589
00:36:31,388 --> 00:36:32,288
the people.

590
00:36:32,768 --> 00:36:34,788
All those who see me mock me.

591
00:36:35,388 --> 00:36:37,148
They insult me with their lips.

592
00:36:37,668 --> 00:36:41,468
They shake their heads, saying, “He trusts
in the LORD.

593
00:36:42,168 --> 00:36:43,328
Let him deliver him.

594
00:36:43,868 --> 00:36:46,808
Let him rescue him, since he delights in
him.”

595
00:36:47,988 --> 00:36:49,628
But you brought me out of the womb.

596
00:36:50,408 --> 00:36:52,928
You made me trust while at my mother’s
breasts.

597
00:36:54,068 --> 00:36:56,348
I was thrown on you from my mother’s womb.

598
00:36:57,288 --> 00:37:00,068
You are my God since my mother bore me.

599
00:37:00,348 --> 00:37:02,968
Don’t be far from me, for trouble is near.

600
00:37:03,848 --> 00:37:05,168
For there is no one to help.

601
00:37:05,908 --> 00:37:07,648
Many bulls have surrounded me.

602
00:37:08,308 --> 00:37:11,368
Strong bulls of Bashan have encircled me.

603
00:37:12,188 --> 00:37:17,488
They open their mouths wide against me,
lions tearing prey and roaring.

604
00:37:18,628 --> 00:37:20,168
I am poured out like water.

605
00:37:20,648 --> 00:37:22,208
All my bones are out of joint.

606
00:37:23,228 --> 00:37:24,428
My heart is like wax.

607
00:37:25,468 --> 00:37:26,848
It is melted within me.

608
00:37:27,748 --> 00:37:31,108
My strength is dried up like a potsherd.

609
00:37:31,148 --> 00:37:33,508
My tongue sticks to the roof of my mouth.

610
00:37:34,348 --> 00:37:36,688
You have brought me into the dust of
death.

611
00:37:37,648 --> 00:37:39,388
For dogs have surrounded me.

612
00:37:40,288 --> 00:37:42,728
A company of evildoers have enclosed me.

613
00:37:42,981 --> 00:37:45,181
They have pierced my hands and feet.

614
00:37:46,141 --> 00:37:48,081
I can count all of my bones.

615
00:37:48,821 --> 00:37:50,661
They look and stare at me.

616
00:37:51,421 --> 00:37:53,741
They divide my garments amongst them.

617
00:37:54,501 --> 00:37:56,481
They cast lots for my clothing.

618
00:37:57,601 --> 00:37:59,161
But don’t be far off, LORD.

619
00:37:59,921 --> 00:38:00,821
You are my help.

620
00:38:01,701 --> 00:38:02,601
Hurry to help me!

621
00:38:03,341 --> 00:38:08,721
Deliver my soul from the sword, my
precious life from the power of the dog.

622
00:38:09,401 --> 00:38:11,701
Save me from the lion’s mouth!

623
00:38:12,521 --> 00:38:17,041
Yes, you have rescued me from the horns of
the wild oxen.

624
00:38:17,801 --> 00:38:19,921
I will declare your name to my brothers.

625
00:38:19,961 --> 00:38:23,041
Amongst the assembly, I will praise you.

626
00:38:23,741 --> 00:38:26,381
You who fear the LORD, praise him!

627
00:38:27,081 --> 00:38:30,161
All you descendants of Jacob, glorify him!

628
00:38:30,901 --> 00:38:34,181
Stand in awe of him, all you descendants
of Israel!

629
00:38:35,161 --> 00:38:40,881
For he has not despised nor abhorred
the affliction of the afflicted, Neither has he

630
00:38:40,921 --> 00:38:45,161
hidden his face from him; but when he
cried to him, he heard.

631
00:38:46,061 --> 00:38:48,481
My praise of you comes in the great
assembly.

632
00:38:49,381 --> 00:38:52,361
I will pay my vows before those who fear
him.

633
00:38:53,381 --> 00:38:55,341
The humble shall eat and be satisfied.

634
00:38:56,641 --> 00:38:59,221
They shall praise the LORD who seek after
him.

635
00:39:00,081 --> 00:39:01,581
Let your hearts live forever.

636
00:39:01,621 --> 00:39:05,881
All the ends of the earth shall remember
and turn to the LORD.

637
00:39:06,781 --> 00:39:10,301
All the relatives of the nations shall
worship before you.

638
00:39:10,881 --> 00:39:12,601
For the kingdom is the LORD’s.

639
00:39:13,261 --> 00:39:15,021
He is the ruler over the nations.

640
00:39:16,121 --> 00:39:18,821
All the rich ones of the earth shall eat
and worship.

641
00:39:19,901 --> 00:39:25,901
All those who go down to the dust shall
bow before him, even he who can’t keep his soul

642
00:39:25,941 --> 00:39:26,461
alive.

643
00:39:26,501 --> 00:39:29,001
Posterity shall serve him.

644
00:39:29,421 --> 00:39:32,121
Future generations shall be told about the
Lord.

645
00:39:32,701 --> 00:39:38,281
They shall come and shall declare his righteousness
to a people that shall be born, for

646
00:39:38,321 --> 00:39:39,221
he has done it.

647
00:39:40,281 --> 00:39:42,641
Psalm twenty-three.

648
00:39:42,681 --> 00:39:45,581
The LORD is my shepherd; I shall lack
nothing.

649
00:39:46,001 --> 00:39:48,481
He makes me lie down in green pastures.

650
00:39:48,961 --> 00:39:51,181
He leads me beside still waters.

651
00:39:52,041 --> 00:39:53,301
He restores my soul.

652
00:39:54,001 --> 00:39:57,741
He guides me in the paths of righteousness
for his name’s sake.

653
00:39:58,087 --> 00:40:04,247
Even though I walk through the valley of the
shadow of death, I will fear no evil, for

654
00:40:04,287 --> 00:40:05,187
you are with me.

655
00:40:06,027 --> 00:40:09,167
Your rod and your staff, they comfort me.

656
00:40:10,087 --> 00:40:13,507
You prepare a table before me in the
presence of my enemies.

657
00:40:14,707 --> 00:40:16,307
You anoint my head with oil.

658
00:40:17,307 --> 00:40:18,387
My cup runs over.

659
00:40:19,447 --> 00:40:25,307
Surely goodness and loving kindness shall follow me
all the days of my life, and I will

660
00:40:25,347 --> 00:40:27,207
dwell in the LORD’s house forever.

661
00:40:28,427 --> 00:40:30,487
Psalm twenty-four.

662
00:40:30,527 --> 00:40:36,667
The earth is the LORD’s, with its fullness;
the world, and those who dwell in it.

663
00:40:36,947 --> 00:40:41,007
For he has founded it on the seas, and
established it on the floods.

664
00:40:41,627 --> 00:40:43,507
Who may ascend to the LORD’s hill?

665
00:40:44,247 --> 00:40:46,247
Who may stand in his holy place?

666
00:40:47,247 --> 00:40:53,167
He who has clean hands and a pure heart;
who has not lifted up his soul to falsehood,

667
00:40:53,207 --> 00:40:55,727
and has not sworn deceitfully.

668
00:40:56,147 --> 00:41:01,087
He shall receive a blessing from the
LORD, righteousness from the God of his salvation.

669
00:41:02,107 --> 00:41:07,767
This is the generation of those who seek
Him, who seek your face—even Jacob.

670
00:41:07,807 --> 00:41:10,407
Selah.

671
00:41:10,447 --> 00:41:12,027
Lift up your heads, you gates!

672
00:41:12,607 --> 00:41:17,667
Be lifted up, you everlasting doors, and
the King of glory will come in.

673
00:41:18,487 --> 00:41:19,887
Who is the King of glory?

674
00:41:20,847 --> 00:41:24,787
The LORD strong and mighty, The LORD
mighty in battle.

675
00:41:25,347 --> 00:41:31,667
Lift up your heads, you gates; yes, lift
them up, you everlasting doors, and the King

676
00:41:31,707 --> 00:41:33,127
of glory will come in.

677
00:41:34,007 --> 00:41:35,387
Who is this King of glory?

678
00:41:36,287 --> 00:41:38,587
The LORD of Armies is the King of glory!

679
00:41:38,627 --> 00:41:40,387
Selah.

680
00:41:40,427 --> 00:41:42,687
Psalm twenty-five.

681
00:41:42,727 --> 00:41:44,807
To you, LORD, I lift up my soul.

682
00:41:45,747 --> 00:41:47,927
My God, I have trusted in you.

683
00:41:48,667 --> 00:41:50,007
Don’t let me be shamed.

684
00:41:50,687 --> 00:41:53,007
Don’t let my enemies triumph over me.

685
00:41:53,767 --> 00:41:57,607
Yes, no one who waits for you will be
shamed.

686
00:41:58,287 --> 00:42:01,947
They will be shamed who deal treacherously
without cause.

687
00:42:03,267 --> 00:42:04,707
Show me your ways, LORD.

688
00:42:05,487 --> 00:42:06,467
Teach me your paths.

689
00:42:07,127 --> 00:42:12,227
Guide me in your truth, and teach me, For
you are the God of my salvation.

690
00:42:13,607 --> 00:42:15,507
I wait for you all day long.

691
00:42:16,327 --> 00:42:22,507
LORD, remember your tender mercies and your
loving kindness, for they are from old times.

692
00:42:22,954 --> 00:42:27,034
Don’t remember the sins of my youth, nor
my transgressions.

693
00:42:27,774 --> 00:42:32,894
Remember me according to your loving
kindness, for your goodness’ sake, LORD.

694
00:42:33,794 --> 00:42:39,694
Good and upright is the LORD, therefore he
will instruct sinners in the way.

695
00:42:40,694 --> 00:42:42,454
He will guide the humble in justice.

696
00:42:43,574 --> 00:42:45,354
He will teach the humble his way.

697
00:42:46,034 --> 00:42:51,814
All the paths of the LORD are loving
kindness and truth to such as keep his covenant

698
00:42:51,854 --> 00:42:52,814
and his testimonies.

699
00:42:54,194 --> 00:42:59,174
For your name’s sake, LORD, pardon my
iniquity, for it is great.

700
00:43:00,254 --> 00:43:02,474
What man is he who fears the LORD?

701
00:43:02,914 --> 00:43:05,594
He shall instruct him in the way that he
shall choose.

702
00:43:06,554 --> 00:43:08,074
His soul will dwell at ease.

703
00:43:08,894 --> 00:43:10,894
His offspring will inherit the land.

704
00:43:12,014 --> 00:43:14,854
The friendship of the LORD is with those
who fear him.

705
00:43:15,534 --> 00:43:17,114
He will show them his covenant.

706
00:43:17,954 --> 00:43:23,054
My eyes are ever on the LORD, for he will
pluck my feet out of the net.

707
00:43:23,454 --> 00:43:28,114
Turn to me, and have mercy on me, for I am
desolate and afflicted.

708
00:43:29,034 --> 00:43:30,794
The troubles of my heart are enlarged.

709
00:43:30,834 --> 00:43:34,194
Oh bring me out of my distresses.

710
00:43:35,334 --> 00:43:37,634
Consider my affliction and my travail.

711
00:43:38,494 --> 00:43:39,614
Forgive all my sins.

712
00:43:40,614 --> 00:43:42,794
Consider my enemies, for they are many.

713
00:43:43,594 --> 00:43:45,214
They hate me with cruel hatred.

714
00:43:45,254 --> 00:43:48,294
Oh keep my soul, and deliver me.

715
00:43:49,034 --> 00:43:52,954
Let me not be disappointed, for I take
refuge in you.

716
00:43:53,514 --> 00:43:57,874
Let integrity and uprightness preserve me,
for I wait for you.

717
00:43:58,774 --> 00:44:02,134
God, redeem Israel out of all his
troubles.

718
00:44:03,194 --> 00:44:05,434
Psalm twenty-six.

719
00:44:05,474 --> 00:44:08,634
Judge me, LORD, for I have walked in my
integrity.

720
00:44:09,274 --> 00:44:12,414
I have trusted also in the LORD without
wavering.

721
00:44:13,174 --> 00:44:15,634
Examine me, LORD, and prove me.

722
00:44:16,314 --> 00:44:18,174
Try my heart and my mind.

723
00:44:18,734 --> 00:44:21,394
For your loving kindness is before my
eyes.

724
00:44:21,914 --> 00:44:23,734
I have walked in your truth.

725
00:44:24,574 --> 00:44:29,774
I have not sat with deceitful men, neither
will I go in with hypocrites.

726
00:44:30,454 --> 00:44:35,134
I hate the assembly of evildoers, and will
not sit with the wicked.

727
00:44:35,774 --> 00:44:42,314
I will wash my hands in innocence, so I
will go about your altar, LORD, that I may

728
00:44:42,354 --> 00:44:47,274
make the voice of thanksgiving to be heard
and tell of all your wondrous deeds.

729
00:44:47,849 --> 00:44:54,289
LORD, I love the habitation of your house,
the place where your glory dwells.

730
00:44:55,069 --> 00:45:01,249
Don’t gather my soul with sinners, nor my
life with bloodthirsty men in whose hands is

731
00:45:01,289 --> 00:45:04,529
wickedness; their right hand is full of
bribes.

732
00:45:05,149 --> 00:45:08,209
But as for me, I will walk in my
integrity.

733
00:45:09,229 --> 00:45:11,629
Redeem me, and be merciful to me.

734
00:45:12,349 --> 00:45:14,349
My foot stands in an even place.

735
00:45:14,929 --> 00:45:17,749
In the congregations I will bless the
LORD.

736
00:45:19,029 --> 00:45:20,209
Psalm twenty-seven.

737
00:45:20,249 --> 00:45:23,429
The LORD is my light and my salvation.

738
00:45:24,709 --> 00:45:25,669
Whom shall I fear?

739
00:45:26,689 --> 00:45:28,469
The LORD is the strength of my life.

740
00:45:29,229 --> 00:45:30,569
Of whom shall I be afraid?

741
00:45:31,489 --> 00:45:38,169
When evildoers came at me to eat up my
flesh, even my adversaries and my foes, they stumbled

742
00:45:38,209 --> 00:45:39,109
and fell.

743
00:45:40,089 --> 00:45:44,189
Though an army should encamp against me,
my heart shall not fear.

744
00:45:45,229 --> 00:45:49,269
Though war should rise against me, even
then I will be confident.

745
00:45:49,989 --> 00:45:56,049
One thing I have asked of the LORD, that I
will seek after: that I may dwell in the LORD’s

746
00:45:56,089 --> 00:46:02,249
house all the days of my life, to see
the LORD’s beauty, and to enquire in his temple.

747
00:46:03,229 --> 00:46:07,329
For in the day of trouble, he will keep me
secretly in his pavilion.

748
00:46:08,009 --> 00:46:11,449
In the secret place of his tabernacle, he
will hide me.

749
00:46:12,069 --> 00:46:13,749
He will lift me up on a rock.

750
00:46:14,569 --> 00:46:18,249
Now my head will be lifted up above my
enemies around me.

751
00:46:18,969 --> 00:46:22,069
I will offer sacrifices of joy in his
tent.

752
00:46:22,529 --> 00:46:26,829
I will sing, yes, I will sing praises to
the LORD.

753
00:46:27,649 --> 00:46:30,609
Hear, LORD, when I cry with my voice.

754
00:46:31,189 --> 00:46:34,249
Have mercy also on me, and answer me.

755
00:46:35,489 --> 00:46:41,149
When you said, “Seek my face,” my heart
said to you, “I will seek your face, LORD.”

756
00:46:42,229 --> 00:46:43,929
Don’t hide your face from me.

757
00:46:44,289 --> 00:46:46,489
Don’t put your servant away in anger.

758
00:46:47,289 --> 00:46:48,329
You have been my help.

759
00:46:49,169 --> 00:46:52,869
Don’t abandon me, neither forsake me, God
of my salvation.

760
00:46:53,949 --> 00:46:58,309
When my father and my mother forsake me,
then the LORD will take me up.

761
00:46:58,349 --> 00:47:00,729
Teach me your way, LORD.

762
00:47:01,689 --> 00:47:04,389
Lead me in a straight path, because of my
enemies.

763
00:47:04,923 --> 00:47:11,583
Don’t deliver me over to the desire
of my adversaries, for false witnesses have risen

764
00:47:11,623 --> 00:47:15,103
up against me, such as breathe out
cruelty.

765
00:47:16,463 --> 00:47:22,683
I am still confident of this: I will see
the goodness of the LORD in the land of the

766
00:47:22,723 --> 00:47:23,623
living.

767
00:47:24,103 --> 00:47:25,123
Wait for the LORD.

768
00:47:26,063 --> 00:47:28,903
Be strong, and let your heart take
courage.

769
00:47:29,683 --> 00:47:31,563
Yes, wait for the LORD.

770
00:47:32,983 --> 00:47:35,103
Psalm twenty-eight.

771
00:47:35,143 --> 00:47:36,723
To you, LORD, I call.

772
00:47:37,843 --> 00:47:44,363
My rock, don’t be deaf to me, lest, if you
are silent to me, I would become

773
00:47:44,403 --> 00:47:46,803
like those who go down into the pit.

774
00:47:47,263 --> 00:47:53,703
Hear the voice of my petitions, when I cry
to you, when I lift up my hands towards your

775
00:47:53,743 --> 00:47:54,943
Most Holy Place.

776
00:47:55,563 --> 00:48:01,003
Don’t draw me away with the wicked, with
the workers of iniquity who speak peace with

777
00:48:01,043 --> 00:48:03,943
their neighbours, but mischief is in their
hearts.

778
00:48:04,783 --> 00:48:09,563
Give them according to their work, and
according to the wickedness of their doings.

779
00:48:10,043 --> 00:48:12,863
Give them according to the operation of
their hands.

780
00:48:13,563 --> 00:48:15,623
Bring back on them what they deserve.

781
00:48:16,323 --> 00:48:22,863
Because they don’t respect the works of the
LORD, nor the operation of his hands, he

782
00:48:22,903 --> 00:48:25,863
will break them down and not build them
up.

783
00:48:26,543 --> 00:48:30,963
Blessed be the LORD, because he has heard
the voice of my petitions.

784
00:48:32,163 --> 00:48:34,583
The LORD is my strength and my shield.

785
00:48:35,283 --> 00:48:38,223
My heart has trusted in him, and I am
helped.

786
00:48:39,103 --> 00:48:41,283
Therefore my heart greatly rejoices.

787
00:48:41,323 --> 00:48:43,843
With my song I will thank him.

788
00:48:44,743 --> 00:48:46,043
The LORD is their strength.

789
00:48:47,003 --> 00:48:49,803
He is a stronghold of salvation to his
anointed.

790
00:48:50,523 --> 00:48:52,823
Save your people, and bless your
inheritance.

791
00:48:53,503 --> 00:48:57,063
Be their shepherd also, and bear them up
forever.

792
00:48:57,843 --> 00:49:00,283
Psalm twenty-nine.

793
00:49:00,323 --> 00:49:06,023
Ascribe to the LORD, you sons of the
mighty, ascribe to the LORD glory and strength.

794
00:49:07,023 --> 00:49:09,943
Ascribe to the LORD the glory due to his
name.

795
00:49:11,043 --> 00:49:13,083
Worship the LORD in holy array.

796
00:49:13,563 --> 00:49:15,343
The LORD’s voice is on the waters.

797
00:49:16,383 --> 00:49:20,443
The God of glory thunders, even the LORD
on many waters.

798
00:49:20,483 --> 00:49:22,743
The LORD’s voice is powerful.

799
00:49:23,963 --> 00:49:25,983
The LORD’s voice is full of majesty.

800
00:49:27,263 --> 00:49:29,363
The LORD’s voice breaks the cedars.

801
00:49:29,556 --> 00:49:33,676
Yes, the LORD breaks in pieces the cedars
of Lebanon.

802
00:49:34,916 --> 00:49:41,836
He makes them also to skip like a calf;
Lebanon and Sirion like a young, wild

803
00:49:41,876 --> 00:49:42,776
ox.

804
00:49:43,755 --> 00:49:46,676
The LORD’s voice strikes with flashes of
lightning.

805
00:49:47,936 --> 00:49:49,956
The LORD’s voice shakes the wilderness.

806
00:49:51,096 --> 00:49:53,316
The LORD shakes the wilderness of Kadesh.

807
00:49:53,356 --> 00:49:59,796
The LORD’s voice makes the deer calve, and
strips the forests bare.

808
00:49:59,836 --> 00:50:02,976
In his temple everything says, “Glory!”

809
00:50:04,136 --> 00:50:06,176
The LORD sat enthroned at the Flood.

810
00:50:07,136 --> 00:50:09,996
Yes, the LORD sits as King forever.

811
00:50:10,596 --> 00:50:12,636
The LORD will give strength to his people.

812
00:50:13,576 --> 00:50:15,636
The LORD will bless his people with peace.

813
00:50:17,016 --> 00:50:18,316
Psalm thirty.

814
00:50:18,356 --> 00:50:24,556
I will extol you, LORD, for you have raised
me up, and have not made my foes to rejoice

815
00:50:24,596 --> 00:50:25,496
over me.

816
00:50:26,295 --> 00:50:30,295
LORD my God, I cried to you, and you have
healed me.

817
00:50:30,916 --> 00:50:34,216
LORD, you have brought up my soul from
Sheol.

818
00:50:34,596 --> 00:50:38,296
You have kept me alive, that I should not
go down to the pit.

819
00:50:38,336 --> 00:50:41,716
Sing praise to the LORD, you saints of
his.

820
00:50:42,556 --> 00:50:44,556
Give thanks to his holy name.

821
00:50:45,436 --> 00:50:47,596
For his anger is but for a moment.

822
00:50:48,356 --> 00:50:50,056
His favour is for a lifetime.

823
00:50:51,136 --> 00:50:55,516
Weeping may stay for the night, but joy
comes in the morning.

824
00:50:56,536 --> 00:51:01,576
As for me, I said in my prosperity, “I
shall never be moved.”

825
00:51:02,176 --> 00:51:08,636
You, LORD, when you favoured me, made my
mountain stand strong; but when you hid your

826
00:51:08,676 --> 00:51:09,896
face, I was troubled.

827
00:51:10,816 --> 00:51:11,956
I cried to you, LORD.

828
00:51:12,576 --> 00:51:18,896
I made supplication to the Lord: “What profit
is there in my destruction, if I go down

829
00:51:18,936 --> 00:51:19,836
to the pit?

830
00:51:20,336 --> 00:51:21,856
Shall the dust praise you?

831
00:51:22,376 --> 00:51:23,795
Shall it declare your truth?

832
00:51:24,476 --> 00:51:27,096
Hear, LORD, and have mercy on me.

833
00:51:28,056 --> 00:51:29,696
LORD, be my helper.”

834
00:51:30,996 --> 00:51:33,896
You have turned my mourning into dancing
for me.

835
00:51:34,196 --> 00:51:40,456
You have removed my sackcloth, and clothed
me with gladness, to the end that my heart

836
00:51:40,496 --> 00:51:43,736
may sing praise to you, and not be silent.

837
00:51:44,775 --> 00:51:48,436
LORD my God, I will give thanks to you
forever!

838
00:51:48,476 --> 00:51:49,576
Psalm thirty-one.

839
00:51:49,616 --> 00:51:49,916
In you, LORD, I take refuge.

840
00:51:49,956 --> 00:51:50,256
Let me never be disappointed.

841
00:51:50,296 --> 00:51:50,596
Deliver me in your righteousness.

842
00:51:50,636 --> 00:51:50,936
Bow down your ear to me.

843
00:51:50,976 --> 00:51:51,876
Deliver me speedily.

844
00:52:03,786 --> 00:52:08,446
Be to me a strong rock, a house of defence
to save me.

845
00:52:09,466 --> 00:52:15,886
For you are my rock and my fortress,
therefore for your name’s sake lead me and guide

846
00:52:15,926 --> 00:52:16,826
me.

847
00:52:17,226 --> 00:52:22,606
Pluck me out of the net that they have
laid secretly for me, for you are my stronghold.

848
00:52:24,026 --> 00:52:26,126
Into your hand I commend my spirit.

849
00:52:26,906 --> 00:52:29,186
You redeem me, LORD, God of truth.

850
00:52:29,926 --> 00:52:34,646
I hate those who regard lying vanities,
but I trust in the LORD.

851
00:52:35,686 --> 00:52:41,066
I will be glad and rejoice in your loving
kindness, for you have seen my affliction.

852
00:52:41,986 --> 00:52:44,246
You have known my soul in adversities.

853
00:52:45,046 --> 00:52:47,766
You have not shut me up into the hand of
the enemy.

854
00:52:48,406 --> 00:52:50,786
You have set my feet in a large place.

855
00:52:51,806 --> 00:52:54,746
Have mercy on me, LORD, for I am in
distress.

856
00:52:55,826 --> 00:52:59,926
My eye, my soul, and my body waste away
with grief.

857
00:53:00,546 --> 00:53:05,046
For my life is spent with sorrow, my years
with sighing.

858
00:53:05,326 --> 00:53:07,846
My strength fails because of my iniquity.

859
00:53:08,546 --> 00:53:10,166
My bones are wasted away.

860
00:53:10,886 --> 00:53:16,266
Because of all my adversaries I have
become utterly contemptible to my neighbours, a

861
00:53:16,306 --> 00:53:17,546
horror to my acquaintances.

862
00:53:18,786 --> 00:53:21,426
Those who saw me on the street fled from
me.

863
00:53:22,226 --> 00:53:24,906
I am forgotten from their hearts like a
dead man.

864
00:53:25,706 --> 00:53:27,306
I am like broken pottery.

865
00:53:27,786 --> 00:53:33,986
For I have heard the slander of many,
terror on every side, while they conspire together

866
00:53:34,026 --> 00:53:37,566
against me, they plot to take away my
life.

867
00:53:38,466 --> 00:53:39,886
But I trust in you, LORD.

868
00:53:40,566 --> 00:53:42,646
I said, “You are my God.”

869
00:53:43,486 --> 00:53:44,966
My times are in your hand.

870
00:53:45,526 --> 00:53:49,906
Deliver me from the hand of my enemies,
and from those who persecute me.

871
00:53:50,466 --> 00:53:52,686
Make your face to shine on your servant.

872
00:53:53,566 --> 00:53:55,446
Save me in your loving kindness.

873
00:53:56,506 --> 00:54:00,466
Let me not be disappointed, LORD, for I
have called on you.

874
00:54:01,486 --> 00:54:03,066
Let the wicked be disappointed.

875
00:54:04,046 --> 00:54:06,566
Let them be silent in Sheol.

876
00:54:06,606 --> 00:54:12,446
Let the lying lips be mute, which
speak against the righteous insolently, with pride

877
00:54:12,486 --> 00:54:13,386
and contempt.

878
00:54:14,146 --> 00:54:19,646
Oh how great is your goodness, which you have
laid up for those who fear you, which you

879
00:54:19,686 --> 00:54:23,986
have worked for those who take refuge in
you, before the sons of men!

880
00:54:24,556 --> 00:54:28,316
In the shelter of your presence you will
hide them from the plotting of man.

881
00:54:29,036 --> 00:54:33,456
You will keep them secretly in a dwelling
away from the strife of tongues.

882
00:54:34,836 --> 00:54:40,836
Praise be to the LORD, for he has shown me
his marvellous loving kindness in a strong

883
00:54:40,876 --> 00:54:41,776
city.

884
00:54:42,096 --> 00:54:47,536
As for me, I said in my haste, “I am cut
off from before your eyes.”

885
00:54:48,696 --> 00:54:53,076
Nevertheless you heard the voice of my
petitions when I cried to you.

886
00:54:53,116 --> 00:54:56,716
Oh love the LORD, all you his saints!

887
00:54:58,016 --> 00:55:03,576
The LORD preserves the faithful, and fully
recompenses him who behaves arrogantly.

888
00:55:04,236 --> 00:55:08,996
Be strong, and let your heart take
courage, all you who hope in the LORD.

889
00:55:10,176 --> 00:55:12,136
Psalm thirty-two.

890
00:55:12,176 --> 00:55:17,056
Blessed is he whose disobedience is
forgiven, whose sin is covered.

891
00:55:17,096 --> 00:55:23,196
Blessed is the man to whom the LORD
doesn’t impute iniquity, in whose spirit there is

892
00:55:23,236 --> 00:55:24,136
no deceit.

893
00:55:24,576 --> 00:55:29,836
When I kept silence, my bones wasted away
through my groaning all day long.

894
00:55:30,916 --> 00:55:33,896
For day and night your hand was heavy on
me.

895
00:55:34,696 --> 00:55:37,056
My strength was sapped in the heat of
summer.

896
00:55:37,096 --> 00:55:39,016
Selah.

897
00:55:39,056 --> 00:55:41,176
I acknowledged my sin to you.

898
00:55:41,816 --> 00:55:43,516
I didn’t hide my iniquity.

899
00:55:44,016 --> 00:55:50,216
I said, I will confess my transgressions to
the LORD, and you forgave the iniquity of

900
00:55:50,256 --> 00:55:50,716
my sin.

901
00:55:50,756 --> 00:55:52,396
Selah.

902
00:55:52,436 --> 00:55:58,056
For this, let everyone who is godly pray
to you in a time when you may be found.

903
00:55:58,476 --> 00:56:02,876
Surely when the great waters overflow,
they shall not reach to him.

904
00:56:03,776 --> 00:56:04,996
You are my hiding place.

905
00:56:05,616 --> 00:56:07,096
You will preserve me from trouble.

906
00:56:08,056 --> 00:56:10,896
You will surround me with songs of
deliverance.

907
00:56:10,936 --> 00:56:13,436
Selah.

908
00:56:13,476 --> 00:56:17,176
I will instruct you and teach you in the
way which you shall go.

909
00:56:18,196 --> 00:56:20,476
I will counsel you with my eye on you.

910
00:56:20,936 --> 00:56:27,116
Don’t be like the horse, or like the
mule, which have no understanding, who are controlled

911
00:56:27,156 --> 00:56:31,396
by bit and bridle, or else they will not
come near to you.

912
00:56:32,216 --> 00:56:38,176
Many sorrows come to the wicked, but
loving kindness shall surround him who trusts in

913
00:56:38,216 --> 00:56:39,116
the LORD.

914
00:56:39,536 --> 00:56:42,596
Be glad in the LORD, and rejoice, you
righteous!

915
00:56:43,198 --> 00:56:47,218
Shout for joy, all you who are upright in
heart!

916
00:56:48,578 --> 00:56:50,818
Psalm thirty-three.

917
00:56:50,858 --> 00:56:52,918
Rejoice in the LORD, you righteous!

918
00:56:54,058 --> 00:56:55,898
Praise is fitting for the upright.

919
00:56:56,998 --> 00:57:00,158
Give thanks to the LORD with the lyre.

920
00:57:00,198 --> 00:57:02,878
Sing praises to him with the harp of ten
strings.

921
00:57:04,298 --> 00:57:05,478
Sing to him a new song.

922
00:57:06,638 --> 00:57:08,738
Play skilfully with a shout of joy!

923
00:57:08,778 --> 00:57:11,118
For the LORD’s word is right.

924
00:57:11,978 --> 00:57:14,018
All his work is done in faithfulness.

925
00:57:14,958 --> 00:57:17,118
He loves righteousness and justice.

926
00:57:18,258 --> 00:57:21,378
The earth is full of the loving kindness
of the LORD.

927
00:57:22,338 --> 00:57:28,298
By the LORD’s word, the heavens were made:
all their army by the breath of his mouth.

928
00:57:28,978 --> 00:57:31,998
He gathers the waters of the sea together
as a heap.

929
00:57:32,818 --> 00:57:35,058
He lays up the deeps in storehouses.

930
00:57:36,178 --> 00:57:37,818
Let all the earth fear the LORD.

931
00:57:37,858 --> 00:57:42,278
Let all the inhabitants of the world stand
in awe of him.

932
00:57:43,018 --> 00:57:45,358
For he spoke, and it was done.

933
00:57:46,298 --> 00:57:48,298
He commanded, and it stood firm.

934
00:57:49,478 --> 00:57:52,618
The LORD brings the counsel of the nations
to nothing.

935
00:57:53,218 --> 00:57:56,218
He makes the thoughts of the peoples to be
of no effect.

936
00:57:57,338 --> 00:58:03,118
The counsel of the LORD stands fast forever,
the thoughts of his heart to all generations.

937
00:58:04,618 --> 00:58:10,818
Blessed is the nation whose God is the LORD,
the people whom he has chosen for his own

938
00:58:10,858 --> 00:58:11,758
inheritance.

939
00:58:12,718 --> 00:58:14,078
The LORD looks from heaven.

940
00:58:14,778 --> 00:58:16,638
He sees all the sons of men.

941
00:58:17,478 --> 00:58:23,618
From the place of his habitation he looks
out on all the inhabitants of the earth, he

942
00:58:23,658 --> 00:58:28,178
who fashions all of their hearts; and he
considers all of their works.

943
00:58:29,298 --> 00:58:32,438
There is no king saved by the multitude of
an army.

944
00:58:33,118 --> 00:58:36,158
A mighty man is not delivered by great
strength.

945
00:58:36,878 --> 00:58:42,798
A horse is a vain thing for safety,
neither does he deliver any by his great power.

946
00:58:43,578 --> 00:58:50,178
Behold, the LORD’s eye is on those who fear
him, on those who hope in his loving kindness,

947
00:58:51,058 --> 00:58:55,278
to deliver their soul from death, to keep
them alive in famine.

948
00:58:56,078 --> 00:58:58,398
Our soul has waited for the LORD.

949
00:58:58,968 --> 00:59:00,718
He is our help and our shield.

950
00:59:01,558 --> 00:59:06,738
For our heart rejoices in him, because we
have trusted in his holy name.

951
00:59:07,112 --> 00:59:12,132
Let your loving kindness be on us, LORD,
since we have hoped in you.

952
00:59:13,332 --> 00:59:15,252
Psalm thirty-four.

953
00:59:15,292 --> 00:59:17,872
I will bless the LORD at all times.

954
00:59:18,952 --> 00:59:21,392
His praise will always be in my mouth.

955
00:59:22,372 --> 00:59:24,252
My soul shall boast in the LORD.

956
00:59:25,212 --> 00:59:27,512
The humble shall hear of it and be glad.

957
00:59:27,552 --> 00:59:30,632
Oh magnify the LORD with me.

958
00:59:31,512 --> 00:59:33,132
Let’s exalt his name together.

959
00:59:34,072 --> 00:59:39,052
I sought the LORD, and he answered me, and
delivered me from all my fears.

960
00:59:40,132 --> 00:59:41,992
They looked to him, and were radiant.

961
00:59:43,032 --> 00:59:45,492
Their faces shall never be covered with
shame.

962
00:59:46,612 --> 00:59:52,112
This poor man cried, and the LORD heard
him, and saved him out of all his troubles.

963
00:59:52,992 --> 00:59:57,512
The LORD’s angel encamps around those who
fear him, and delivers them.

964
00:59:57,552 --> 01:00:00,852
Oh taste and see that the LORD is good.

965
01:00:00,892 --> 01:00:04,432
Blessed is the man who takes refuge in
him.

966
01:00:04,472 --> 01:00:10,932
Oh fear the LORD, you his saints, for
there is no lack with those who fear him.

967
01:00:11,472 --> 01:00:17,792
The young lions do lack, and suffer hunger,
but those who seek the LORD shall not lack

968
01:00:17,832 --> 01:00:18,732
any good thing.

969
01:00:19,692 --> 01:00:21,932
Come, you children, listen to me.

970
01:00:22,652 --> 01:00:24,692
I will teach you the fear of the LORD.

971
01:00:25,132 --> 01:00:30,892
Who is someone who desires life, and loves
many days, that he may see good?

972
01:00:31,532 --> 01:00:35,072
Keep your tongue from evil, and your lips
from speaking lies.

973
01:00:36,092 --> 01:00:38,232
Depart from evil, and do good.

974
01:00:39,192 --> 01:00:41,092
Seek peace, and pursue it.

975
01:00:42,052 --> 01:00:44,132
The LORD’s eyes are towards the righteous.

976
01:00:45,112 --> 01:00:46,692
His ears listen to their cry.

977
01:00:47,272 --> 01:00:52,572
The LORD’s face is against those who do
evil, to cut off their memory from the earth.

978
01:00:53,312 --> 01:00:58,712
The righteous cry, and the LORD hears, and
delivers them out of all their troubles.

979
01:00:59,572 --> 01:01:05,332
The LORD is near to those who have a
broken heart, and saves those who have a crushed

980
01:01:05,372 --> 01:01:06,272
spirit.

981
01:01:06,992 --> 01:01:12,192
Many are the afflictions of the righteous,
but the LORD delivers him out of them all.

982
01:01:13,092 --> 01:01:14,612
He protects all of his bones.

983
01:01:15,532 --> 01:01:16,792
Not one of them is broken.

984
01:01:18,172 --> 01:01:19,232
Evil shall kill the wicked.

985
01:01:20,232 --> 01:01:22,392
Those who hate the righteous shall be
condemned.

986
01:01:23,692 --> 01:01:25,852
The LORD redeems the soul of his servants.

987
01:01:26,429 --> 01:01:29,729
None of those who take refuge in him shall
be condemned.

988
01:01:31,289 --> 01:01:33,149
Psalm thirty-five.

989
01:01:33,189 --> 01:01:37,049
Contend, LORD, with those who contend with
me.

990
01:01:38,109 --> 01:01:40,589
Fight against those who fight against me.

991
01:01:40,869 --> 01:01:45,109
Take hold of shield and buckler, and stand
up for my help.

992
01:01:46,269 --> 01:01:49,569
Brandish the spear and block those who
pursue me.

993
01:01:50,189 --> 01:01:52,609
Tell my soul, “I am your salvation.”

994
01:01:53,529 --> 01:01:59,769
Let those who seek after my soul be
disappointed and brought to dishonour.

995
01:01:59,809 --> 01:02:03,589
Let those who plot my ruin be turned back
and confounded.

996
01:02:04,609 --> 01:02:09,549
Let them be as chaff before the wind, The
LORD’s angel driving them on.

997
01:02:10,229 --> 01:02:14,789
Let their way be dark and slippery, The
LORD’s angel pursuing them.

998
01:02:15,769 --> 01:02:19,249
For without cause they have hidden their
net in a pit for me.

999
01:02:20,129 --> 01:02:23,029
Without cause they have dug a pit for my
soul.

1000
01:02:24,069 --> 01:02:26,369
Let destruction come on him unawares.

1001
01:02:26,989 --> 01:02:29,269
Let his net that he has hidden catch
himself.

1002
01:02:30,409 --> 01:02:32,149
Let him fall into that destruction.

1003
01:02:33,029 --> 01:02:35,309
My soul shall be joyful in the LORD.

1004
01:02:36,169 --> 01:02:37,989
It shall rejoice in his salvation.

1005
01:02:39,389 --> 01:02:45,849
All my bones shall say, “LORD, who is like
you, who delivers the poor from

1006
01:02:45,889 --> 01:02:52,409
him who is too strong for him; yes, the
poor and the needy from him who robs him?”

1007
01:02:53,449 --> 01:02:55,449
Unrighteous witnesses rise up.

1008
01:02:55,969 --> 01:02:58,729
They ask me about things that I don’t know
about.

1009
01:02:59,509 --> 01:03:03,669
They reward me evil for good, to the
bereaving of my soul.

1010
01:03:04,629 --> 01:03:09,349
But as for me, when they were sick, my
clothing was sackcloth.

1011
01:03:10,129 --> 01:03:12,229
I afflicted my soul with fasting.

1012
01:03:13,169 --> 01:03:15,649
My prayer returned into my own bosom.

1013
01:03:16,189 --> 01:03:20,029
I behaved myself as though it had been my
friend or my brother.

1014
01:03:21,129 --> 01:03:24,989
I bowed down mourning, as one who mourns
his mother.

1015
01:03:25,989 --> 01:03:30,329
But in my adversity, they rejoiced, and
gathered themselves together.

1016
01:03:31,469 --> 01:03:36,589
The attackers gathered themselves together
against me, and I didn’t know it.

1017
01:03:37,049 --> 01:03:39,129
They tore at me, and didn’t cease.

1018
01:03:40,109 --> 01:03:44,569
Like the profane mockers in feasts, they
gnashed their teeth at me.

1019
01:03:45,589 --> 01:03:48,289
Lord, how long will you look on?

1020
01:03:49,189 --> 01:03:53,649
Rescue my soul from their destruction, my
precious life from the lions.

1021
01:03:54,212 --> 01:03:56,292
I will give you thanks in the great
assembly.

1022
01:03:57,532 --> 01:03:59,732
I will praise you amongst many people.

1023
01:04:00,652 --> 01:04:07,012
Don’t let those who are my enemies
wrongfully rejoice over me; neither let those who

1024
01:04:07,052 --> 01:04:09,452
hate me without a cause wink their eyes.

1025
01:04:10,132 --> 01:04:15,672
For they don’t speak peace, but they
devise deceitful words against those who are quiet

1026
01:04:15,712 --> 01:04:16,612
in the land.

1027
01:04:17,372 --> 01:04:21,072
Yes, they opened their mouth wide against
me.

1028
01:04:21,632 --> 01:04:23,332
They said, “Aha!

1029
01:04:23,892 --> 01:04:24,792
Aha!

1030
01:04:24,872 --> 01:04:26,072
Our eye has seen it!”

1031
01:04:26,452 --> 01:04:27,692
You have seen it, LORD.

1032
01:04:28,432 --> 01:04:29,332
Don’t keep silent.

1033
01:04:30,232 --> 01:04:32,352
Lord, don’t be far from me.

1034
01:04:33,072 --> 01:04:33,972
Wake up!

1035
01:04:34,332 --> 01:04:36,392
Rise up to defend me, my God!

1036
01:04:37,212 --> 01:04:39,212
My Lord, contend for me!

1037
01:04:39,912 --> 01:04:43,352
Vindicate me, LORD my God, according to
your righteousness.

1038
01:04:44,392 --> 01:04:46,152
Don’t let them gloat over me.

1039
01:04:46,952 --> 01:04:49,332
Don’t let them say in their heart, “Aha!

1040
01:04:49,992 --> 01:04:51,192
That’s the way we want it!”

1041
01:04:51,852 --> 01:04:54,712
Don’t let them say, “We have swallowed him
up!”

1042
01:04:55,232 --> 01:05:00,812
Let them be disappointed and confounded
together who rejoice at my calamity.

1043
01:05:01,612 --> 01:05:07,452
Let them be clothed with shame
and dishonour who magnify themselves against me.

1044
01:05:08,292 --> 01:05:13,372
Let those who favour my righteous cause
shout for joy and be glad.

1045
01:05:14,032 --> 01:05:20,832
Yes, let them say continually, “May The
LORD be magnified, who has pleasure

1046
01:05:20,872 --> 01:05:22,812
in the prosperity of his servant!”

1047
01:05:24,012 --> 01:05:29,072
My tongue shall talk about your righteousness
and about your praise all day long.

1048
01:05:30,072 --> 01:05:31,892
Psalm thirty-six.

1049
01:05:31,932 --> 01:05:38,032
A revelation is within my heart about the
disobedience of the wicked: There is no fear

1050
01:05:38,072 --> 01:05:39,632
of God before his eyes.

1051
01:05:40,652 --> 01:05:45,912
For he flatters himself in his own eyes,
too much to detect and hate his sin.

1052
01:05:46,992 --> 01:05:49,652
The words of his mouth are iniquity and
deceit.

1053
01:05:50,832 --> 01:05:53,232
He has ceased to be wise and to do good.

1054
01:05:53,832 --> 01:05:55,692
He plots iniquity on his bed.

1055
01:05:56,612 --> 01:05:59,252
He sets himself in a way that is not good.

1056
01:06:00,292 --> 01:06:01,672
He doesn’t abhor evil.

1057
01:06:02,092 --> 01:06:04,652
Your loving kindness, LORD, is in the
heavens.

1058
01:06:05,672 --> 01:06:07,732
Your faithfulness reaches to the skies.

1059
01:06:08,872 --> 01:06:11,332
Your righteousness is like the mountains
of God.

1060
01:06:12,452 --> 01:06:14,332
Your judgements are like a great deep.

1061
01:06:15,052 --> 01:06:17,832
LORD, you preserve man and animal.

1062
01:06:18,162 --> 01:06:20,902
How precious is your loving kindness, God!

1063
01:06:22,022 --> 01:06:25,742
The children of men take refuge under the
shadow of your wings.

1064
01:06:26,782 --> 01:06:30,522
They shall be abundantly satisfied with
the abundance of your house.

1065
01:06:31,322 --> 01:06:34,342
You will make them drink of the river of
your pleasures.

1066
01:06:35,622 --> 01:06:37,602
For with you is the spring of life.

1067
01:06:38,402 --> 01:06:40,102
In your light we will see light.

1068
01:06:40,142 --> 01:06:46,942
Oh continue your loving kindness to those
who know you, your righteousness to the upright

1069
01:06:46,982 --> 01:06:47,882
in heart.

1070
01:06:48,622 --> 01:06:51,002
Don’t let the foot of pride come against
me.

1071
01:06:51,702 --> 01:06:54,522
Don’t let the hand of the wicked drive me
away.

1072
01:06:54,562 --> 01:06:57,662
There the workers of iniquity are fallen.

1073
01:06:58,362 --> 01:07:01,662
They are thrust down, and shall not be
able to rise.

1074
01:07:02,942 --> 01:07:04,842
Psalm thirty-seven.

1075
01:07:04,882 --> 01:07:11,622
Don’t fret because of evildoers, neither
be envious against those who work unrighteousness.

1076
01:07:11,662 --> 01:07:16,722
For they shall soon be cut down like the
grass, and wither like the green herb.

1077
01:07:17,482 --> 01:07:19,682
Trust in the LORD, and do good.

1078
01:07:20,202 --> 01:07:23,302
Dwell in the land, and enjoy safe pasture.

1079
01:07:24,262 --> 01:07:29,402
Also delight yourself in the LORD, and he
will give you the desires of your heart.

1080
01:07:30,382 --> 01:07:32,022
Commit your way to the LORD.

1081
01:07:32,882 --> 01:07:38,842
Trust also in him, and he will do
this: he will make your righteousness shine out like

1082
01:07:38,882 --> 01:07:41,982
light, and your justice as the noon day
sun.

1083
01:07:42,602 --> 01:07:45,642
Rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for
him.

1084
01:07:46,562 --> 01:07:52,262
Don’t fret because of him who prospers in
his way, because of the man who makes wicked

1085
01:07:52,302 --> 01:07:53,162
plots happen.

1086
01:07:53,202 --> 01:07:56,482
Cease from anger, and forsake wrath.

1087
01:07:57,522 --> 01:08:01,122
Don’t fret; it leads only to evildoing.

1088
01:08:01,162 --> 01:08:06,922
For evildoers shall be cut off, but those
who wait for the LORD shall inherit the land.

1089
01:08:07,602 --> 01:08:11,082
For yet a little while, and the wicked
will be no more.

1090
01:08:11,882 --> 01:08:15,962
Yes, though you look for his place, he
isn’t there.

1091
01:08:16,522 --> 01:08:21,442
But the humble shall inherit the land, and
shall delight themselves in the abundance

1092
01:08:21,482 --> 01:08:22,382
of peace.

1093
01:08:22,862 --> 01:08:27,222
The wicked plots against the just, and
gnashes at him with his teeth.

1094
01:08:27,982 --> 01:08:32,502
The Lord will laugh at him, for he sees
that his day is coming.

1095
01:08:32,855 --> 01:08:38,755
The wicked have drawn out the sword, and have
bent their bow, to cast down the poor and

1096
01:08:38,795 --> 01:08:42,255
needy, to kill those who are upright on
the path.

1097
01:08:43,275 --> 01:08:45,675
Their sword shall enter into their own
heart.

1098
01:08:46,635 --> 01:08:47,975
Their bows shall be broken.

1099
01:08:49,095 --> 01:08:53,855
Better is a little that the righteous has,
than the abundance of many wicked.

1100
01:08:54,395 --> 01:08:59,315
For the arms of the wicked shall
be broken, but the LORD upholds the righteous.

1101
01:09:00,435 --> 01:09:02,555
The LORD knows the days of the perfect.

1102
01:09:03,635 --> 01:09:05,275
Their inheritance shall be forever.

1103
01:09:06,455 --> 01:09:09,055
They shall not be disappointed in the time
of evil.

1104
01:09:10,015 --> 01:09:12,135
In the days of famine they shall be
satisfied.

1105
01:09:13,275 --> 01:09:14,455
But the wicked shall perish.

1106
01:09:15,295 --> 01:09:18,455
The enemies of the LORD shall be like the
beauty of the fields.

1107
01:09:19,415 --> 01:09:21,615
They will vanish— vanish like smoke.

1108
01:09:22,215 --> 01:09:27,415
The wicked borrow, and don’t pay back, but
the righteous give generously.

1109
01:09:28,595 --> 01:09:31,475
For such as are blessed by him shall
inherit the land.

1110
01:09:32,355 --> 01:09:34,815
Those who are cursed by him shall be cut
off.

1111
01:09:35,515 --> 01:09:38,015
A man’s steps are established by the LORD.

1112
01:09:38,915 --> 01:09:40,255
He delights in his way.

1113
01:09:41,255 --> 01:09:46,695
Though he stumble, he shall not fall, for
the LORD holds him up with his hand.

1114
01:09:47,535 --> 01:09:54,315
I have been young, and now am old, yet I
have not seen the righteous forsaken, nor

1115
01:09:54,355 --> 01:09:56,275
his children begging for bread.

1116
01:09:56,915 --> 01:09:59,795
All day long he deals graciously, and
lends.

1117
01:10:00,875 --> 01:10:02,135
His offspring is blessed.

1118
01:10:03,215 --> 01:10:05,175
Depart from evil, and do good.

1119
01:10:05,955 --> 01:10:07,395
Live securely forever.

1120
01:10:08,535 --> 01:10:12,215
For the LORD loves justice, and doesn’t
forsake his saints.

1121
01:10:12,835 --> 01:10:17,295
They are preserved forever, but the
children of the wicked shall be cut off.

1122
01:10:17,335 --> 01:10:21,355
The righteous shall inherit the land, and
live in it forever.

1123
01:10:22,755 --> 01:10:25,175
The mouth of the righteous talks of
wisdom.

1124
01:10:26,195 --> 01:10:27,555
His tongue speaks justice.

1125
01:10:28,595 --> 01:10:30,495
The law of his God is in his heart.

1126
01:10:31,435 --> 01:10:32,915
None of his steps shall slide.

1127
01:10:34,155 --> 01:10:37,335
The wicked watch the righteous, and seek
to kill him.

1128
01:10:37,955 --> 01:10:42,335
The LORD will not leave him in his hand,
nor condemn him when he is judged.

1129
01:10:43,475 --> 01:10:48,855
Wait for the LORD, and keep his way, and
he will exalt you to inherit the land.

1130
01:10:49,279 --> 01:10:52,179
When the wicked are cut off, you shall see
it.

1131
01:10:53,279 --> 01:10:59,319
I have seen the wicked in great power,
spreading himself like a green tree in its native

1132
01:10:59,359 --> 01:11:00,259
soil.

1133
01:11:00,559 --> 01:11:04,399
But he passed away, and behold, he was
not.

1134
01:11:05,239 --> 01:11:09,039
Yes, I sought him, but he could not be
found.

1135
01:11:09,619 --> 01:11:15,839
Mark the perfect man, and see the upright, for
there is a future for the man of peace.

1136
01:11:17,139 --> 01:11:20,459
As for transgressors, they shall be
destroyed together.

1137
01:11:21,599 --> 01:11:23,739
The future of the wicked shall be cut off.

1138
01:11:24,079 --> 01:11:26,739
But the salvation of the righteous is from
the LORD.

1139
01:11:27,659 --> 01:11:30,059
He is their stronghold in the time of
trouble.

1140
01:11:30,899 --> 01:11:33,359
The LORD helps them and rescues them.

1141
01:11:34,179 --> 01:11:40,099
He rescues them from the wicked and saves
them, because they have taken refuge in him.

1142
01:11:41,359 --> 01:11:43,079
Psalm thirty-eight.

1143
01:11:43,119 --> 01:11:48,859
LORD, don’t rebuke me in your wrath,
neither chasten me in your hot displeasure.

1144
01:11:49,959 --> 01:11:54,059
For your arrows have pierced me, your hand
presses hard on me.

1145
01:11:54,619 --> 01:12:00,999
There is no soundness in my flesh because
of your indignation, neither is there any health

1146
01:12:01,039 --> 01:12:03,119
in my bones because of my sin.

1147
01:12:03,839 --> 01:12:06,579
For my iniquities have gone over my head.

1148
01:12:07,479 --> 01:12:10,079
As a heavy burden, they are too heavy for
me.

1149
01:12:10,459 --> 01:12:14,319
My wounds are loathsome and corrupt
because of my foolishness.

1150
01:12:14,959 --> 01:12:17,379
I am in pain and bowed down greatly.

1151
01:12:18,539 --> 01:12:20,119
I go mourning all day long.

1152
01:12:20,899 --> 01:12:22,859
For my waist is filled with burning.

1153
01:12:23,819 --> 01:12:25,799
There is no soundness in my flesh.

1154
01:12:26,659 --> 01:12:28,879
I am faint and severely bruised.

1155
01:12:29,419 --> 01:12:32,419
I have groaned by reason of the anguish of
my heart.

1156
01:12:33,119 --> 01:12:36,239
Lord, all my desire is before you.

1157
01:12:36,999 --> 01:12:38,979
My groaning is not hidden from you.

1158
01:12:39,579 --> 01:12:40,859
My heart throbs.

1159
01:12:41,499 --> 01:12:42,859
My strength fails me.

1160
01:12:43,919 --> 01:12:47,419
As for the light of my eyes, it has also
left me.

1161
01:12:48,319 --> 01:12:51,819
My lovers and my friends stand aloof from
my plague.

1162
01:12:52,899 --> 01:12:54,859
My kinsmen stand far away.

1163
01:12:55,319 --> 01:12:58,699
They also who seek after my life lay
snares.

1164
01:12:59,339 --> 01:13:05,859
Those who seek my hurt speak mischievous
things, and meditate deceits all day long.

1165
01:13:06,539 --> 01:13:09,039
But I, as a deaf man, don’t hear.

1166
01:13:10,079 --> 01:13:13,119
I am as a mute man who doesn’t open his
mouth.

1167
01:13:13,488 --> 01:13:19,848
Yes, I am as a man who doesn’t hear, in
whose mouth are no reproofs.

1168
01:13:20,688 --> 01:13:22,128
For I hope in you, LORD.

1169
01:13:22,668 --> 01:13:24,948
You will answer, Lord my God.

1170
01:13:25,848 --> 01:13:32,528
For I said, “Don’t let them gloat over me,
or exalt themselves over me when my foot slips.”

1171
01:13:33,708 --> 01:13:35,148
For I am ready to fall.

1172
01:13:35,968 --> 01:13:38,208
My pain is continually before me.

1173
01:13:38,808 --> 01:13:40,588
For I will declare my iniquity.

1174
01:13:40,628 --> 01:13:43,348
I will be sorry for my sin.

1175
01:13:44,228 --> 01:13:46,388
But my enemies are vigourous and many.

1176
01:13:47,348 --> 01:13:50,068
Those who hate me without reason are
numerous.

1177
01:13:50,788 --> 01:13:57,468
They who render evil for good are also
adversaries to me, because I follow what is good.

1178
01:13:58,548 --> 01:13:59,948
Don’t forsake me, LORD.

1179
01:14:00,588 --> 01:14:03,088
My God, don’t be far from me.

1180
01:14:03,708 --> 01:14:05,808
Hurry to help me, Lord, my salvation.

1181
01:14:07,368 --> 01:14:09,568
Psalm thirty-nine.

1182
01:14:09,608 --> 01:14:14,608
I said, “I will watch my ways, so that I
don’t sin with my tongue.

1183
01:14:15,668 --> 01:14:19,628
I will keep my mouth with a bridle while
the wicked is before me.”

1184
01:14:20,568 --> 01:14:21,828
I was mute with silence.

1185
01:14:22,948 --> 01:14:25,248
I held my peace, even from good.

1186
01:14:26,128 --> 01:14:27,288
My sorrow was stirred.

1187
01:14:28,128 --> 01:14:29,808
My heart was hot within me.

1188
01:14:30,428 --> 01:14:32,748
While I meditated, the fire burnt.

1189
01:14:33,608 --> 01:14:40,088
I spoke with my tongue: “LORD, show me my
end, what is the measure of my days.

1190
01:14:40,908 --> 01:14:43,068
Let me know how frail I am.

1191
01:14:43,868 --> 01:14:47,748
Behold, you have made my days hand widths.

1192
01:14:47,788 --> 01:14:50,068
My lifetime is as nothing before you.

1193
01:14:50,808 --> 01:14:53,248
Surely every man stands as a breath.”

1194
01:14:53,288 --> 01:14:55,188
Selah.

1195
01:14:55,228 --> 01:14:57,648
“Surely every man walks like a shadow.

1196
01:14:58,428 --> 01:15:00,688
Surely they busy themselves in vain.

1197
01:15:01,628 --> 01:15:04,688
He heaps up, and doesn’t know who shall
gather.

1198
01:15:05,688 --> 01:15:08,128
Now, Lord, what do I wait for?

1199
01:15:08,888 --> 01:15:10,068
My hope is in you.

1200
01:15:10,848 --> 01:15:13,008
Deliver me from all my transgressions.

1201
01:15:13,788 --> 01:15:15,908
Don’t make me the reproach of the foolish.

1202
01:15:16,688 --> 01:15:17,588
I was mute.

1203
01:15:18,228 --> 01:15:21,228
I didn’t open my mouth, because you did
it.

1204
01:15:22,068 --> 01:15:24,208
Remove your scourge away from me.

1205
01:15:25,088 --> 01:15:27,508
I am overcome by the blow of your hand.

1206
01:15:28,508 --> 01:15:34,368
When you rebuke and correct man for
iniquity, you consume his wealth like a moth.

1207
01:15:35,308 --> 01:15:37,528
Surely every man is but a breath.”

1208
01:15:37,568 --> 01:15:39,348
Selah.

1209
01:15:39,388 --> 01:15:42,608
“Hear my prayer, LORD, and give ear to my
cry.

1210
01:15:42,648 --> 01:15:45,248
Don’t be silent at my tears.

1211
01:15:46,048 --> 01:15:51,168
For I am a stranger with you, a foreigner,
as all my fathers were.

1212
01:15:51,534 --> 01:15:58,294
Oh spare me, that I may recover strength,
before I go away and exist no

1213
01:15:58,334 --> 01:15:59,234
more.”

1214
01:15:59,954 --> 01:16:02,194
Psalm forty.

1215
01:16:02,234 --> 01:16:03,994
I waited patiently for the LORD.

1216
01:16:04,874 --> 01:16:07,274
He turned to me, and heard my cry.

1217
01:16:07,814 --> 01:16:12,674
He brought me up also out of a horrible
pit, out of the miry clay.

1218
01:16:13,534 --> 01:16:18,034
He set my feet on a rock, and gave me a
firm place to stand.

1219
01:16:18,654 --> 01:16:22,834
He has put a new song in my mouth, even
praise to our God.

1220
01:16:23,854 --> 01:16:27,814
Many shall see it, and fear, and shall
trust in the LORD.

1221
01:16:28,614 --> 01:16:35,014
Blessed is the man who makes the LORD
his trust, and doesn’t respect the proud, nor such

1222
01:16:35,054 --> 01:16:36,274
as turn away to lies.

1223
01:16:37,114 --> 01:16:43,054
Many, LORD, my God, are the wonderful works
which you have done, and your thoughts which

1224
01:16:43,094 --> 01:16:43,994
are towards us.

1225
01:16:44,774 --> 01:16:46,674
They can’t be declared back to you.

1226
01:16:47,394 --> 01:16:51,714
If I would declare and speak of them, they
are more than can be counted.

1227
01:16:52,714 --> 01:16:55,574
Sacrifice and offering you didn’t desire.

1228
01:16:56,454 --> 01:16:57,814
You have opened my ears.

1229
01:16:58,554 --> 01:17:01,734
You have not required burnt offering and
sin offering.

1230
01:17:02,734 --> 01:17:05,594
Then I said, “Behold, I have come.

1231
01:17:06,254 --> 01:17:09,014
It is written about me in the book in the
scroll.

1232
01:17:09,054 --> 01:17:12,214
I delight to do your will, my God.

1233
01:17:13,054 --> 01:17:15,654
Yes, your law is within my heart.”

1234
01:17:16,494 --> 01:17:20,394
I have proclaimed glad news of
righteousness in the great assembly.

1235
01:17:21,234 --> 01:17:24,614
Behold, I will not seal my lips, LORD, you
know.

1236
01:17:25,354 --> 01:17:28,274
I have not hidden your righteousness
within my heart.

1237
01:17:28,994 --> 01:17:31,854
I have declared your faithfulness and your
salvation.

1238
01:17:32,854 --> 01:17:37,334
I have not concealed your loving kindness
and your truth from the great assembly.

1239
01:17:37,914 --> 01:17:40,494
Don’t withhold your tender mercies from
me, LORD.

1240
01:17:41,054 --> 01:17:45,194
Let your loving kindness and your truth
continually preserve me.

1241
01:17:45,994 --> 01:17:48,414
For innumerable evils have surrounded me.

1242
01:17:49,154 --> 01:17:53,734
My iniquities have overtaken me, so that I
am not able to look up.

1243
01:17:54,494 --> 01:17:56,614
They are more than the hairs of my head.

1244
01:17:57,214 --> 01:17:58,534
My heart has failed me.

1245
01:17:58,894 --> 01:18:00,914
Be pleased, LORD, to deliver me.

1246
01:18:01,574 --> 01:18:02,954
Hurry to help me, LORD.

1247
01:18:03,814 --> 01:18:09,314
Let them be disappointed and confounded together
who seek after my soul to destroy it.

1248
01:18:09,553 --> 01:18:14,633
Let them be turned backward and brought to
dishonour who delight in my hurt.

1249
01:18:15,673 --> 01:18:20,153
Let them be desolate by reason of their
shame that tell me, “Aha!

1250
01:18:20,813 --> 01:18:21,633
Aha!”

1251
01:18:21,673 --> 01:18:25,533
Let all those who seek you rejoice and be
glad in you.

1252
01:18:26,393 --> 01:18:32,153
Let such as love your salvation say
continually, “Let the LORD be exalted!”

1253
01:18:33,093 --> 01:18:34,453
But I am poor and needy.

1254
01:18:35,453 --> 01:18:36,993
May the Lord think about me.

1255
01:18:37,813 --> 01:18:39,893
You are my help and my deliverer.

1256
01:18:40,613 --> 01:18:42,013
Don’t delay, my God.

1257
01:18:43,033 --> 01:18:44,773
Psalm forty-one.

1258
01:18:44,813 --> 01:18:47,433
Blessed is he who considers the poor.

1259
01:18:48,473 --> 01:18:50,733
The LORD will deliver him in the day of
evil.

1260
01:18:51,753 --> 01:18:54,473
The LORD will preserve him, and keep him
alive.

1261
01:18:55,293 --> 01:18:59,933
He shall be blessed on the earth, and he
will not surrender him to the will of his enemies.

1262
01:19:01,053 --> 01:19:05,873
The LORD will sustain him on his sickbed,
and restore him from his bed of illness.

1263
01:19:06,993 --> 01:19:09,173
I said, “LORD, have mercy on me!

1264
01:19:09,793 --> 01:19:12,253
Heal me, for I have sinned against you.”

1265
01:19:12,853 --> 01:19:18,413
My enemies speak evil against me: “When
will he die, and his name perish?”

1266
01:19:19,553 --> 01:19:22,153
If he comes to see me, he speaks
falsehood.

1267
01:19:23,213 --> 01:19:25,253
His heart gathers iniquity to itself.

1268
01:19:26,313 --> 01:19:28,273
When he goes abroad, he tells it.

1269
01:19:28,313 --> 01:19:31,393
All who hate me whisper together against
me.

1270
01:19:32,313 --> 01:19:33,933
They imagine the worst for me.

1271
01:19:34,573 --> 01:19:37,713
“An evil disease”, they say, “has
afflicted him.

1272
01:19:38,373 --> 01:19:41,013
Now that he lies he shall rise up no
more.”

1273
01:19:41,793 --> 01:19:48,533
Yes, my own familiar friend, in whom I
trusted, who ate bread with me, has lifted up

1274
01:19:48,573 --> 01:19:49,773
his heel against me.

1275
01:19:50,573 --> 01:19:55,753
But you, LORD, have mercy on me, and raise
me up, that I may repay them.

1276
01:19:56,393 --> 01:20:02,073
By this I know that you delight in me,
because my enemy doesn’t triumph over me.

1277
01:20:03,073 --> 01:20:08,833
As for me, you uphold me in my integrity,
and set me in your presence forever.

1278
01:20:09,533 --> 01:20:15,253
Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel,
from everlasting and to everlasting!

1279
01:20:16,033 --> 01:20:17,453
Amen and amen.

1280
01:20:18,053 --> 01:20:19,473
Psalm forty-two.

1281
01:20:19,513 --> 01:20:24,653
As the deer pants for the water brooks, so
my soul pants after you, God.

1282
01:20:25,553 --> 01:20:28,733
My soul thirsts for God, for the living
God.

1283
01:20:29,793 --> 01:20:32,113
When shall I come and appear before God?

1284
01:20:32,489 --> 01:20:38,949
My tears have been my food day and night,
while they continually ask me, “Where is

1285
01:20:38,989 --> 01:20:39,889
your God?”

1286
01:20:40,429 --> 01:20:47,109
These things I remember, and pour out my
soul within me, how I used to go with

1287
01:20:47,149 --> 01:20:53,709
the crowd, and led them to God’s house,
with the voice of joy and praise, a multitude

1288
01:20:53,749 --> 01:20:55,229
keeping a holy day.

1289
01:20:56,009 --> 01:20:57,909
Why are you in despair, my soul?

1290
01:20:58,759 --> 01:21:00,709
Why are you disturbed within me?

1291
01:21:01,449 --> 01:21:02,349
Hope in God!

1292
01:21:03,149 --> 01:21:06,969
For I shall still praise him for the
saving help of his presence.

1293
01:21:07,789 --> 01:21:11,589
My God, my soul is in despair within me.

1294
01:21:11,889 --> 01:21:17,549
Therefore I remember you from the land of
the Jordan, the heights of Hermon, from the

1295
01:21:17,589 --> 01:21:18,489
hill Mizar.

1296
01:21:18,869 --> 01:21:22,049
Deep calls to deep at the noise of your
waterfalls.

1297
01:21:22,809 --> 01:21:25,929
All your waves and your billows have swept
over me.

1298
01:21:27,149 --> 01:21:30,289
The LORD will command his loving kindness
in the daytime.

1299
01:21:31,329 --> 01:21:35,989
In the night his song shall be with me: a
prayer to the God of my life.

1300
01:21:37,129 --> 01:21:40,929
I will ask God, my rock, “Why have you
forgotten me?

1301
01:21:41,509 --> 01:21:44,809
Why do I go mourning because of the
oppression of the enemy?”

1302
01:21:45,749 --> 01:21:52,349
As with a sword in my bones, my
adversaries reproach me, while they continually ask me,

1303
01:21:52,709 --> 01:21:53,809
“Where is your God?”

1304
01:21:54,609 --> 01:21:56,629
Why are you in despair, my soul?

1305
01:21:57,369 --> 01:21:59,229
Why are you disturbed within me?

1306
01:22:00,029 --> 01:22:00,929
Hope in God!

1307
01:22:01,489 --> 01:22:06,729
For I shall still praise him, the saving
help of my countenance, and my God.

1308
01:22:07,769 --> 01:22:10,009
Psalm forty-three.

1309
01:22:10,049 --> 01:22:14,589
Vindicate me, God, and plead my cause
against an ungodly nation.

1310
01:22:15,149 --> 01:22:18,189
Oh, deliver me from deceitful and wicked
men.

1311
01:22:19,009 --> 01:22:20,789
For you are the God of my strength.

1312
01:22:21,529 --> 01:22:22,989
Why have you rejected me?

1313
01:22:23,489 --> 01:22:26,689
Why do I go mourning because of the
oppression of the enemy?

1314
01:22:27,489 --> 01:22:30,429
Oh, send out your light and your truth.

1315
01:22:31,349 --> 01:22:32,269
Let them lead me.

1316
01:22:32,969 --> 01:22:36,229
Let them bring me to your holy hill, to
your tents.

1317
01:22:37,369 --> 01:22:41,889
Then I will go to the altar of God, to
God, my exceeding joy.

1318
01:22:42,509 --> 01:22:45,209
I will praise you on the harp, God, my
God.

1319
01:22:45,889 --> 01:22:47,669
Why are you in despair, my soul?

1320
01:22:48,569 --> 01:22:50,409
Why are you disturbed within me?

1321
01:22:51,209 --> 01:22:52,109
Hope in God!

1322
01:22:52,949 --> 01:22:57,569
For I shall still praise him: my Saviour,
my helper, and my God.

1323
01:22:58,000 --> 01:22:58,973
Psalm forty-four.

1324
01:22:59,013 --> 01:23:05,650
We have heard with our ears, God; our
fathers have told us what work you did in

1325
01:23:05,690 --> 01:23:08,399
their days, in the days of old.

1326
01:23:08,439 --> 01:23:13,113
You drove out the nations with your hand,
but you planted them.

1327
01:23:13,153 --> 01:23:16,647
You afflicted the peoples, but you spread
them abroad.

1328
01:23:16,687 --> 01:23:22,932
For they didn’t get the land in possession
by their own sword, neither did their own

1329
01:23:22,972 --> 01:23:29,609
arm save them; but your right hand, your
arm, and the light of your face, because you

1330
01:23:29,649 --> 01:23:31,180
were favourable to them.

1331
01:23:31,220 --> 01:23:34,460
God, you are my King.

1332
01:23:34,900 --> 01:23:36,520
Command victories for Jacob!

1333
01:23:37,240 --> 01:23:39,980
Through you, we will push down our
adversaries.

1334
01:23:40,920 --> 01:23:44,800
Through your name, we will tread down
those who rise up against us.

1335
01:23:45,620 --> 01:23:50,000
For I will not trust in my bow, neither
will my sword save me.

1336
01:23:50,640 --> 01:23:55,760
But you have saved us from our
adversaries, and have shamed those who hate us.

1337
01:23:56,120 --> 01:23:59,000
In God we have made our boast all day
long.

1338
01:23:59,680 --> 01:24:01,880
We will give thanks to your name forever.

1339
01:24:01,920 --> 01:24:03,960
Selah.

1340
01:24:04,000 --> 01:24:09,860
But now you rejected us, and brought us
to dishonour, and don’t go out with our armies.

1341
01:24:10,860 --> 01:24:13,100
You make us turn back from the adversary.

1342
01:24:14,160 --> 01:24:16,600
Those who hate us take plunder for
themselves.

1343
01:24:17,440 --> 01:24:21,880
You have made us like sheep for food, and
have scattered us amongst the nations.

1344
01:24:22,700 --> 01:24:27,060
You sell your people for nothing, and have
gained nothing from their sale.

1345
01:24:28,000 --> 01:24:33,740
You make us a reproach to our neighbours,
a scoffing and a derision to those who are

1346
01:24:33,780 --> 01:24:34,680
around us.

1347
01:24:35,320 --> 01:24:40,560
You make us a byword amongst the nations,
a shaking of the head amongst the peoples.

1348
01:24:41,320 --> 01:24:47,860
All day long my dishonour is before me, and
shame covers my face, at the taunt of one

1349
01:24:47,900 --> 01:24:52,840
who reproaches and verbally abuses,
because of the enemy and the avenger.

1350
01:24:53,540 --> 01:24:57,520
All this has come on us, yet we haven’t
forgotten you.

1351
01:24:57,860 --> 01:24:59,980
We haven’t been false to your covenant.

1352
01:25:00,740 --> 01:25:06,460
Our heart has not turned back, neither
have our steps strayed from your path, though

1353
01:25:06,500 --> 01:25:11,620
you have crushed us in the haunt of
jackals, and covered us with the shadow of death.

1354
01:25:12,019 --> 01:25:19,339
If we have forgotten the name of our God,
or spread out our hands to a strange god, won’t

1355
01:25:19,379 --> 01:25:20,699
God search this out?

1356
01:25:21,759 --> 01:25:23,679
For he knows the secrets of the heart.

1357
01:25:24,599 --> 01:25:28,519
Yes, for your sake we are killed all day
long.

1358
01:25:29,039 --> 01:25:31,079
We are regarded as sheep for the
slaughter.

1359
01:25:32,419 --> 01:25:33,319
Wake up!

1360
01:25:33,539 --> 01:25:35,019
Why do you sleep, Lord?

1361
01:25:35,899 --> 01:25:36,799
Arise!

1362
01:25:37,259 --> 01:25:38,399
Don’t reject us forever.

1363
01:25:39,459 --> 01:25:44,279
Why do you hide your face, and forget our
affliction and our oppression?

1364
01:25:45,619 --> 01:25:48,219
For our soul is bowed down to the dust.

1365
01:25:48,979 --> 01:25:50,759
Our body clings to the earth.

1366
01:25:51,519 --> 01:25:52,939
Rise up to help us.

1367
01:25:53,799 --> 01:25:56,159
Redeem us for your loving kindness’ sake.

1368
01:25:56,639 --> 01:25:58,419
Psalm forty-five.

1369
01:25:58,459 --> 01:26:01,179
My heart overflows with a noble theme.

1370
01:26:01,959 --> 01:26:03,819
I recite my verses for the king.

1371
01:26:04,899 --> 01:26:07,539
My tongue is like the pen of a skilful
writer.

1372
01:26:08,399 --> 01:26:11,339
You are the most excellent of the sons of
men.

1373
01:26:12,299 --> 01:26:16,919
Grace has anointed your lips, therefore
God has blessed you forever.

1374
01:26:17,519 --> 01:26:22,939
Strap your sword on your thigh, O mighty
one, in your splendour and your majesty.

1375
01:26:23,679 --> 01:26:30,339
In your majesty ride on victoriously on
behalf of truth, humility, and

1376
01:26:30,379 --> 01:26:31,159
righteousness.

1377
01:26:31,199 --> 01:26:33,919
Let your right hand display awesome deeds.

1378
01:26:34,959 --> 01:26:36,099
Your arrows are sharp.

1379
01:26:37,039 --> 01:26:41,699
The nations fall under you, with arrows in
the heart of the king’s enemies.

1380
01:26:42,339 --> 01:26:45,279
Your throne, God, is forever and ever.

1381
01:26:45,959 --> 01:26:49,139
A sceptre of equity is the sceptre of your
kingdom.

1382
01:26:50,099 --> 01:26:53,299
You have loved righteousness, and hated
wickedness.

1383
01:26:54,179 --> 01:27:00,419
Therefore God, your God, has anointed you
with the oil of gladness above your fellows.

1384
01:27:01,519 --> 01:27:05,699
All your garments smell like myrrh, aloes,
and cassia.

1385
01:27:06,219 --> 01:27:10,259
Out of ivory palaces stringed instruments
have made you glad.

1386
01:27:11,439 --> 01:27:14,039
Kings’ daughters are amongst your
honourable women.

1387
01:27:15,039 --> 01:27:18,679
At your right hand the queen stands in
gold of Ophir.

1388
01:27:19,559 --> 01:27:23,099
Listen, daughter, consider, and turn your
ear.

1389
01:27:23,519 --> 01:27:27,079
Forget your own people, and also your
father’s house.

1390
01:27:27,839 --> 01:27:32,719
So the king will desire your beauty,
honour him, for he is your lord.

1391
01:27:33,619 --> 01:27:35,999
The daughter of Tyre comes with a gift.

1392
01:27:37,059 --> 01:27:39,259
The rich amongst the people entreat your
favour.

1393
01:27:40,025 --> 01:27:42,705
The princess inside is all glorious.

1394
01:27:43,905 --> 01:27:46,085
Her clothing is interwoven with gold.

1395
01:27:47,265 --> 01:27:50,065
She shall be led to the king in
embroidered work.

1396
01:27:51,125 --> 01:27:55,905
The virgins, her companions who follow
her, shall be brought to you.

1397
01:27:56,285 --> 01:27:59,085
With gladness and rejoicing they shall be
led.

1398
01:28:00,025 --> 01:28:01,905
They shall enter into the king’s palace.

1399
01:28:02,865 --> 01:28:05,125
Your sons will take the place of your
fathers.

1400
01:28:06,125 --> 01:28:08,665
You shall make them princes in all the
earth.

1401
01:28:09,545 --> 01:28:12,725
I will make your name to be remembered in
all generations.

1402
01:28:14,145 --> 01:28:17,585
Therefore the peoples shall give you
thanks forever and ever.

1403
01:28:17,985 --> 01:28:20,005
Psalm forty-six.

1404
01:28:20,045 --> 01:28:24,625
God is our refuge and strength, a very
present help in trouble.

1405
01:28:25,345 --> 01:28:31,165
Therefore we won’t be afraid, though the
earth changes, though the mountains are shaken

1406
01:28:31,205 --> 01:28:37,165
into the heart of the seas; though its
waters roar and are troubled, though the mountains

1407
01:28:37,205 --> 01:28:38,565
tremble with their swelling.

1408
01:28:38,605 --> 01:28:40,425
Selah.

1409
01:28:40,465 --> 01:28:47,105
There is a river, the streams of which make
the city of God glad, the holy place of

1410
01:28:47,145 --> 01:28:48,565
the tents of the Most High.

1411
01:28:49,605 --> 01:28:50,845
God is within her.

1412
01:28:51,485 --> 01:28:52,665
She shall not be moved.

1413
01:28:53,465 --> 01:28:54,925
God will help her at dawn.

1414
01:28:56,025 --> 01:28:56,925
The nations raged.

1415
01:28:57,825 --> 01:28:58,985
The kingdoms were moved.

1416
01:28:59,885 --> 01:29:01,965
He lifted his voice and the earth melted.

1417
01:29:03,045 --> 01:29:04,865
The LORD of Armies is with us.

1418
01:29:05,485 --> 01:29:07,305
The God of Jacob is our refuge.

1419
01:29:07,345 --> 01:29:09,185
Selah.

1420
01:29:09,225 --> 01:29:14,525
Come, see the LORD’s works, what
desolations he has made in the earth.

1421
01:29:15,485 --> 01:29:18,065
He makes wars cease to the end of the
earth.

1422
01:29:18,885 --> 01:29:21,485
He breaks the bow, and shatters the spear.

1423
01:29:22,385 --> 01:29:24,405
He burns the chariots in the fire.

1424
01:29:24,965 --> 01:29:27,625
“Be still, and know that I am God.

1425
01:29:28,365 --> 01:29:30,425
I will be exalted amongst the nations.

1426
01:29:31,545 --> 01:29:33,285
I will be exalted in the earth.”

1427
01:29:34,305 --> 01:29:36,205
The LORD of Armies is with us.

1428
01:29:36,965 --> 01:29:38,805
The God of Jacob is our refuge.

1429
01:29:38,845 --> 01:29:41,545
Selah.

1430
01:29:41,585 --> 01:29:42,775
Psalm forty-seven.

1431
01:29:42,815 --> 01:29:45,745
Oh clap your hands, all you nations.

1432
01:29:46,945 --> 01:29:48,905
Shout to God with the voice of triumph!

1433
01:29:49,525 --> 01:29:51,665
For the LORD Most High is awesome.

1434
01:29:52,285 --> 01:29:54,585
He is a great King over all the earth.

1435
01:29:55,445 --> 01:29:59,385
He subdues nations under us, and peoples
under our feet.

1436
01:30:00,265 --> 01:30:05,125
He chooses our inheritance for us, the
glory of Jacob whom he loved.

1437
01:30:06,975 --> 01:30:07,275
Selah.

1438
01:30:07,315 --> 01:30:11,735
God has gone up with a shout, The LORD
with the sound of a trumpet.

1439
01:30:13,215 --> 01:30:14,555
Sing praises to God!

1440
01:30:15,515 --> 01:30:16,415
Sing praises!

1441
01:30:17,155 --> 01:30:18,515
Sing praises to our King!

1442
01:30:19,435 --> 01:30:20,335
Sing praises!

1443
01:30:20,855 --> 01:30:23,375
For God is the King of all the earth.

1444
01:30:24,035 --> 01:30:25,275
Sing praises with understanding.

1445
01:30:26,935 --> 01:30:28,255
God reigns over the nations.

1446
01:30:29,495 --> 01:30:31,135
God sits on his holy throne.

1447
01:30:31,995 --> 01:30:37,215
The princes of the peoples are gathered
together, the people of the God of Abraham.

1448
01:30:38,235 --> 01:30:41,035
For the shields of the earth belong to
God.

1449
01:30:41,875 --> 01:30:43,135
He is greatly exalted!

1450
01:30:43,795 --> 01:30:45,595
Psalm forty-eight.

1451
01:30:45,635 --> 01:30:52,255
Great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised,
in the city of our God, in his holy

1452
01:30:52,295 --> 01:30:53,195
mountain.

1453
01:30:53,375 --> 01:31:00,155
Beautiful in elevation, the joy of the whole
earth, is Mount Zion, on the north sides,

1454
01:31:00,825 --> 01:31:02,595
the city of the great King.

1455
01:31:03,595 --> 01:31:07,075
God has shown himself in her citadels as a
refuge.

1456
01:31:07,755 --> 01:31:13,095
For, behold, the kings assembled
themselves, they passed by together.

1457
01:31:14,015 --> 01:31:16,295
They saw it, then they were amazed.

1458
01:31:17,135 --> 01:31:18,155
They were dismayed.

1459
01:31:18,655 --> 01:31:19,555
They hurried away.

1460
01:31:20,395 --> 01:31:25,725
Trembling took hold of them there, pain,
as of a woman in travail.

1461
01:31:26,445 --> 01:31:30,145
With the east wind, you break the ships of
Tarshish.

1462
01:31:30,185 --> 01:31:36,705
As we have heard, so we have seen, in the
city of the LORD of Armies, in the city of

1463
01:31:36,745 --> 01:31:37,645
our God.

1464
01:31:38,105 --> 01:31:39,845
God will establish it forever.

1465
01:31:39,885 --> 01:31:41,985
Selah.

1466
01:31:42,025 --> 01:31:46,425
We have thought about your loving kindness,
God, in the middle of your temple.

1467
01:31:47,565 --> 01:31:51,685
As is your name, God, so is your praise to
the ends of the earth.

1468
01:31:52,435 --> 01:31:54,705
Your right hand is full of righteousness.

1469
01:31:55,865 --> 01:31:57,545
Let Mount Zion be glad!

1470
01:31:58,345 --> 01:32:02,685
Let the daughters of Judah rejoice because
of your judgements.

1471
01:32:02,725 --> 01:32:05,385
Walk about Zion, and go around her.

1472
01:32:06,085 --> 01:32:07,125
Number its towers.

1473
01:32:08,165 --> 01:32:09,245
Notice her bulwarks.

1474
01:32:10,105 --> 01:32:14,145
Consider her palaces, that you may tell it
to the next generation.

1475
01:32:14,185 --> 01:32:18,785
For this God is our God forever and ever.

1476
01:32:19,205 --> 01:32:21,385
He will be our guide even to death.

1477
01:32:22,425 --> 01:32:24,825
Psalm forty-nine.

1478
01:32:24,865 --> 01:32:26,525
Hear this, all you peoples.

1479
01:32:27,345 --> 01:32:33,985
Listen, all you inhabitants of the world,
both low and high, rich and poor together.

1480
01:32:35,125 --> 01:32:37,405
My mouth will speak words of wisdom.

1481
01:32:37,943 --> 01:32:39,903
My heart will utter understanding.

1482
01:32:41,143 --> 01:32:43,283
I will incline my ear to a proverb.

1483
01:32:44,643 --> 01:32:47,003
I will solve my riddle on the harp.

1484
01:32:47,703 --> 01:32:53,303
Why should I fear in the days of evil,
when iniquity at my heels surrounds me?

1485
01:32:53,783 --> 01:32:59,563
Those who trust in their wealth, and boast
in the multitude of their riches— none of

1486
01:32:59,603 --> 01:33:04,983
them can by any means redeem his brother,
nor give God a ransom for him.

1487
01:33:05,663 --> 01:33:12,063
For the redemption of their life is costly,
no payment is ever enough, that he should

1488
01:33:12,103 --> 01:33:15,503
live on forever, that he should not see
corruption.

1489
01:33:16,303 --> 01:33:22,823
For he sees that wise men die; likewise
the fool and the senseless perish, and

1490
01:33:22,863 --> 01:33:24,323
leave their wealth to others.

1491
01:33:25,303 --> 01:33:30,583
Their inward thought is that their houses
will endure forever, and their dwelling places

1492
01:33:30,623 --> 01:33:31,863
to all generations.

1493
01:33:32,843 --> 01:33:35,363
They name their lands after themselves.

1494
01:33:35,863 --> 01:33:39,583
But man, despite his riches, doesn’t
endure.

1495
01:33:40,663 --> 01:33:42,703
He is like the animals that perish.

1496
01:33:43,743 --> 01:33:49,423
This is the destiny of those who are
foolish, and of those who approve their sayings.

1497
01:33:49,463 --> 01:33:51,463
Selah.

1498
01:33:51,503 --> 01:33:53,843
They are appointed as a flock for Sheol.

1499
01:33:54,663 --> 01:33:55,983
Death shall be their shepherd.

1500
01:33:56,803 --> 01:33:59,703
The upright shall have dominion over them
in the morning.

1501
01:34:00,703 --> 01:34:04,443
Their beauty shall decay in Sheol, far
from their mansion.

1502
01:34:05,583 --> 01:34:11,083
But God will redeem my soul from the power
of Sheol, for he will receive me.

1503
01:34:11,123 --> 01:34:12,763
Selah.

1504
01:34:12,803 --> 01:34:19,163
Don’t be afraid when a man is made rich,
when the glory of his house is increased; for

1505
01:34:19,203 --> 01:34:21,603
when he dies he will carry nothing away.

1506
01:34:22,723 --> 01:34:24,823
His glory won’t descend after him.

1507
01:34:25,903 --> 01:34:32,043
Though while he lived he blessed his soul— and
men praise you when you do well for yourself—

1508
01:34:33,003 --> 01:34:35,343
he shall go to the generation of his
fathers.

1509
01:34:36,263 --> 01:34:37,943
They shall never see the light.

1510
01:34:38,663 --> 01:34:43,603
A man who has riches without
understanding, is like the animals that perish.

1511
01:34:44,923 --> 01:34:47,003
Psalm fifty.

1512
01:34:47,043 --> 01:34:53,723
The Mighty One, God, The LORD, speaks, and
calls the earth from sunrise to

1513
01:34:53,763 --> 01:34:54,663
sunset.

1514
01:34:54,923 --> 01:34:59,743
Out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, God
shines out.

1515
01:35:00,803 --> 01:35:03,663
Our God comes, and does not keep silent.

1516
01:35:04,128 --> 01:35:06,308
A fire devours before him.

1517
01:35:07,168 --> 01:35:09,248
It is very stormy around him.

1518
01:35:10,288 --> 01:35:17,008
He calls to the heavens above, to the
earth, that he may judge his people: “Gather

1519
01:35:17,048 --> 01:35:22,468
my saints together to me, those who have
made a covenant with me by sacrifice.”

1520
01:35:23,088 --> 01:35:27,628
The heavens shall declare his
righteousness, for God himself is judge.

1521
01:35:27,668 --> 01:35:29,668
Selah.

1522
01:35:29,708 --> 01:35:32,048
“Hear, my people, and I will speak.

1523
01:35:32,928 --> 01:35:35,568
Israel, I will testify against you.

1524
01:35:36,348 --> 01:35:38,048
I am God, your God.

1525
01:35:38,948 --> 01:35:41,168
I don’t rebuke you for your sacrifices.

1526
01:35:42,228 --> 01:35:44,868
Your burnt offerings are continually
before me.

1527
01:35:45,248 --> 01:35:49,988
I have no need for a bull from your stall,
nor male goats from your pens.

1528
01:35:50,668 --> 01:35:55,988
For every animal of the forest is mine,
and the livestock on a thousand hills.

1529
01:35:56,968 --> 01:35:58,748
I know all the birds of the mountains.

1530
01:35:59,568 --> 01:36:01,928
The wild animals of the field are mine.

1531
01:36:02,808 --> 01:36:08,948
If I were hungry, I would not tell you, for
the world is mine, and all that is in it.

1532
01:36:09,388 --> 01:36:13,008
Will I eat the meat of bulls, or drink the
blood of goats?

1533
01:36:14,028 --> 01:36:16,748
Offer to God the sacrifice of
thanksgiving.

1534
01:36:17,388 --> 01:36:19,648
Pay your vows to the Most High.

1535
01:36:20,528 --> 01:36:22,328
Call on me in the day of trouble.

1536
01:36:23,208 --> 01:36:26,048
I will deliver you, and you will honour
me.”

1537
01:36:26,628 --> 01:36:33,028
But to the wicked God says, “What right do
you have to declare my statutes, that you

1538
01:36:33,068 --> 01:36:39,068
have taken my covenant on your lips, since
you hate instruction, and throw my words behind

1539
01:36:39,108 --> 01:36:40,008
you?

1540
01:36:40,228 --> 01:36:45,888
When you saw a thief, you consented
with him, and have participated with adulterers.

1541
01:36:46,508 --> 01:36:48,108
“You give your mouth to evil.

1542
01:36:48,928 --> 01:36:50,248
Your tongue frames deceit.

1543
01:36:51,188 --> 01:36:53,448
You sit and speak against your brother.

1544
01:36:54,128 --> 01:36:56,228
You slander your own mother’s son.

1545
01:36:56,948 --> 01:36:59,768
You have done these things, and I kept
silent.

1546
01:37:00,648 --> 01:37:02,668
You thought that I was just like you.

1547
01:37:03,148 --> 01:37:07,008
I will rebuke you, and accuse you in front
of your eyes.

1548
01:37:07,708 --> 01:37:14,168
“Now consider this, you who forget God,
lest I tear you into pieces, and there be

1549
01:37:14,208 --> 01:37:15,288
no one to deliver.

1550
01:37:16,348 --> 01:37:22,708
Whoever offers the sacrifice of thanksgiving glorifies
me, and prepares his way so that

1551
01:37:22,748 --> 01:37:24,808
I will show God’s salvation to him.”

1552
01:37:26,008 --> 01:37:26,908
Psalm fifty-one.

1553
01:37:27,536 --> 01:37:31,316
Have mercy on me, God, according to your
loving kindness.

1554
01:37:32,616 --> 01:37:37,996
According to the multitude of your tender
mercies, blot out my transgressions.

1555
01:37:38,796 --> 01:37:41,136
Wash me thoroughly from my iniquity.

1556
01:37:42,156 --> 01:37:43,336
Cleanse me from my sin.

1557
01:37:44,336 --> 01:37:46,076
For I know my transgressions.

1558
01:37:46,696 --> 01:37:48,876
My sin is constantly before me.

1559
01:37:49,496 --> 01:37:56,096
Against you, and you only, I have sinned,
and done that which is evil in your sight,

1560
01:37:56,836 --> 01:38:01,396
so you may be proved right when you speak,
and justified when you judge.

1561
01:38:02,676 --> 01:38:05,316
Behold, I was born in iniquity.

1562
01:38:05,956 --> 01:38:07,856
My mother conceived me in sin.

1563
01:38:08,436 --> 01:38:11,656
Behold, you desire truth in the inward
parts.

1564
01:38:12,556 --> 01:38:14,936
You teach me wisdom in the inmost place.

1565
01:38:15,796 --> 01:38:18,456
Purify me with hyssop, and I will be
clean.

1566
01:38:19,036 --> 01:38:21,896
Wash me, and I will be whiter than snow.

1567
01:38:22,756 --> 01:38:27,736
Let me hear joy and gladness, that the
bones which you have broken may rejoice.

1568
01:38:28,336 --> 01:38:32,836
Hide your face from my sins, and blot out
all of my iniquities.

1569
01:38:33,256 --> 01:38:35,456
Create in me a clean heart, O God.

1570
01:38:36,356 --> 01:38:38,356
Renew a right spirit within me.

1571
01:38:39,156 --> 01:38:43,916
Don’t throw me from your presence, and
don’t take your Holy Spirit from me.

1572
01:38:44,696 --> 01:38:47,136
Restore to me the joy of your salvation.

1573
01:38:47,836 --> 01:38:49,536
Uphold me with a willing spirit.

1574
01:38:50,556 --> 01:38:52,816
Then I will teach transgressors your ways.

1575
01:38:53,716 --> 01:38:55,556
Sinners will be converted to you.

1576
01:38:56,276 --> 01:39:00,656
Deliver me from the guilt of bloodshed, O
God, the God of my salvation.

1577
01:39:01,916 --> 01:39:04,376
My tongue will sing aloud of your
righteousness.

1578
01:39:05,516 --> 01:39:07,056
Lord, open my lips.

1579
01:39:07,896 --> 01:39:09,736
My mouth will declare your praise.

1580
01:39:10,296 --> 01:39:13,996
For you don’t delight in sacrifice, or
else I would give it.

1581
01:39:14,736 --> 01:39:16,796
You have no pleasure in burnt offering.

1582
01:39:17,616 --> 01:39:20,536
The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit.

1583
01:39:21,676 --> 01:39:25,916
O God, you will not despise a broken and
contrite heart.

1584
01:39:26,816 --> 01:39:28,976
Do well in your good pleasure to Zion.

1585
01:39:29,916 --> 01:39:31,356
Build the walls of Jerusalem.

1586
01:39:32,116 --> 01:39:37,776
Then you will delight in the sacrifices
of righteousness, in burnt offerings and in whole

1587
01:39:37,816 --> 01:39:38,776
burnt offerings.

1588
01:39:39,416 --> 01:39:41,536
Then they will offer bulls on your altar.

1589
01:39:42,816 --> 01:39:45,356
Psalm fifty-two.

1590
01:39:45,396 --> 01:39:47,636
Why do you boast of mischief, mighty man?

1591
01:39:48,496 --> 01:39:50,976
God’s loving kindness endures continually.

1592
01:39:51,537 --> 01:39:57,437
Your tongue plots destruction, like a
sharp razor, working deceitfully.

1593
01:39:58,257 --> 01:40:03,497
You love evil more than good, lying rather
than speaking the truth.

1594
01:40:03,537 --> 01:40:05,777
Selah.

1595
01:40:05,817 --> 01:40:10,077
You love all devouring words, you
deceitful tongue.

1596
01:40:11,177 --> 01:40:13,777
God will likewise destroy you forever.

1597
01:40:14,557 --> 01:40:20,677
He will take you up, and pluck you out of
your tent, and root you out of the land of

1598
01:40:20,717 --> 01:40:21,137
the living.

1599
01:40:21,177 --> 01:40:22,977
Selah.

1600
01:40:23,017 --> 01:40:29,577
The righteous also will see it, and fear,
and laugh at him, saying, “Behold,

1601
01:40:30,457 --> 01:40:36,157
this is the man who didn’t make God
his strength, but trusted in the abundance of his

1602
01:40:36,197 --> 01:40:39,517
riches, and strengthened himself in his
wickedness.”

1603
01:40:39,797 --> 01:40:44,297
But as for me, I am like a green olive
tree in God’s house.

1604
01:40:44,937 --> 01:40:48,897
I trust in God’s loving kindness forever
and ever.

1605
01:40:49,477 --> 01:40:53,557
I will give you thanks forever, because
you have done it.

1606
01:40:54,557 --> 01:40:59,437
I will hope in your name, for it is good,
in the presence of your saints.

1607
01:41:00,137 --> 01:41:02,297
Psalm fifty-three.

1608
01:41:02,337 --> 01:41:05,877
The fool has said in his heart, “There is
no God.”

1609
01:41:06,517 --> 01:41:09,977
They are corrupt, and have done abominable
iniquity.

1610
01:41:10,737 --> 01:41:12,737
There is no one who does good.

1611
01:41:13,597 --> 01:41:19,417
God looks down from heaven on the children of
men, to see if there are any who understood,

1612
01:41:20,137 --> 01:41:21,497
who seek after God.

1613
01:41:22,217 --> 01:41:24,037
Every one of them has gone back.

1614
01:41:24,737 --> 01:41:26,397
They have become filthy together.

1615
01:41:27,077 --> 01:41:31,097
There is no one who does good, no, not
one.

1616
01:41:31,997 --> 01:41:38,537
Have the workers of iniquity no knowledge, who
eat up my people as they eat bread, and

1617
01:41:38,577 --> 01:41:39,677
don’t call on God?

1618
01:41:40,657 --> 01:41:46,997
There they were in great fear, where no
fear was, for God has scattered the bones of

1619
01:41:47,037 --> 01:41:48,957
him who encamps against you.

1620
01:41:49,417 --> 01:41:53,377
You have put them to shame, because God
has rejected them.

1621
01:41:54,297 --> 01:41:57,397
Oh that the salvation of Israel would come
out of Zion!

1622
01:41:57,437 --> 01:42:03,977
When God brings back his people from
captivity, then Jacob shall rejoice, and

1623
01:42:04,017 --> 01:42:05,337
Israel shall be glad.

1624
01:42:06,817 --> 01:42:09,117
Psalm fifty-four.

1625
01:42:09,157 --> 01:42:10,777
Save me, God, by your name.

1626
01:42:11,517 --> 01:42:13,117
Vindicate me in your might.

1627
01:42:13,757 --> 01:42:15,057
Hear my prayer, God.

1628
01:42:15,957 --> 01:42:17,877
Listen to the words of my mouth.

1629
01:42:18,797 --> 01:42:21,057
For strangers have risen up against me.

1630
01:42:21,359 --> 01:42:23,879
Violent men have sought after my soul.

1631
01:42:24,859 --> 01:42:26,759
They haven’t set God before them.

1632
01:42:26,799 --> 01:42:29,259
Selah.

1633
01:42:29,299 --> 01:42:31,519
Behold, God is my helper.

1634
01:42:32,519 --> 01:42:35,359
The Lord is the one who sustains my soul.

1635
01:42:36,379 --> 01:42:38,499
He will repay the evil to my enemies.

1636
01:42:39,539 --> 01:42:40,919
Destroy them in your truth.

1637
01:42:40,959 --> 01:42:44,819
With a free will offering, I will
sacrifice to you.

1638
01:42:45,399 --> 01:42:48,959
I will give thanks to your name, LORD, for
it is good.

1639
01:42:49,639 --> 01:42:52,119
For he has delivered me out of all
trouble.

1640
01:42:53,179 --> 01:42:55,779
My eye has seen triumph over my enemies.

1641
01:42:57,019 --> 01:42:59,259
Psalm fifty-five.

1642
01:42:59,299 --> 01:43:00,879
Listen to my prayer, God.

1643
01:43:01,279 --> 01:43:03,599
Don’t hide yourself from my supplication.

1644
01:43:04,479 --> 01:43:06,519
Attend to me, and answer me.

1645
01:43:06,999 --> 01:43:12,899
I am restless in my complaint, and moan
because of the voice of the enemy, because of

1646
01:43:12,939 --> 01:43:14,219
the oppression of the wicked.

1647
01:43:15,039 --> 01:43:16,739
For they bring suffering on me.

1648
01:43:17,519 --> 01:43:20,059
In anger they hold a grudge against me.

1649
01:43:20,799 --> 01:43:23,119
My heart is severely pained within me.

1650
01:43:23,879 --> 01:43:26,099
The terrors of death have fallen on me.

1651
01:43:26,759 --> 01:43:29,219
Fearfulness and trembling have come on me.

1652
01:43:30,059 --> 01:43:31,739
Horror has overwhelmed me.

1653
01:43:32,739 --> 01:43:35,819
I said, “Oh that I had wings like a dove!

1654
01:43:36,759 --> 01:43:39,399
Then I would fly away, and be at rest.

1655
01:43:40,299 --> 01:43:43,259
Behold, then I would wander far off.

1656
01:43:43,899 --> 01:43:45,319
I would lodge in the wilderness.”

1657
01:43:45,359 --> 01:43:47,859
Selah.

1658
01:43:47,899 --> 01:43:51,219
“I would hurry to a shelter from the
stormy wind and storm.”

1659
01:43:51,879 --> 01:43:57,679
Confuse them, Lord, and confound their language,
for I have seen violence and strife

1660
01:43:57,719 --> 01:43:58,619
in the city.

1661
01:43:59,419 --> 01:44:02,259
Day and night they prowl around on its
walls.

1662
01:44:03,179 --> 01:44:05,679
Malice and abuse are also within her.

1663
01:44:06,559 --> 01:44:08,539
Destructive forces are within her.

1664
01:44:09,379 --> 01:44:11,959
Threats and lies don’t depart from her
streets.

1665
01:44:11,999 --> 01:44:17,259
For it was not an enemy who insulted me,
then I could have endured it.

1666
01:44:18,119 --> 01:44:24,139
Neither was it he who hated me who raised
himself up against me, then I would have hidden

1667
01:44:24,179 --> 01:44:25,299
myself from him.

1668
01:44:26,099 --> 01:44:31,919
But it was you, a man like me, my
companion, and my familiar friend.

1669
01:44:32,739 --> 01:44:34,799
We took sweet fellowship together.

1670
01:44:35,619 --> 01:44:37,819
We walked in God’s house with company.

1671
01:44:39,059 --> 01:44:40,899
Let death come suddenly on them.

1672
01:44:40,939 --> 01:44:44,099
Let them go down alive into Sheol.

1673
01:44:45,059 --> 01:44:47,779
For wickedness is amongst them, in their
dwelling.

1674
01:44:48,304 --> 01:44:51,044
As for me, I will call on God.

1675
01:44:51,964 --> 01:44:53,344
The LORD will save me.

1676
01:44:54,464 --> 01:44:58,484
Evening, morning, and at noon, I will cry
out in distress.

1677
01:44:59,444 --> 01:45:00,664
He will hear my voice.

1678
01:45:01,704 --> 01:45:07,324
He has redeemed my soul in peace from the
battle that was against me, although there

1679
01:45:07,364 --> 01:45:08,804
are many who oppose me.

1680
01:45:09,404 --> 01:45:13,964
God, who is enthroned forever, will hear
and answer them.

1681
01:45:14,004 --> 01:45:15,904
Selah.

1682
01:45:15,944 --> 01:45:18,444
They never change and don’t fear God.

1683
01:45:19,344 --> 01:45:21,764
He raises his hands against his friends.

1684
01:45:22,564 --> 01:45:24,184
He has violated his covenant.

1685
01:45:24,704 --> 01:45:28,304
His mouth was smooth as butter, but his
heart was war.

1686
01:45:29,284 --> 01:45:33,164
His words were softer than oil, yet they
were drawn swords.

1687
01:45:34,004 --> 01:45:37,464
Cast your burden on the LORD and he will
sustain you.

1688
01:45:38,064 --> 01:45:40,724
He will never allow the righteous to be
moved.

1689
01:45:41,224 --> 01:45:45,204
But you, God, will bring them down into
the pit of destruction.

1690
01:45:46,724 --> 01:45:52,364
Bloodthirsty and deceitful men shall not live out
half their days, but I will trust in

1691
01:45:52,404 --> 01:45:53,304
you.

1692
01:45:53,884 --> 01:45:55,864
Psalm fifty-six.

1693
01:45:55,904 --> 01:46:00,244
Be merciful to me, God, for man wants to
swallow me up.

1694
01:46:01,184 --> 01:46:03,964
All day long, he attacks and oppresses me.

1695
01:46:04,944 --> 01:46:10,964
My enemies want to swallow me up all day
long, for they are many who fight proudly against

1696
01:46:11,004 --> 01:46:11,624
me.

1697
01:46:11,664 --> 01:46:14,604
When I am afraid, I will put my trust in
you.

1698
01:46:15,364 --> 01:46:17,164
In God, I praise his word.

1699
01:46:18,224 --> 01:46:19,744
In God, I put my trust.

1700
01:46:20,384 --> 01:46:21,584
I will not be afraid.

1701
01:46:22,604 --> 01:46:24,224
What can flesh do to me?

1702
01:46:24,984 --> 01:46:26,984
All day long they twist my words.

1703
01:46:28,004 --> 01:46:30,024
All their thoughts are against me for
evil.

1704
01:46:30,844 --> 01:46:33,904
They conspire and lurk, watching my steps.

1705
01:46:34,884 --> 01:46:36,644
They are eager to take my life.

1706
01:46:37,124 --> 01:46:38,804
Shall they escape by iniquity?

1707
01:46:38,844 --> 01:46:41,924
In anger cast down the peoples, God.

1708
01:46:42,904 --> 01:46:44,344
You count my wanderings.

1709
01:46:44,904 --> 01:46:46,884
You put my tears into your container.

1710
01:46:47,824 --> 01:46:48,964
Aren’t they in your book?

1711
01:46:50,004 --> 01:46:53,064
Then my enemies shall turn back in the day
that I call.

1712
01:46:53,784 --> 01:46:56,724
I know this: that God is for me.

1713
01:46:57,584 --> 01:46:59,824
In God, I will praise his word.

1714
01:47:00,724 --> 01:47:02,904
In the LORD, I will praise his word.

1715
01:47:03,904 --> 01:47:05,604
I have put my trust in God.

1716
01:47:06,304 --> 01:47:07,444
I will not be afraid.

1717
01:47:08,644 --> 01:47:09,944
What can man do to me?

1718
01:47:10,544 --> 01:47:11,944
Your vows are on me, God.

1719
01:47:12,744 --> 01:47:14,704
I will give thank offerings to you.

1720
01:47:15,008 --> 01:47:21,468
For you have delivered my soul from death,
and prevented my feet from falling, that I

1721
01:47:21,508 --> 01:47:24,528
may walk before God in the light of the
living.

1722
01:47:25,948 --> 01:47:28,158
Psalm fifty-seven.

1723
01:47:28,198 --> 01:47:34,768
Be merciful to me, God, be merciful to me,
for my soul takes refuge in you.

1724
01:47:35,288 --> 01:47:41,668
Yes, in the shadow of your wings, I will
take refuge, until disaster has passed.

1725
01:47:41,708 --> 01:47:48,428
I cry out to God Most High, to God who
accomplishes my requests for

1726
01:47:48,468 --> 01:47:49,048
me.

1727
01:47:49,088 --> 01:47:54,768
He will send from heaven, and save me, he
rebukes the one who is pursuing me.

1728
01:47:54,808 --> 01:47:56,568
Selah.

1729
01:47:56,608 --> 01:48:00,548
God will send out his loving kindness and
his truth.

1730
01:48:01,288 --> 01:48:02,748
My soul is amongst lions.

1731
01:48:03,748 --> 01:48:09,848
I lie amongst those who are set on fire,
even the sons of men, whose teeth are spears

1732
01:48:09,888 --> 01:48:12,908
and arrows, and their tongue a sharp
sword.

1733
01:48:13,808 --> 01:48:16,168
Be exalted, God, above the heavens!

1734
01:48:16,888 --> 01:48:19,388
Let your glory be above all the earth!

1735
01:48:19,808 --> 01:48:21,768
They have prepared a net for my steps.

1736
01:48:22,628 --> 01:48:24,048
My soul is bowed down.

1737
01:48:24,728 --> 01:48:26,348
They dig a pit before me.

1738
01:48:27,008 --> 01:48:28,928
They fall into the middle of it
themselves.

1739
01:48:28,968 --> 01:48:31,088
Selah.

1740
01:48:31,128 --> 01:48:33,448
My heart is steadfast, God.

1741
01:48:34,048 --> 01:48:35,128
My heart is steadfast.

1742
01:48:36,308 --> 01:48:39,488
I will sing, yes, I will sing praises.

1743
01:48:40,428 --> 01:48:41,608
Wake up, my glory!

1744
01:48:42,228 --> 01:48:44,008
Wake up, lute and harp!

1745
01:48:44,568 --> 01:48:46,028
I will wake up the dawn.

1746
01:48:46,948 --> 01:48:50,008
I will give thanks to you, Lord, amongst
the peoples.

1747
01:48:50,668 --> 01:48:53,388
I will sing praises to you amongst the
nations.

1748
01:48:54,288 --> 01:48:59,528
For your great loving kindness reaches to
the heavens, and your truth to the skies.

1749
01:49:00,388 --> 01:49:02,808
Be exalted, God, above the heavens.

1750
01:49:03,628 --> 01:49:05,988
Let your glory be over all the earth.

1751
01:49:06,768 --> 01:49:08,368
Psalm fifty-eight.

1752
01:49:08,408 --> 01:49:11,508
Do you indeed speak righteousness, silent
ones?

1753
01:49:12,248 --> 01:49:14,908
Do you judge blamelessly, you sons of men?

1754
01:49:15,588 --> 01:49:18,468
No, in your heart you plot injustice.

1755
01:49:19,648 --> 01:49:22,568
You measure out the violence of your hands
in the earth.

1756
01:49:23,248 --> 01:49:25,388
The wicked go astray from the womb.

1757
01:49:26,248 --> 01:49:29,688
They are wayward as soon as they are born,
speaking lies.

1758
01:49:30,608 --> 01:49:36,928
Their poison is like the poison of a snake,
like a deaf cobra that stops its ear, which

1759
01:49:36,968 --> 01:49:42,308
doesn’t listen to the voice of charmers,
no matter how skilful the charmer may be.

1760
01:49:42,614 --> 01:49:45,034
Break their teeth, God, in their mouth.

1761
01:49:46,054 --> 01:49:49,114
Break out the great teeth of the young
lions, LORD.

1762
01:49:50,114 --> 01:49:52,754
Let them vanish like water that flows
away.

1763
01:49:53,754 --> 01:49:57,294
When they draw the bow, let their arrows
be made blunt.

1764
01:49:57,814 --> 01:50:04,194
Let them be like a snail which melts
and passes away, like the stillborn child, who has

1765
01:50:04,234 --> 01:50:05,394
not seen the sun.

1766
01:50:06,094 --> 01:50:11,494
Before your pots can feel the heat of the
thorns, he will sweep away the green and the

1767
01:50:11,534 --> 01:50:12,434
burning alike.

1768
01:50:13,434 --> 01:50:16,474
The righteous shall rejoice when he sees
the vengeance.

1769
01:50:17,074 --> 01:50:23,014
He shall wash his feet in the blood of
the wicked, so that men shall say, “Most certainly

1770
01:50:23,054 --> 01:50:24,934
there is a reward for the righteous.

1771
01:50:25,694 --> 01:50:28,674
Most certainly there is a God who judges
the earth.”

1772
01:50:29,914 --> 01:50:31,894
Psalm fifty-nine.

1773
01:50:31,934 --> 01:50:33,934
Deliver me from my enemies, my God.

1774
01:50:33,974 --> 01:50:37,994
Set me on high from those who rise up
against me.

1775
01:50:38,734 --> 01:50:41,034
Deliver me from the workers of iniquity.

1776
01:50:41,394 --> 01:50:43,374
Save me from the bloodthirsty men.

1777
01:50:44,154 --> 01:50:47,454
For, behold, they lie in wait for my soul.

1778
01:50:48,214 --> 01:50:54,574
The mighty gather themselves together against me,
not for my disobedience, nor for my

1779
01:50:54,614 --> 01:50:55,514
sin, LORD.

1780
01:50:55,954 --> 01:50:59,894
I have done no wrong, yet they are ready
to attack me.

1781
01:51:00,534 --> 01:51:03,254
Rise up, behold, and help me!

1782
01:51:03,734 --> 01:51:09,334
You, LORD God of Armies, the God
of Israel, rouse yourself to punish the nations.

1783
01:51:10,214 --> 01:51:12,854
Show no mercy to the wicked traitors.

1784
01:51:12,894 --> 01:51:14,154
Selah.

1785
01:51:14,194 --> 01:51:18,934
They return at evening, howling like dogs,
and prowl around the city.

1786
01:51:19,834 --> 01:51:22,034
Behold, they spew with their mouth.

1787
01:51:22,874 --> 01:51:26,934
Swords are in their lips, “For”, they say,
“who hears us?”

1788
01:51:26,974 --> 01:51:29,314
But you, LORD, laugh at them.

1789
01:51:29,894 --> 01:51:31,394
You scoff at all the nations.

1790
01:51:31,434 --> 01:51:37,234
Oh, my Strength, I watch for you, for God
is my high tower.

1791
01:51:38,094 --> 01:51:41,214
My God will go before me with his loving
kindness.

1792
01:51:42,254 --> 01:51:44,994
God will let me look at my enemies in
triumph.

1793
01:51:46,054 --> 01:51:48,914
Don’t kill them, or my people may forget.

1794
01:51:49,534 --> 01:51:53,614
Scatter them by your power, and bring them
down, Lord our shield.

1795
01:51:54,334 --> 01:51:59,394
For the sin of their mouth, and the words
of their lips, let them be caught in their

1796
01:51:59,434 --> 01:52:02,734
pride, for the curses and lies which they
utter.

1797
01:52:03,039 --> 01:52:04,379
Consume them in wrath.

1798
01:52:05,399 --> 01:52:08,099
Consume them, and they will be no more.

1799
01:52:09,299 --> 01:52:13,939
Let them know that God rules in Jacob, to
the ends of the earth.

1800
01:52:13,979 --> 01:52:16,079
Selah.

1801
01:52:16,119 --> 01:52:17,999
At evening let them return.

1802
01:52:19,199 --> 01:52:22,679
Let them howl like a dog, and go around
the city.

1803
01:52:23,099 --> 01:52:28,259
They shall wander up and down for food,
and wait all night if they aren’t satisfied.

1804
01:52:29,079 --> 01:52:30,699
But I will sing of your strength.

1805
01:52:31,499 --> 01:52:36,119
Yes, I will sing aloud of your loving
kindness in the morning.

1806
01:52:37,219 --> 01:52:41,919
For you have been my high tower, a refuge
in the day of my distress.

1807
01:52:41,959 --> 01:52:45,759
To you, my strength, I will sing praises.

1808
01:52:46,939 --> 01:52:50,419
For God is my high tower, the God of my
mercy.

1809
01:52:51,759 --> 01:52:53,439
Psalm sixty.

1810
01:52:53,479 --> 01:52:56,019
God, you have rejected us.

1811
01:52:56,619 --> 01:52:57,839
You have broken us down.

1812
01:52:58,619 --> 01:52:59,579
You have been angry.

1813
01:53:00,279 --> 01:53:01,819
Restore us, again.

1814
01:53:03,079 --> 01:53:04,759
You have made the land tremble.

1815
01:53:05,339 --> 01:53:06,239
You have torn it.

1816
01:53:06,639 --> 01:53:09,059
Mend its fractures, for it quakes.

1817
01:53:09,939 --> 01:53:11,839
You have shown your people hard things.

1818
01:53:12,719 --> 01:53:15,519
You have made us drink the wine that makes
us stagger.

1819
01:53:16,339 --> 01:53:21,619
You have given a banner to those who fear
you, that it may be displayed because of the

1820
01:53:21,659 --> 01:53:21,959
truth.

1821
01:53:21,999 --> 01:53:24,079
Selah.

1822
01:53:24,119 --> 01:53:29,499
So that your beloved may be delivered,
save with your right hand, and answer us.

1823
01:53:29,539 --> 01:53:34,099
God has spoken from his sanctuary: “I will
triumph.

1824
01:53:35,219 --> 01:53:39,879
I will divide Shechem, and measure out the
valley of Succoth.

1825
01:53:39,919 --> 01:53:42,979
Gilead is mine, and Manasseh is mine.

1826
01:53:44,019 --> 01:53:46,799
Ephraim also is the defence of my head.

1827
01:53:47,819 --> 01:53:49,999
Judah is my sceptre.

1828
01:53:50,039 --> 01:53:51,539
Moab is my wash basin.

1829
01:53:52,819 --> 01:53:54,899
I will throw my sandal on Edom.

1830
01:53:55,529 --> 01:53:58,059
I shout in triumph over Philistia.”

1831
01:53:58,339 --> 01:54:00,399
Who will bring me into the strong city?

1832
01:54:01,359 --> 01:54:02,799
Who has led me to Edom?

1833
01:54:03,579 --> 01:54:05,619
Haven’t you, God, rejected us?

1834
01:54:06,079 --> 01:54:08,419
You don’t go out with our armies, God.

1835
01:54:09,379 --> 01:54:13,739
Give us help against the adversary, for
the help of man is vain.

1836
01:54:14,999 --> 01:54:20,519
Through God we will do valiantly, for it
is he who will tread down our adversaries.

1837
01:54:21,399 --> 01:54:23,239
Psalm sixty-one.

1838
01:54:23,279 --> 01:54:24,719
Hear my cry, God.

1839
01:54:25,619 --> 01:54:26,579
Listen to my prayer.

1840
01:54:27,319 --> 01:54:31,459
From the end of the earth, I will call to
you when my heart is overwhelmed.

1841
01:54:32,559 --> 01:54:34,959
Lead me to the rock that is higher than I.

1842
01:54:35,306 --> 01:54:39,766
For you have been a refuge for me, a
strong tower from the enemy.

1843
01:54:40,726 --> 01:54:42,506
I will dwell in your tent forever.

1844
01:54:43,506 --> 01:54:46,126
I will take refuge in the shelter of your
wings.

1845
01:54:46,166 --> 01:54:48,066
Selah.

1846
01:54:48,106 --> 01:54:50,706
For you, God, have heard my vows.

1847
01:54:51,426 --> 01:54:54,586
You have given me the heritage of those
who fear your name.

1848
01:54:55,486 --> 01:54:57,406
You will prolong the king’s life.

1849
01:54:58,226 --> 01:54:59,606
His years will be for generations.

1850
01:55:01,166 --> 01:55:03,726
He shall be enthroned in God’s presence
forever.

1851
01:55:04,606 --> 01:55:08,906
Appoint your loving kindness and truth,
that they may preserve him.

1852
01:55:09,706 --> 01:55:15,186
So I will sing praise to your name
forever, that I may fulfil my vows daily.

1853
01:55:16,426 --> 01:55:18,526
Psalm sixty-two.

1854
01:55:18,566 --> 01:55:20,526
My soul rests in God alone.

1855
01:55:21,286 --> 01:55:22,806
My salvation is from him.

1856
01:55:23,666 --> 01:55:27,486
He alone is my rock, my salvation, and my
fortress.

1857
01:55:28,526 --> 01:55:30,166
I will never be greatly shaken.

1858
01:55:30,986 --> 01:55:33,226
How long will you assault a man?

1859
01:55:33,266 --> 01:55:38,346
Would all of you throw him down, like a
leaning wall, like a tottering fence?

1860
01:55:39,366 --> 01:55:43,006
They fully intend to throw him down from
his lofty place.

1861
01:55:43,706 --> 01:55:44,746
They delight in lies.

1862
01:55:45,606 --> 01:55:48,926
They bless with their mouth, but they
curse inwardly.

1863
01:55:48,966 --> 01:55:50,986
Selah.

1864
01:55:51,026 --> 01:55:56,966
My soul, wait in silence for God alone,
for my expectation is from him.

1865
01:55:57,826 --> 01:56:01,666
He alone is my rock and my salvation, my
fortress.

1866
01:56:02,486 --> 01:56:03,806
I will not be shaken.

1867
01:56:04,706 --> 01:56:07,126
My salvation and my honour is with God.

1868
01:56:07,766 --> 01:56:11,226
The rock of my strength, and my refuge, is
in God.

1869
01:56:12,126 --> 01:56:14,466
Trust in him at all times, you people.

1870
01:56:15,286 --> 01:56:17,046
Pour out your heart before him.

1871
01:56:17,966 --> 01:56:19,546
God is a refuge for us.

1872
01:56:19,586 --> 01:56:21,506
Selah.

1873
01:56:21,546 --> 01:56:26,726
Surely men of low degree are just a
breath, and men of high degree are a lie.

1874
01:56:27,646 --> 01:56:29,426
In the balances they will go up.

1875
01:56:29,766 --> 01:56:31,766
They are together lighter than a breath.

1876
01:56:32,846 --> 01:56:33,866
Don’t trust in oppression.

1877
01:56:34,666 --> 01:56:36,086
Don’t become vain in robbery.

1878
01:56:37,266 --> 01:56:40,446
If riches increase, don’t set your heart
on them.

1879
01:56:41,386 --> 01:56:47,026
God has spoken once; twice I have heard
this, that power belongs to God.

1880
01:56:47,726 --> 01:56:54,286
Also to you, Lord, belongs loving kindness,
for you reward every man according to his

1881
01:56:54,326 --> 01:56:55,226
work.

1882
01:56:55,606 --> 01:56:57,526
Psalm sixty-three.

1883
01:56:57,566 --> 01:56:59,466
God, you are my God.

1884
01:57:00,226 --> 01:57:01,766
I will earnestly seek you.

1885
01:57:02,346 --> 01:57:03,986
My soul thirsts for you.

1886
01:57:04,269 --> 01:57:10,689
My flesh longs for you, in a dry and weary
land, where there is no water.

1887
01:57:11,709 --> 01:57:16,829
So I have seen you in the sanctuary,
watching your power and your glory.

1888
01:57:18,429 --> 01:57:23,289
Because your loving kindness is better
than life, my lips shall praise you.

1889
01:57:23,769 --> 01:57:25,609
So I will bless you while I live.

1890
01:57:26,469 --> 01:57:28,949
I will lift up my hands in your name.

1891
01:57:29,429 --> 01:57:33,009
My soul shall be satisfied as with the
richest food.

1892
01:57:34,249 --> 01:57:40,689
My mouth shall praise you with joyful lips,
when I remember you on my bed, and think

1893
01:57:40,729 --> 01:57:42,449
about you in the night watches.

1894
01:57:43,109 --> 01:57:44,989
For you have been my help.

1895
01:57:45,809 --> 01:57:48,449
I will rejoice in the shadow of your
wings.

1896
01:57:49,649 --> 01:57:51,649
My soul stays close to you.

1897
01:57:52,279 --> 01:57:54,269
Your right hand holds me up.

1898
01:57:54,829 --> 01:58:00,209
But those who seek my soul to destroy it
shall go into the lower parts of the earth.

1899
01:58:01,149 --> 01:58:03,769
They shall be given over to the power of
the sword.

1900
01:58:04,729 --> 01:58:06,069
They shall be jackal food.

1901
01:58:06,709 --> 01:58:09,009
But the king shall rejoice in God.

1902
01:58:09,569 --> 01:58:15,429
Everyone who swears by him will praise him,
for the mouth of those who speak lies shall

1903
01:58:15,469 --> 01:58:16,369
be silenced.

1904
01:58:16,969 --> 01:58:19,229
Psalm sixty-four.

1905
01:58:19,269 --> 01:58:21,929
Hear my voice, God, in my complaint.

1906
01:58:22,969 --> 01:58:25,729
Preserve my life from fear of the enemy.

1907
01:58:26,789 --> 01:58:32,809
Hide me from the conspiracy of the wicked,
from the noisy crowd of the ones doing evil;

1908
01:58:33,649 --> 01:58:40,189
who sharpen their tongue like a sword, and
aim their arrows, deadly words, to shoot innocent

1909
01:58:40,229 --> 01:58:41,669
men from ambushes.

1910
01:58:42,369 --> 01:58:44,909
They shoot at him suddenly and fearlessly.

1911
01:58:45,909 --> 01:58:48,649
They encourage themselves in evil plans.

1912
01:58:49,589 --> 01:58:51,989
They talk about laying snares secretly.

1913
01:58:53,109 --> 01:58:55,049
They say, “Who will see them?”

1914
01:58:55,449 --> 01:58:59,609
They plot injustice, saying, “We have made
a perfect plan!”

1915
01:59:00,609 --> 01:59:03,149
Surely man’s mind and heart are cunning.

1916
01:59:04,009 --> 01:59:05,429
But God will shoot at them.

1917
01:59:05,949 --> 01:59:08,489
They will be suddenly struck down with an
arrow.

1918
01:59:09,529 --> 01:59:11,429
Their own tongues shall ruin them.

1919
01:59:12,309 --> 01:59:14,329
All who see them will shake their heads.

1920
01:59:15,449 --> 01:59:17,089
All mankind shall be afraid.

1921
01:59:18,209 --> 01:59:23,069
They shall declare the work of God, and
shall wisely ponder what he has done.

1922
01:59:23,709 --> 01:59:28,049
The righteous shall be glad in the LORD,
and shall take refuge in him.

1923
01:59:28,428 --> 01:59:30,928
All the upright in heart shall praise him!

1924
01:59:31,868 --> 01:59:34,128
Psalm sixty-five.

1925
01:59:34,168 --> 01:59:36,748
Praise waits for you, God, in Zion.

1926
01:59:38,028 --> 01:59:39,888
Vows shall be performed to you.

1927
01:59:40,948 --> 01:59:44,328
You who hear prayer, all men will come to
you.

1928
01:59:45,348 --> 01:59:49,828
Sins overwhelmed me, but you atoned for
our transgressions.

1929
01:59:50,388 --> 01:59:56,828
Blessed is the one whom you choose and cause
to come near, that he may live in your courts.

1930
01:59:57,928 --> 02:00:01,888
We will be filled with the goodness of
your house, your holy temple.

1931
02:00:02,828 --> 02:00:07,828
By awesome deeds of righteousness, you
answer us, God of our salvation.

1932
02:00:08,728 --> 02:00:14,628
You who are the hope of all the ends of
the earth, of those who are far away on the sea.

1933
02:00:15,668 --> 02:00:20,548
By your power, you form the mountains,
having armed yourself with strength.

1934
02:00:20,588 --> 02:00:26,928
You still the roaring of the seas, the
roaring of their waves, and the turmoil of the

1935
02:00:26,968 --> 02:00:27,868
nations.

1936
02:00:28,088 --> 02:00:32,688
They also who dwell in faraway places are
afraid at your wonders.

1937
02:00:33,708 --> 02:00:37,568
You call the morning’s dawn and the
evening with songs of joy.

1938
02:00:38,728 --> 02:00:40,968
You visit the earth, and water it.

1939
02:00:41,728 --> 02:00:43,068
You greatly enrich it.

1940
02:00:43,908 --> 02:00:45,968
The river of God is full of water.

1941
02:00:46,608 --> 02:00:50,408
You provide them grain, for so you have
ordained it.

1942
02:00:50,588 --> 02:00:52,268
You drench its furrows.

1943
02:00:52,948 --> 02:00:54,128
You level its ridges.

1944
02:00:54,748 --> 02:00:56,068
You soften it with showers.

1945
02:00:57,108 --> 02:00:58,368
You bless it with a crop.

1946
02:00:59,328 --> 02:01:01,268
You crown the year with your bounty.

1947
02:01:02,188 --> 02:01:04,208
Your carts overflow with abundance.

1948
02:01:05,308 --> 02:01:07,208
The wilderness grasslands overflow.

1949
02:01:08,388 --> 02:01:10,568
The hills are clothed with gladness.

1950
02:01:11,508 --> 02:01:13,608
The pastures are covered with flocks.

1951
02:01:14,168 --> 02:01:16,608
The valleys also are clothed with grain.

1952
02:01:17,448 --> 02:01:18,568
They shout for joy!

1953
02:01:19,568 --> 02:01:20,648
They also sing.

1954
02:01:21,588 --> 02:01:23,648
Psalm sixty-six.

1955
02:01:23,688 --> 02:01:26,688
Make a joyful shout to God, all the earth!

1956
02:01:27,448 --> 02:01:29,388
Sing to the glory of his name!

1957
02:01:30,248 --> 02:01:31,668
Offer glory and praise!

1958
02:01:32,728 --> 02:01:35,308
Tell God, “How awesome are your deeds!

1959
02:01:35,348 --> 02:01:40,708
Through the greatness of your power, your
enemies submit themselves to you.

1960
02:01:41,548 --> 02:01:47,068
All the earth will worship you, and will
sing to you; they will sing to your name.”

1961
02:01:47,108 --> 02:01:48,428
Selah.

1962
02:01:48,468 --> 02:01:54,068
Come, and see God’s deeds— awesome work on
behalf of the children of men.

1963
02:01:55,168 --> 02:01:57,348
He turned the sea into dry land.

1964
02:01:57,733 --> 02:01:59,513
They went through the river on foot.

1965
02:02:00,473 --> 02:02:02,673
There, we rejoiced in him.

1966
02:02:03,473 --> 02:02:05,453
He rules by his might forever.

1967
02:02:06,533 --> 02:02:08,453
His eyes watch the nations.

1968
02:02:09,613 --> 02:02:12,113
Don’t let the rebellious rise up against
him.

1969
02:02:12,153 --> 02:02:14,133
Selah.

1970
02:02:14,173 --> 02:02:15,693
Praise our God, you peoples!

1971
02:02:16,533 --> 02:02:23,093
Make the sound of his praise heard, who
preserves our life amongst the living, and doesn’t

1972
02:02:23,133 --> 02:02:24,753
allow our feet to be moved.

1973
02:02:25,633 --> 02:02:27,973
For you, God, have tested us.

1974
02:02:28,353 --> 02:02:31,233
You have refined us, as silver is refined.

1975
02:02:32,213 --> 02:02:33,773
You brought us into prison.

1976
02:02:34,413 --> 02:02:35,953
You laid a burden on our backs.

1977
02:02:36,853 --> 02:02:39,333
You allowed men to ride over our heads.

1978
02:02:39,913 --> 02:02:44,893
We went through fire and through water, but
you brought us to the place of abundance.

1979
02:02:46,113 --> 02:02:48,513
I will come into your temple with burnt
offerings.

1980
02:02:49,393 --> 02:02:55,733
I will pay my vows to you, which my
lips promised, and my mouth spoke, when I was in

1981
02:02:55,773 --> 02:02:56,673
distress.

1982
02:02:56,893 --> 02:03:03,313
I will offer to you burnt offerings of fat
animals, with the offering of rams, I will

1983
02:03:03,353 --> 02:03:04,733
offer bulls with goats.

1984
02:03:04,773 --> 02:03:06,853
Selah.

1985
02:03:06,893 --> 02:03:09,693
Come and hear, all you who fear God.

1986
02:03:10,473 --> 02:03:13,293
I will declare what he has done for my
soul.

1987
02:03:13,753 --> 02:03:15,313
I cried to him with my mouth.

1988
02:03:15,913 --> 02:03:17,733
He was extolled with my tongue.

1989
02:03:18,433 --> 02:03:22,353
If I cherished sin in my heart, the Lord
wouldn’t have listened.

1990
02:03:23,033 --> 02:03:25,573
But most certainly, God has listened.

1991
02:03:26,613 --> 02:03:28,513
He has heard the voice of my prayer.

1992
02:03:29,033 --> 02:03:35,193
Blessed be God, who has not turned away my
prayer, nor his loving kindness from me.

1993
02:03:36,193 --> 02:03:38,213
Psalm sixty-seven.

1994
02:03:38,253 --> 02:03:44,173
May God be merciful to us, bless us, and
cause his face to shine on us.

1995
02:03:44,213 --> 02:03:45,933
Selah.

1996
02:03:45,973 --> 02:03:52,473
That your way may be known on earth, and
your salvation amongst all nations, let

1997
02:03:52,513 --> 02:03:54,213
the peoples praise you, God.

1998
02:03:54,953 --> 02:03:56,873
Let all the peoples praise you.

1999
02:03:56,913 --> 02:04:03,573
Oh let the nations be glad and sing for
joy, for you will judge the peoples with

2000
02:04:03,613 --> 02:04:06,413
equity, and govern the nations on earth.

2001
02:04:06,453 --> 02:04:08,093
Selah.

2002
02:04:08,133 --> 02:04:10,153
Let the peoples praise you, God.

2003
02:04:10,833 --> 02:04:12,653
Let all the peoples praise you.

2004
02:04:12,953 --> 02:04:14,933
The earth has yielded its increase.

2005
02:04:15,853 --> 02:04:19,093
God, even our own God, will bless us.

2006
02:04:19,753 --> 02:04:20,973
God will bless us.

2007
02:04:21,593 --> 02:04:24,013
All the ends of the earth shall fear him.

2008
02:04:24,303 --> 02:04:25,384
Psalm sixty-eight.

2009
02:04:25,424 --> 02:04:26,889
Let God arise!

2010
02:04:26,929 --> 02:04:29,397
Let his enemies be scattered!

2011
02:04:29,437 --> 02:04:33,912
Let them who hate him also flee before
him.

2012
02:04:33,952 --> 02:04:38,426
As smoke is driven away, so drive them
away.

2013
02:04:38,466 --> 02:04:44,947
As wax melts before the fire, so let the
wicked perish at the

2014
02:04:44,987 --> 02:04:46,452
presence of God.

2015
02:04:46,492 --> 02:04:49,461
But let the righteous be glad.

2016
02:04:49,501 --> 02:04:51,969
Let them rejoice before God.

2017
02:04:52,009 --> 02:04:54,979
Yes, let them rejoice with gladness.

2018
02:04:55,019 --> 02:04:56,484
Sing to God!

2019
02:04:56,524 --> 02:04:58,992
Sing praises to his name!

2020
02:04:59,032 --> 02:05:05,011
Extol him who rides on the clouds: to the
LORD, his name!

2021
02:05:05,051 --> 02:05:06,516
Rejoice before him!

2022
02:05:06,556 --> 02:05:13,036
A father of the fatherless, and a defender
of the widows, is God

2023
02:05:13,076 --> 02:05:15,043
in his holy habitation.

2024
02:05:15,083 --> 02:05:18,123
God sets the lonely in families.

2025
02:05:18,163 --> 02:05:24,643
He brings out the prisoners with singing,
but the rebellious dwell in a sun-scorched

2026
02:05:24,683 --> 02:05:25,583
land.

2027
02:05:25,943 --> 02:05:31,403
God, when you went out before your people,
when you marched through the wilderness...

2028
02:05:31,443 --> 02:05:33,203
Selah.

2029
02:05:33,243 --> 02:05:34,323
The earth trembled.

2030
02:05:35,043 --> 02:05:41,663
The sky also poured down rain at the presence
of the God of Sinai— at the presence of

2031
02:05:41,703 --> 02:05:43,523
God, the God of Israel.

2032
02:05:44,663 --> 02:05:47,283
You, God, sent a plentiful rain.

2033
02:05:48,283 --> 02:05:50,943
You confirmed your inheritance when it was
weary.

2034
02:05:51,383 --> 02:05:53,123
Your congregation lived therein.

2035
02:05:54,083 --> 02:05:57,043
You, God, prepared your goodness for the
poor.

2036
02:05:57,723 --> 02:05:59,183
The Lord announced the word.

2037
02:06:00,023 --> 02:06:02,323
The ones who proclaim it are a great
company.

2038
02:06:03,323 --> 02:06:04,723
“Kings of armies flee!

2039
02:06:05,383 --> 02:06:06,283
They flee!”

2040
02:06:07,043 --> 02:06:13,383
She who waits at home divides the plunder,
while you sleep amongst the camp fires, the

2041
02:06:13,423 --> 02:06:18,003
wings of a dove sheathed with silver, her
feathers with shining gold.

2042
02:06:18,743 --> 02:06:24,203
When the Almighty scattered kings in her,
it snowed on Zalmon.

2043
02:06:24,243 --> 02:06:27,343
The mountains of Bashan are majestic
mountains.

2044
02:06:28,103 --> 02:06:30,503
The mountains of Bashan are rugged.

2045
02:06:31,303 --> 02:06:38,423
Why do you look in envy, you rugged
mountains, at the mountain where God chooses to reign?

2046
02:06:38,463 --> 02:06:41,183
Yes, the LORD will dwell there forever.

2047
02:06:42,123 --> 02:06:46,443
The chariots of God are tens of thousands
and thousands of thousands.

2048
02:06:47,163 --> 02:06:51,543
The Lord is amongst them, from Sinai, into
the sanctuary.

2049
02:06:52,663 --> 02:06:54,483
You have ascended on high.

2050
02:06:55,303 --> 02:06:56,503
You have led away captives.

2051
02:06:57,138 --> 02:07:04,218
You have received gifts amongst people,
yes, amongst the rebellious also, that

2052
02:07:04,258 --> 02:07:06,218
the LORD God might dwell there.

2053
02:07:07,318 --> 02:07:13,738
Blessed be the Lord, who daily bears our
burdens, even the God who is our salvation.

2054
02:07:13,778 --> 02:07:16,878
Selah.

2055
02:07:16,918 --> 02:07:19,058
God is to us a God of deliverance.

2056
02:07:19,098 --> 02:07:23,338
To the LORD, the Lord, belongs escape from
death.

2057
02:07:23,378 --> 02:07:29,718
But God will strike through the head of his
enemies, the hairy scalp of such a one as

2058
02:07:29,758 --> 02:07:31,798
still continues in his guiltiness.

2059
02:07:32,438 --> 02:07:38,538
The Lord said, “I will bring you again from
Bashan, I will bring you again from the depths

2060
02:07:38,578 --> 02:07:44,958
of the sea, that you may crush them,
dipping your foot in blood, that the tongues of

2061
02:07:44,998 --> 02:07:47,698
your dogs may have their portion from your
enemies.”

2062
02:07:48,158 --> 02:07:55,018
They have seen your processions, God, even
the processions of my God, my King, into

2063
02:07:55,058 --> 02:07:55,958
the sanctuary.

2064
02:07:57,038 --> 02:08:03,138
The singers went before, the minstrels
followed after, amongst the ladies playing with

2065
02:08:03,178 --> 02:08:09,278
tambourines, “Bless God in the congregations, even
the Lord in the assembly of Israel!”

2066
02:08:10,018 --> 02:08:16,258
There is little Benjamin, their ruler, the
princes of Judah, their council, the princes

2067
02:08:16,298 --> 02:08:19,378
of Zebulun, and the princes of Naphtali.

2068
02:08:20,338 --> 02:08:22,478
Your God has commanded your strength.

2069
02:08:22,518 --> 02:08:26,178
Strengthen, God, that which you have done
for us.

2070
02:08:26,558 --> 02:08:30,998
Because of your temple at Jerusalem, kings
shall bring presents to you.

2071
02:08:31,658 --> 02:08:37,518
Rebuke the wild animal of the reeds, the
multitude of the bulls with the calves of the

2072
02:08:37,558 --> 02:08:38,458
peoples.

2073
02:08:38,798 --> 02:08:41,098
Trample under foot the bars of silver.

2074
02:08:42,018 --> 02:08:44,438
Scatter the nations who delight in war.

2075
02:08:45,298 --> 02:08:46,918
Princes shall come out of Egypt.

2076
02:08:47,698 --> 02:08:50,658
Ethiopia shall hurry to stretch out her
hands to God.

2077
02:08:51,458 --> 02:08:53,998
Sing to God, you kingdoms of the earth!

2078
02:08:54,838 --> 02:09:01,498
Sing praises to the Lord— Selah— to him
who rides on the heaven of heavens, which

2079
02:09:01,538 --> 02:09:06,598
are of old; behold, he utters his voice, a
mighty voice.

2080
02:09:06,638 --> 02:09:08,678
Ascribe strength to God!

2081
02:09:09,598 --> 02:09:13,958
His excellency is over Israel, his
strength is in the skies.

2082
02:09:14,858 --> 02:09:17,578
You are awesome, God, in your sanctuaries.

2083
02:09:17,992 --> 02:09:21,712
The God of Israel gives strength and power
to his people.

2084
02:09:21,752 --> 02:09:23,633
Praise be to God!

2085
02:09:23,673 --> 02:09:24,594
Psalm sixty-nine.

2086
02:09:24,634 --> 02:09:30,358
Save me, God, for the waters have come up
to my neck!

2087
02:09:30,398 --> 02:09:35,162
I sink in deep mire, where there is no
foothold.

2088
02:09:35,202 --> 02:09:40,446
I have come into deep waters, where the
floods overflow me.

2089
02:09:40,486 --> 02:09:43,328
I am weary with my crying.

2090
02:09:43,368 --> 02:09:45,249
My throat is dry.

2091
02:09:45,289 --> 02:09:48,692
My eyes fail looking for my God.

2092
02:09:48,732 --> 02:09:52,972
Those who hate me without a cause are more
than the hairs of my head.

2093
02:09:53,692 --> 02:09:58,352
Those who want to cut me off, being my
enemies wrongfully, are mighty.

2094
02:09:59,432 --> 02:10:01,812
I have to restore what I didn’t take away.

2095
02:10:02,572 --> 02:10:05,132
God, you know my foolishness.

2096
02:10:05,772 --> 02:10:07,692
My sins aren’t hidden from you.

2097
02:10:08,352 --> 02:10:12,912
Don’t let those who wait for you be shamed
through me, Lord GOD of Armies.

2098
02:10:13,612 --> 02:10:18,712
Don’t let those who seek you be brought to
dishonour through me, God of Israel.

2099
02:10:19,532 --> 02:10:22,532
Because for your sake, I have borne
reproach.

2100
02:10:23,072 --> 02:10:24,692
Shame has covered my face.

2101
02:10:25,412 --> 02:10:30,092
I have become a stranger to my brothers,
an alien to my mother’s children.

2102
02:10:31,232 --> 02:10:33,572
For the zeal of your house consumes me.

2103
02:10:34,472 --> 02:10:38,112
The reproaches of those who reproach you
have fallen on me.

2104
02:10:38,152 --> 02:10:42,712
When I wept and I fasted, that was to my
reproach.

2105
02:10:43,452 --> 02:10:47,952
When I made sackcloth my clothing, I
became a byword to them.

2106
02:10:48,452 --> 02:10:50,952
Those who sit in the gate talk about me.

2107
02:10:51,632 --> 02:10:53,552
I am the song of the drunkards.

2108
02:10:54,332 --> 02:10:59,212
But as for me, my prayer is to you, LORD,
in an acceptable time.

2109
02:10:59,632 --> 02:11:05,212
God, in the abundance of your loving kindness,
answer me in the truth of your salvation.

2110
02:11:06,392 --> 02:11:09,972
Deliver me out of the mire, and don’t let
me sink.

2111
02:11:10,632 --> 02:11:15,172
Let me be delivered from those who hate
me, and out of the deep waters.

2112
02:11:16,312 --> 02:11:21,332
Don’t let the flood waters overwhelm me,
neither let the deep swallow me up.

2113
02:11:22,232 --> 02:11:24,592
Don’t let the pit shut its mouth on me.

2114
02:11:24,952 --> 02:11:28,232
Answer me, LORD, for your loving kindness
is good.

2115
02:11:28,852 --> 02:11:32,692
According to the multitude of your tender
mercies, turn to me.

2116
02:11:33,252 --> 02:11:37,172
Don’t hide your face from your servant,
for I am in distress.

2117
02:11:38,292 --> 02:11:39,432
Answer me speedily!

2118
02:11:40,172 --> 02:11:42,632
Draw near to my soul and redeem it.

2119
02:11:42,885 --> 02:11:44,785
Ransom me because of my enemies.

2120
02:11:45,805 --> 02:11:50,605
You know my reproach, my shame, and my
dishonour.

2121
02:11:50,645 --> 02:11:52,965
My adversaries are all before you.

2122
02:11:53,925 --> 02:11:57,845
Reproach has broken my heart, and I am
full of heaviness.

2123
02:11:58,345 --> 02:12:04,505
I looked for some to take pity, but
there was none; for comforters, but I found none.

2124
02:12:05,405 --> 02:12:08,085
They also gave me poison for my food.

2125
02:12:08,825 --> 02:12:11,325
In my thirst, they gave me vinegar to
drink.

2126
02:12:11,945 --> 02:12:14,785
Let their table before them become a
snare.

2127
02:12:15,605 --> 02:12:17,805
May it become a retribution and a trap.

2128
02:12:18,785 --> 02:12:21,985
Let their eyes be darkened, so that they
can’t see.

2129
02:12:22,625 --> 02:12:25,045
Let their backs be continually bent.

2130
02:12:25,465 --> 02:12:27,445
Pour out your indignation on them.

2131
02:12:28,065 --> 02:12:30,725
Let the fierceness of your anger overtake
them.

2132
02:12:31,465 --> 02:12:33,245
Let their habitation be desolate.

2133
02:12:34,265 --> 02:12:36,025
Let no one dwell in their tents.

2134
02:12:36,945 --> 02:12:39,405
For they persecute him whom you have
wounded.

2135
02:12:40,065 --> 02:12:43,245
They tell of the sorrow of those whom you
have hurt.

2136
02:12:43,665 --> 02:12:45,645
Charge them with crime upon crime.

2137
02:12:46,485 --> 02:12:48,445
Don’t let them come into your
righteousness.

2138
02:12:49,185 --> 02:12:53,945
Let them be blotted out of the book
of life, and not be written with the righteous.

2139
02:12:54,965 --> 02:12:56,945
But I am in pain and distress.

2140
02:12:57,965 --> 02:13:00,885
Let your salvation, God, protect me.

2141
02:13:01,525 --> 02:13:07,145
I will praise the name of God with a song,
and will magnify him with thanksgiving.

2142
02:13:07,185 --> 02:13:13,065
It will please the LORD better than an ox,
or a bull that has horns and hoofs.

2143
02:13:13,845 --> 02:13:16,045
The humble have seen it, and are glad.

2144
02:13:17,185 --> 02:13:20,365
You who seek after God, let your heart
live.

2145
02:13:21,245 --> 02:13:25,665
For the LORD hears the needy, and doesn’t
despise his captive people.

2146
02:13:26,485 --> 02:13:31,885
Let heaven and earth praise him; the seas,
and everything that moves therein!

2147
02:13:32,625 --> 02:13:36,705
For God will save Zion, and build the
cities of Judah.

2148
02:13:37,605 --> 02:13:39,785
They shall settle there, and own it.

2149
02:13:40,625 --> 02:13:43,625
The children also of his servants shall
inherit it.

2150
02:13:44,065 --> 02:13:46,545
Those who love his name shall dwell
therein.

2151
02:13:47,825 --> 02:13:49,605
Psalm seventy.

2152
02:13:49,645 --> 02:13:51,765
Hurry, God, to deliver me.

2153
02:13:52,405 --> 02:13:53,945
Come quickly to help me, LORD.

2154
02:13:54,805 --> 02:13:58,165
Let them be disappointed and confounded
who seek my soul.

2155
02:13:58,205 --> 02:14:02,745
Let those who desire my ruin be turned
back in disgrace.

2156
02:14:03,365 --> 02:14:07,585
Let them be turned because of their shame
who say, “Aha!

2157
02:14:08,245 --> 02:14:09,145
Aha!”

2158
02:14:09,465 --> 02:14:14,185
Let all those who seek you rejoice and be
glad in you.

2159
02:14:14,865 --> 02:14:20,705
Let those who love your salvation
continually say, “Let God be exalted!”

2160
02:14:21,325 --> 02:14:22,845
But I am poor and needy.

2161
02:14:24,045 --> 02:14:25,345
Come to me quickly, God.

2162
02:14:26,085 --> 02:14:28,425
You are my help and my deliverer.

2163
02:14:29,065 --> 02:14:30,605
LORD, don’t delay.

2164
02:14:32,185 --> 02:14:34,845
Psalm seventy-one.

2165
02:14:34,885 --> 02:14:36,905
In you, LORD, I take refuge.

2166
02:14:37,965 --> 02:14:39,405
Never let me be disappointed.

2167
02:14:40,725 --> 02:14:43,945
Deliver me in your righteousness, and
rescue me.

2168
02:14:44,265 --> 02:14:46,485
Turn your ear to me, and save me.

2169
02:14:47,405 --> 02:14:51,185
Be to me a rock of refuge to which I may
always go.

2170
02:14:52,225 --> 02:14:56,885
Give the command to save me, for you are
my rock and my fortress.

2171
02:14:57,605 --> 02:15:03,405
Rescue me, my God, from the hand of
the wicked, from the hand of the unrighteous and

2172
02:15:03,445 --> 02:15:04,345
cruel man.

2173
02:15:05,105 --> 02:15:09,345
For you are my hope, Lord GOD, my
confidence from my youth.

2174
02:15:10,425 --> 02:15:12,385
I have relied on you from the womb.

2175
02:15:12,905 --> 02:15:15,585
You are he who took me out of my mother’s
womb.

2176
02:15:16,625 --> 02:15:18,205
I will always praise you.

2177
02:15:18,825 --> 02:15:22,745
I am a marvel to many, but you are my
strong refuge.

2178
02:15:23,605 --> 02:15:28,845
My mouth shall be filled with your praise,
with your honour all day long.

2179
02:15:30,025 --> 02:15:32,065
Don’t reject me in my old age.

2180
02:15:32,845 --> 02:15:35,185
Don’t forsake me when my strength fails.

2181
02:15:36,185 --> 02:15:37,985
For my enemies talk about me.

2182
02:15:38,625 --> 02:15:44,545
Those who watch for my soul conspire
together, saying, “God has forsaken him.

2183
02:15:45,325 --> 02:15:48,825
Pursue and take him, for no one will
rescue him.”

2184
02:15:49,585 --> 02:15:52,145
God, don’t be far from me.

2185
02:15:52,985 --> 02:15:55,085
My God, hurry to help me.

2186
02:15:55,705 --> 02:15:58,845
Let my accusers be disappointed and
consumed.

2187
02:15:59,925 --> 02:16:04,165
Let them be covered with disgrace and
scorn who want to harm me.

2188
02:16:04,765 --> 02:16:08,565
But I will always hope, and will add to
all of your praise.

2189
02:16:09,585 --> 02:16:15,945
My mouth will tell about your righteousness,
and of your salvation all day, though I

2190
02:16:15,985 --> 02:16:17,445
don’t know its full measure.

2191
02:16:18,425 --> 02:16:21,505
I will come with the mighty acts of the
Lord GOD.

2192
02:16:22,085 --> 02:16:25,925
I will make mention of your righteousness,
even of yours alone.

2193
02:16:26,805 --> 02:16:29,585
God, you have taught me from my youth.

2194
02:16:30,505 --> 02:16:33,945
Until now, I have declared your wondrous
works.

2195
02:16:34,479 --> 02:16:41,259
Yes, even when I am old and grey-haired,
God, don’t forsake me, until

2196
02:16:41,299 --> 02:16:47,619
I have declared your strength to the next
generation, your might to everyone who is to

2197
02:16:47,659 --> 02:16:48,559
come.

2198
02:16:48,699 --> 02:16:52,759
God, your righteousness also reaches to
the heavens.

2199
02:16:53,639 --> 02:16:54,939
You have done great things.

2200
02:16:55,659 --> 02:16:57,199
God, who is like you?

2201
02:16:57,839 --> 02:17:02,819
You, who have shown us many and bitter
troubles, you will let me live.

2202
02:17:03,479 --> 02:17:06,379
You will bring us up again from the depths
of the earth.

2203
02:17:07,119 --> 02:17:09,899
Increase my honour and comfort me again.

2204
02:17:11,039 --> 02:17:14,879
I will also praise you with the harp for
your faithfulness, my God.

2205
02:17:15,319 --> 02:17:18,999
I sing praises to you with the lyre, Holy
One of Israel.

2206
02:17:19,719 --> 02:17:21,599
My lips shall shout for joy!

2207
02:17:22,539 --> 02:17:26,499
My soul, which you have redeemed, sings
praises to you!

2208
02:17:27,419 --> 02:17:32,959
My tongue will also talk about your
righteousness all day long, for they are disappointed,

2209
02:17:32,999 --> 02:17:36,279
and they are confounded, who want to harm
me.

2210
02:17:36,639 --> 02:17:38,619
Psalm seventy-two.

2211
02:17:38,659 --> 02:17:43,939
God, give the king your justice; your
righteousness to the royal son.

2212
02:17:44,859 --> 02:17:49,059
He will judge your people with
righteousness, and your poor with justice.

2213
02:17:50,339 --> 02:17:53,039
The mountains shall bring prosperity to
the people.

2214
02:17:53,779 --> 02:17:55,859
The hills bring the fruit of
righteousness.

2215
02:17:57,099 --> 02:17:58,999
He will judge the poor of the people.

2216
02:17:59,539 --> 02:18:03,979
He will save the children of the needy,
and will break the oppressor in pieces.

2217
02:18:04,899 --> 02:18:10,599
They shall fear you while the sun endures;
and as long as the moon, throughout all generations.

2218
02:18:11,459 --> 02:18:16,319
He will come down like rain on the mown
grass, as showers that water the earth.

2219
02:18:16,359 --> 02:18:22,939
In his days, the righteous shall flourish,
and abundance of peace, until the

2220
02:18:22,979 --> 02:18:24,239
moon is no more.

2221
02:18:25,379 --> 02:18:30,959
He shall have dominion also from sea to sea,
from the River to the ends of the earth.

2222
02:18:31,839 --> 02:18:35,319
Those who dwell in the wilderness shall
bow before him.

2223
02:18:36,199 --> 02:18:38,079
His enemies shall lick the dust.

2224
02:18:38,959 --> 02:18:42,039
The kings of Tarshish and of the islands
will bring tribute.

2225
02:18:42,679 --> 02:18:46,079
The kings of Sheba and Seba shall offer
gifts.

2226
02:18:46,959 --> 02:18:50,099
Yes, all kings shall fall down before him.

2227
02:18:50,839 --> 02:18:52,439
All nations shall serve him.

2228
02:18:52,746 --> 02:18:58,186
For he will deliver the needy when he
cries; the poor, who has no helper.

2229
02:18:59,546 --> 02:19:01,606
He will have pity on the poor and needy.

2230
02:19:02,566 --> 02:19:04,846
He will save the souls of the needy.

2231
02:19:05,906 --> 02:19:09,086
He will redeem their soul from oppression
and violence.

2232
02:19:10,126 --> 02:19:12,486
Their blood will be precious in his sight.

2233
02:19:13,486 --> 02:19:17,546
He will live; and Sheba’s gold will be
given to him.

2234
02:19:18,506 --> 02:19:20,386
Men will pray for him continually.

2235
02:19:21,086 --> 02:19:23,386
They will bless him all day long.

2236
02:19:24,366 --> 02:19:27,066
Abundance of grain shall be throughout the
land.

2237
02:19:27,806 --> 02:19:29,766
Its fruit sways like Lebanon.

2238
02:19:30,826 --> 02:19:34,466
Let it flourish, thriving like the grass
of the field.

2239
02:19:35,006 --> 02:19:36,346
His name endures forever.

2240
02:19:37,326 --> 02:19:39,826
His name continues as long as the sun.

2241
02:19:40,786 --> 02:19:42,506
Men shall be blessed by him.

2242
02:19:43,406 --> 02:19:45,106
All nations will call him blessed.

2243
02:19:45,866 --> 02:19:52,126
Praise be to the LORD God, the God of
Israel, who alone does marvellous deeds.

2244
02:19:53,046 --> 02:19:55,386
Blessed be his glorious name forever!

2245
02:19:56,046 --> 02:19:58,386
Let the whole earth be filled with his
glory!

2246
02:19:59,386 --> 02:20:01,066
Amen and amen.

2247
02:20:01,806 --> 02:20:05,106
This ends the prayers by David, the son of
Jesse.

2248
02:20:06,386 --> 02:20:08,926
Psalm seventy-three.

2249
02:20:08,966 --> 02:20:13,546
Surely God is good to Israel, to those who
are pure in heart.

2250
02:20:14,526 --> 02:20:17,766
But as for me, my feet were almost gone.

2251
02:20:18,666 --> 02:20:20,226
My steps had nearly slipped.

2252
02:20:20,766 --> 02:20:25,426
For I was envious of the arrogant, when I
saw the prosperity of the wicked.

2253
02:20:26,066 --> 02:20:30,066
For there are no struggles in their death,
but their strength is firm.

2254
02:20:30,986 --> 02:20:35,966
They are free from burdens of men, neither
are they plagued like other men.

2255
02:20:36,766 --> 02:20:39,906
Therefore pride is like a chain around
their neck.

2256
02:20:40,686 --> 02:20:42,766
Violence covers them like a garment.

2257
02:20:43,626 --> 02:20:45,546
Their eyes bulge with fat.

2258
02:20:46,226 --> 02:20:48,906
Their minds pass the limits of conceit.

2259
02:20:49,386 --> 02:20:51,406
They scoff and speak with malice.

2260
02:20:52,606 --> 02:20:54,646
In arrogance, they threaten oppression.

2261
02:20:55,866 --> 02:20:57,786
They have set their mouth in the heavens.

2262
02:20:58,706 --> 02:21:00,446
Their tongue walks through the earth.

2263
02:21:00,846 --> 02:21:05,586
Therefore their people return to them, and
they drink up waters of abundance.

2264
02:21:06,426 --> 02:21:08,786
They say, “How does God know?

2265
02:21:09,586 --> 02:21:11,186
Is there knowledge in the Most High?”

2266
02:21:12,146 --> 02:21:14,306
Behold, these are the wicked.

2267
02:21:15,206 --> 02:21:18,586
Being always at ease, they increase in
riches.

2268
02:21:19,072 --> 02:21:25,632
Surely I have cleansed my heart in vain,
and washed my hands in innocence, For all

2269
02:21:25,672 --> 02:21:29,332
day long I have been plagued, and punished
every morning.

2270
02:21:30,332 --> 02:21:36,832
If I had said, “I will speak
thus”, behold, I would have betrayed the generation

2271
02:21:36,872 --> 02:21:37,852
of your children.

2272
02:21:38,712 --> 02:21:45,112
When I tried to understand this, it was
too painful for me— until I entered God’s sanctuary,

2273
02:21:45,152 --> 02:21:47,592
and considered their latter end.

2274
02:21:48,512 --> 02:21:51,052
Surely you set them in slippery places.

2275
02:21:51,772 --> 02:21:53,432
You throw them down to destruction.

2276
02:21:54,532 --> 02:21:56,092
How they are suddenly destroyed!

2277
02:21:57,232 --> 02:21:59,852
They are completely swept away with
terrors.

2278
02:21:59,892 --> 02:22:06,692
As a dream when one wakes up, so, Lord,
when you awake, you will despise their

2279
02:22:06,732 --> 02:22:07,632
fantasies.

2280
02:22:07,872 --> 02:22:09,772
For my soul was grieved.

2281
02:22:10,492 --> 02:22:12,072
I was embittered in my heart.

2282
02:22:12,932 --> 02:22:14,712
I was so senseless and ignorant.

2283
02:22:15,472 --> 02:22:17,472
I was a brute beast before you.

2284
02:22:18,432 --> 02:22:21,332
Nevertheless, I am continually with you.

2285
02:22:21,932 --> 02:22:23,592
You have held my right hand.

2286
02:22:24,192 --> 02:22:28,852
You will guide me with your counsel, and
afterward receive me to glory.

2287
02:22:29,872 --> 02:22:31,492
Whom do I have in heaven?

2288
02:22:32,452 --> 02:22:35,652
There is no one on earth whom I desire
besides you.

2289
02:22:36,272 --> 02:22:42,832
My flesh and my heart fails, but God is
the strength of my heart and my portion forever.

2290
02:22:43,332 --> 02:22:47,652
For, behold, those who are far from you
shall perish.

2291
02:22:48,412 --> 02:22:51,552
You have destroyed all those who are
unfaithful to you.

2292
02:22:52,392 --> 02:22:55,032
But it is good for me to come close to
God.

2293
02:22:55,752 --> 02:23:00,992
I have made the Lord the LORD my refuge,
that I may tell of all your works.

2294
02:23:02,392 --> 02:23:04,132
Psalm seventy-four.

2295
02:23:04,172 --> 02:23:07,112
God, why have you rejected us forever?

2296
02:23:08,172 --> 02:23:11,512
Why does your anger smoulder against the
sheep of your pasture?

2297
02:23:12,192 --> 02:23:18,232
Remember your congregation, which you purchased of
old, which you have redeemed to be

2298
02:23:18,272 --> 02:23:22,972
the tribe of your inheritance: Mount Zion,
in which you have lived.

2299
02:23:23,892 --> 02:23:29,612
Lift up your feet to the perpetual ruins, all
the evil that the enemy has done in the

2300
02:23:29,652 --> 02:23:29,992
sanctuary.

2301
02:23:30,032 --> 02:23:33,892
Your adversaries have roared in the middle
of your assembly.

2302
02:23:34,912 --> 02:23:37,032
They have set up their standards as signs.

2303
02:23:37,654 --> 02:23:42,554
They behaved like men wielding axes,
cutting through a thicket of trees.

2304
02:23:43,494 --> 02:23:48,014
Now they break all its carved work down
with hatchet and hammers.

2305
02:23:48,674 --> 02:23:51,334
They have burnt your sanctuary to the
ground.

2306
02:23:52,274 --> 02:23:54,934
They have profaned the dwelling place of
your Name.

2307
02:23:55,854 --> 02:23:59,314
They said in their heart, “We will crush
them completely.”

2308
02:24:00,114 --> 02:24:04,054
They have burnt up all the places in the
land where God was worshipped.

2309
02:24:05,034 --> 02:24:06,854
We see no miraculous signs.

2310
02:24:07,874 --> 02:24:13,594
There is no longer any prophet, neither is
there amongst us anyone who knows how long.

2311
02:24:14,154 --> 02:24:17,734
How long, God, shall the adversary
reproach?

2312
02:24:18,534 --> 02:24:20,874
Shall the enemy blaspheme your name
forever?

2313
02:24:21,674 --> 02:24:24,954
Why do you draw back your hand, even your
right hand?

2314
02:24:25,594 --> 02:24:27,974
Take it from your chest and consume them!

2315
02:24:28,274 --> 02:24:32,754
Yet God is my King of old, working
salvation throughout the earth.

2316
02:24:33,674 --> 02:24:35,654
You divided the sea by your strength.

2317
02:24:36,294 --> 02:24:39,114
You broke the heads of the sea monsters in
the waters.

2318
02:24:40,034 --> 02:24:42,314
You broke the heads of Leviathan in
pieces.

2319
02:24:43,134 --> 02:24:45,834
You gave him as food to people and desert
creatures.

2320
02:24:46,734 --> 02:24:48,834
You opened up spring and stream.

2321
02:24:49,594 --> 02:24:51,194
You dried up mighty rivers.

2322
02:24:51,934 --> 02:24:55,294
The day is yours, the night is also yours.

2323
02:24:56,214 --> 02:24:58,314
You have prepared the light and the sun.

2324
02:24:58,774 --> 02:25:01,014
You have set all the boundaries of the
earth.

2325
02:25:01,754 --> 02:25:03,414
You have made summer and winter.

2326
02:25:03,934 --> 02:25:07,354
Remember this, that the enemy has mocked
you, LORD.

2327
02:25:08,274 --> 02:25:10,714
Foolish people have blasphemed your name.

2328
02:25:11,654 --> 02:25:14,734
Don’t deliver the soul of your dove to
wild beasts.

2329
02:25:15,654 --> 02:25:18,034
Don’t forget the life of your poor
forever.

2330
02:25:18,074 --> 02:25:23,554
Honour your covenant, for haunts of violence
fill the dark places of the earth.

2331
02:25:24,114 --> 02:25:26,354
Don’t let the oppressed return ashamed.

2332
02:25:27,354 --> 02:25:29,554
Let the poor and needy praise your name.

2333
02:25:30,414 --> 02:25:31,374
Arise, God!

2334
02:25:32,194 --> 02:25:33,274
Plead your own cause.

2335
02:25:34,354 --> 02:25:37,254
Remember how the foolish man mocks you all
day.

2336
02:25:38,154 --> 02:25:40,134
Don’t forget the voice of your
adversaries.

2337
02:25:40,854 --> 02:25:44,914
The tumult of those who rise up against
you ascends continually.

2338
02:25:46,354 --> 02:25:48,554
Psalm seventy-five.

2339
02:25:48,594 --> 02:25:49,874
We give thanks to you, God.

2340
02:25:50,674 --> 02:25:53,094
We give thanks, for your Name is near.

2341
02:25:53,430 --> 02:25:55,890
Men tell about your wondrous works.

2342
02:25:57,010 --> 02:26:01,490
When I choose the appointed time, I will
judge blamelessly.

2343
02:26:02,420 --> 02:26:05,170
The earth and all its inhabitants quake.

2344
02:26:06,310 --> 02:26:07,930
I firmly hold its pillars.

2345
02:26:07,970 --> 02:26:09,990
Selah.

2346
02:26:10,030 --> 02:26:12,530
I said to the arrogant, “Don’t boast!”

2347
02:26:13,610 --> 02:26:16,990
I said to the wicked, “Don’t lift up the
horn.

2348
02:26:17,710 --> 02:26:19,690
Don’t lift up your horn on high.

2349
02:26:20,390 --> 02:26:22,350
Don’t speak with a stiff neck.”

2350
02:26:23,410 --> 02:26:29,810
For neither from the east, nor from the
west, nor yet from the south, comes exaltation.

2351
02:26:30,570 --> 02:26:31,770
But God is the judge.

2352
02:26:32,730 --> 02:26:35,610
He puts down one, and lifts up another.

2353
02:26:36,430 --> 02:26:41,690
For in the LORD’s hand there is a cup,
full of foaming wine mixed with spices.

2354
02:26:42,790 --> 02:26:43,690
He pours it out.

2355
02:26:44,270 --> 02:26:49,290
Indeed the wicked of the earth drink and
drink it to its very dregs.

2356
02:26:49,750 --> 02:26:55,070
But I will declare this forever: I will
sing praises to the God of Jacob.

2357
02:26:55,990 --> 02:27:01,830
I will cut off all the horns of the
wicked, but the horns of the righteous shall be lifted

2358
02:27:01,870 --> 02:27:02,770
up.

2359
02:27:03,390 --> 02:27:05,910
Psalm seventy-six.

2360
02:27:05,950 --> 02:27:07,750
In Judah, God is known.

2361
02:27:08,590 --> 02:27:10,490
His name is great in Israel.

2362
02:27:10,970 --> 02:27:13,150
His tabernacle is also in Salem.

2363
02:27:14,130 --> 02:27:15,630
His dwelling place in Zion.

2364
02:27:16,530 --> 02:27:22,610
There he broke the flaming arrows of the
bow, the shield, and the sword, and the weapons

2365
02:27:22,650 --> 02:27:23,190
of war.

2366
02:27:23,230 --> 02:27:25,950
Selah.

2367
02:27:25,990 --> 02:27:30,690
Glorious are you, and excellent, more than
mountains of game.

2368
02:27:30,730 --> 02:27:35,070
Valiant men lie plundered, they have slept
their last sleep.

2369
02:27:35,900 --> 02:27:38,630
None of the men of war can lift their
hands.

2370
02:27:39,310 --> 02:27:45,330
At your rebuke, God of Jacob, both chariot
and horse are cast into a dead sleep.

2371
02:27:46,270 --> 02:27:49,130
You, even you, are to be feared.

2372
02:27:49,930 --> 02:27:53,010
Who can stand in your sight when you are
angry?

2373
02:27:54,030 --> 02:27:55,810
You pronounced judgement from heaven.

2374
02:27:56,630 --> 02:28:03,250
The earth feared, and was silent, when God
arose to judgement, to save all the afflicted

2375
02:28:03,290 --> 02:28:04,290
ones of the earth.

2376
02:28:04,330 --> 02:28:07,090
Selah.

2377
02:28:07,130 --> 02:28:09,070
Surely the wrath of man praises you.

2378
02:28:09,930 --> 02:28:12,130
The survivors of your wrath are
restrained.

2379
02:28:12,970 --> 02:28:16,210
Make vows to the LORD your God, and fulfil
them!

2380
02:28:16,970 --> 02:28:21,130
Let all of his neighbours bring presents
to him who is to be feared.

2381
02:28:22,210 --> 02:28:24,170
He will cut off the spirit of princes.

2382
02:28:24,821 --> 02:28:27,141
He is feared by the kings of the earth.

2383
02:28:28,361 --> 02:28:31,141
Psalm seventy-seven.

2384
02:28:31,181 --> 02:28:32,861
My cry goes to God!

2385
02:28:33,641 --> 02:28:38,401
Indeed, I cry to God for help, and for him
to listen to me.

2386
02:28:39,101 --> 02:28:42,061
In the day of my trouble I sought the
Lord.

2387
02:28:43,161 --> 02:28:47,081
My hand was stretched out in the night,
and didn’t get tired.

2388
02:28:48,021 --> 02:28:50,401
My soul refused to be comforted.

2389
02:28:50,821 --> 02:28:53,241
I remember God, and I groan.

2390
02:28:53,941 --> 02:28:56,701
I complain, and my spirit is overwhelmed.

2391
02:28:56,741 --> 02:28:59,341
Selah.

2392
02:28:59,381 --> 02:29:01,421
You hold my eyelids open.

2393
02:29:02,261 --> 02:29:04,561
I am so troubled that I can’t speak.

2394
02:29:05,021 --> 02:29:09,021
I have considered the days of old, the
years of ancient times.

2395
02:29:10,001 --> 02:29:11,841
I remember my song in the night.

2396
02:29:12,571 --> 02:29:19,081
I consider in my own heart; my spirit
diligently enquires: “Will the Lord reject

2397
02:29:19,121 --> 02:29:20,021
us forever?

2398
02:29:20,881 --> 02:29:22,781
Will he be favourable no more?

2399
02:29:23,541 --> 02:29:26,101
Has his loving kindness vanished forever?

2400
02:29:27,181 --> 02:29:29,241
Does his promise fail for generations?

2401
02:29:30,721 --> 02:29:32,281
Has God forgotten to be gracious?

2402
02:29:33,381 --> 02:29:35,781
Has he, in anger, withheld his
compassion?”

2403
02:29:35,821 --> 02:29:38,681
Selah.

2404
02:29:38,721 --> 02:29:44,781
Then I thought, “I will appeal to this: the
years of the right hand of the Most High.”

2405
02:29:45,821 --> 02:29:50,821
I will remember the LORD’s deeds; for I
will remember your wonders of old.

2406
02:29:51,301 --> 02:29:55,821
I will also meditate on all your work, and
consider your doings.

2407
02:29:56,601 --> 02:29:58,901
Your way, God, is in the sanctuary.

2408
02:30:00,181 --> 02:30:02,261
What god is great like God?

2409
02:30:03,001 --> 02:30:04,741
You are the God who does wonders.

2410
02:30:05,581 --> 02:30:08,541
You have made your strength known amongst
the peoples.

2411
02:30:09,181 --> 02:30:14,301
You have redeemed your people with your
arm, the sons of Jacob and Joseph.

2412
02:30:14,341 --> 02:30:16,141
Selah.

2413
02:30:16,181 --> 02:30:18,061
The waters saw you, God.

2414
02:30:18,961 --> 02:30:21,661
The waters saw you, and they writhed.

2415
02:30:22,161 --> 02:30:24,101
The depths also convulsed.

2416
02:30:24,601 --> 02:30:26,161
The clouds poured out water.

2417
02:30:26,861 --> 02:30:28,661
The skies resounded with thunder.

2418
02:30:29,821 --> 02:30:31,741
Your arrows also flashed around.

2419
02:30:32,901 --> 02:30:35,041
The voice of your thunder was in the
whirlwind.

2420
02:30:35,081 --> 02:30:38,141
The lightnings lit up the world.

2421
02:30:39,001 --> 02:30:40,581
The earth trembled and shook.

2422
02:30:41,141 --> 02:30:45,221
Your way was through the sea, your paths
through the great waters.

2423
02:30:46,221 --> 02:30:47,861
Your footsteps were not known.

2424
02:30:48,581 --> 02:30:52,861
You led your people like a flock, by the
hand of Moses and Aaron.

2425
02:30:54,101 --> 02:30:56,401
Psalm seventy-eight.

2426
02:30:56,441 --> 02:30:58,081
Hear my teaching, my people.

2427
02:30:58,390 --> 02:31:00,910
Turn your ears to the words of my mouth.

2428
02:31:01,830 --> 02:31:03,870
I will open my mouth in a parable.

2429
02:31:04,570 --> 02:31:10,930
I will utter dark sayings of old, which we
have heard and known, and our fathers have

2430
02:31:10,970 --> 02:31:11,870
told us.

2431
02:31:12,050 --> 02:31:17,250
We will not hide them from their children,
telling to the generation to come the praises

2432
02:31:17,290 --> 02:31:22,370
of the LORD, his strength, and his
wondrous deeds that he has done.

2433
02:31:23,070 --> 02:31:28,850
For he established a covenant in Jacob,
and appointed a teaching in Israel, which he

2434
02:31:28,890 --> 02:31:34,390
commanded our fathers, that they should make
them known to their children; that the generation

2435
02:31:34,430 --> 02:31:40,550
to come might know, even the children who
should be born; who should arise and tell their

2436
02:31:40,590 --> 02:31:46,790
children, that they might set their hope in
God, and not forget God’s deeds, but keep

2437
02:31:46,830 --> 02:31:53,190
his commandments, and might not be as
their fathers— a stubborn and rebellious generation,

2438
02:31:53,670 --> 02:31:59,850
a generation that didn’t make their hearts
loyal, whose spirit was not steadfast with

2439
02:31:59,890 --> 02:32:00,790
God.

2440
02:32:00,890 --> 02:32:06,870
The children of Ephraim, being armed and carrying
bows, turned back in the day of battle.

2441
02:32:07,570 --> 02:32:11,770
They didn’t keep God’s covenant, and
refused to walk in his law.

2442
02:32:12,550 --> 02:32:16,690
They forgot his doings, his wondrous deeds
that he had shown them.

2443
02:32:17,170 --> 02:32:22,850
He did marvellous things in the sight of
their fathers, in the land of Egypt, in the

2444
02:32:22,890 --> 02:32:23,830
field of Zoan.

2445
02:32:24,810 --> 02:32:28,030
He split the sea, and caused them to pass
through.

2446
02:32:28,910 --> 02:32:31,190
He made the waters stand as a heap.

2447
02:32:32,050 --> 02:32:37,530
In the daytime he also led them with a
cloud, and all night with a light of fire.

2448
02:32:38,270 --> 02:32:43,550
He split rocks in the wilderness, and gave
them drink abundantly as out of the depths.

2449
02:32:44,490 --> 02:32:50,110
He brought streams also out of the rock,
and caused waters to run down like rivers.

2450
02:32:51,110 --> 02:32:56,590
Yet they still went on to sin against him,
to rebel against the Most High in the desert.

2451
02:32:57,350 --> 02:33:01,430
They tempted God in their heart by asking
food according to their desire.

2452
02:33:02,310 --> 02:33:04,950
Yes, they spoke against God.

2453
02:33:05,670 --> 02:33:08,810
They said, “Can God prepare a table in the
wilderness?

2454
02:33:09,458 --> 02:33:15,738
Behold, he struck the rock, so that waters
gushed out, and streams overflowed.

2455
02:33:16,598 --> 02:33:18,318
Can he give bread also?

2456
02:33:19,178 --> 02:33:21,418
Will he provide meat for his people?”

2457
02:33:22,078 --> 02:33:25,158
Therefore the LORD heard, and was angry.

2458
02:33:25,958 --> 02:33:32,418
A fire was kindled against Jacob, anger
also went up against Israel, because they didn’t

2459
02:33:32,458 --> 02:33:35,478
believe in God, and didn’t trust in his
salvation.

2460
02:33:36,958 --> 02:33:41,038
Yet he commanded the skies above, and
opened the doors of heaven.

2461
02:33:41,578 --> 02:33:46,258
He rained down manna on them to eat, and
gave them food from the sky.

2462
02:33:46,978 --> 02:33:48,518
Man ate the bread of angels.

2463
02:33:49,418 --> 02:33:51,098
He sent them food to the full.

2464
02:33:51,898 --> 02:33:54,798
He caused the east wind to blow in the
sky.

2465
02:33:55,758 --> 02:33:58,218
By his power he guided the south wind.

2466
02:33:58,898 --> 02:34:04,978
He also rained meat on them as the dust,
winged birds as the sand of the seas.

2467
02:34:05,638 --> 02:34:09,778
He let them fall in the middle of their
camp, around their habitations.

2468
02:34:10,358 --> 02:34:12,558
So they ate, and were well filled.

2469
02:34:13,498 --> 02:34:15,318
He gave them their own desire.

2470
02:34:16,318 --> 02:34:18,178
They didn’t turn from their cravings.

2471
02:34:19,078 --> 02:34:24,698
Their food was yet in their mouths, when
the anger of God went up against them, killed

2472
02:34:24,738 --> 02:34:28,718
some of their strongest, and struck down
the young men of Israel.

2473
02:34:28,758 --> 02:34:33,898
For all this they still sinned, and didn’t
believe in his wondrous works.

2474
02:34:34,838 --> 02:34:39,398
Therefore he consumed their days in
vanity, and their years in terror.

2475
02:34:40,278 --> 02:34:43,658
When he killed them, then they enquired
after him.

2476
02:34:44,378 --> 02:34:47,058
They returned and sought God earnestly.

2477
02:34:47,598 --> 02:34:52,798
They remembered that God was their rock,
the Most High God, their redeemer.

2478
02:34:53,498 --> 02:34:57,778
But they flattered him with their mouth,
and lied to him with their tongue.

2479
02:34:58,758 --> 02:35:03,298
For their heart was not right with
him, neither were they faithful in his covenant.

2480
02:35:04,058 --> 02:35:09,238
But he, being merciful, forgave iniquity,
and didn’t destroy them.

2481
02:35:09,898 --> 02:35:15,898
Yes, many times he turned his anger away,
and didn’t stir up all his wrath.

2482
02:35:16,858 --> 02:35:22,978
He remembered that they were but flesh, a
wind that passes away, and doesn’t come again.

2483
02:35:23,538 --> 02:35:28,238
How often they rebelled against him in the
wilderness, and grieved him in the desert!

2484
02:35:28,698 --> 02:35:33,858
They turned again and tempted God, and
provoked the Holy One of Israel.

2485
02:35:34,858 --> 02:35:40,298
They didn’t remember his hand, nor the day
when he redeemed them from the adversary;

2486
02:35:41,078 --> 02:35:47,738
how he set his signs in Egypt, his wonders
in the field of Zoan, he turned their rivers

2487
02:35:47,778 --> 02:35:51,998
into blood, and their streams, so that
they could not drink.

2488
02:35:53,158 --> 02:35:59,658
He sent amongst them swarms of flies,
which devoured them; and frogs, which destroyed

2489
02:35:59,698 --> 02:36:00,598
them.

2490
02:36:00,658 --> 02:36:05,478
He also gave their increase to the
caterpillar, and their labour to the locust.

2491
02:36:06,338 --> 02:36:11,418
He destroyed their vines with hail, their
sycamore fig trees with frost.

2492
02:36:12,498 --> 02:36:18,438
He also gave over their livestock to
the hail, and their flocks to hot thunderbolts.

2493
02:36:18,798 --> 02:36:25,658
He threw on them the fierceness of
his anger, wrath, indignation, and trouble, and

2494
02:36:25,698 --> 02:36:27,358
a band of angels of evil.

2495
02:36:28,518 --> 02:36:30,398
He made a path for his anger.

2496
02:36:30,998 --> 02:36:36,957
He didn’t spare their soul from death, but
gave their life over to the pestilence, and

2497
02:36:36,998 --> 02:36:43,457
struck all the firstborn in Egypt, the chief
of their strength in the tents of Ham.

2498
02:36:43,498 --> 02:36:49,038
But he led out his own people like sheep,
and guided them in the wilderness like a flock.

2499
02:36:49,778 --> 02:36:55,998
He led them safely, so that they
weren’t afraid, but the sea overwhelmed their enemies.

2500
02:36:56,938 --> 02:37:02,698
He brought them to the border of his
sanctuary, to this mountain, which his right hand

2501
02:37:02,738 --> 02:37:03,638
had taken.

2502
02:37:03,958 --> 02:37:09,578
He also drove out the nations before them,
allotted them for an inheritance by line,

2503
02:37:10,378 --> 02:37:13,278
and made the tribes of Israel to dwell in
their tents.

2504
02:37:13,758 --> 02:37:18,938
Yet they tempted and rebelled against the
Most High God, and didn’t keep his testimonies,

2505
02:37:19,878 --> 02:37:23,378
but turned back, and dealt treacherously
like their fathers.

2506
02:37:24,018 --> 02:37:26,078
They were twisted like a deceitful bow.

2507
02:37:26,798 --> 02:37:32,617
For they provoked him to anger with their
high places, and moved him to jealousy with

2508
02:37:32,658 --> 02:37:33,718
their engraved images.

2509
02:37:34,235 --> 02:37:40,915
When God heard this, he was angry,
and greatly abhorred Israel, so that he abandoned

2510
02:37:40,955 --> 02:37:47,175
the tent of Shiloh, the tent which
he placed amongst men, and delivered his strength

2511
02:37:47,215 --> 02:37:51,495
into captivity, his glory into the
adversary’s hand.

2512
02:37:52,115 --> 02:37:57,075
He also gave his people over to the sword,
and was angry with his inheritance.

2513
02:37:58,435 --> 02:38:00,575
Fire devoured their young men.

2514
02:38:01,255 --> 02:38:03,295
Their virgins had no wedding song.

2515
02:38:04,175 --> 02:38:08,195
Their priests fell by the sword, and their
widows couldn’t weep.

2516
02:38:08,875 --> 02:38:15,015
Then the Lord awakened as one out of sleep,
like a mighty man who shouts by reason of

2517
02:38:15,055 --> 02:38:15,955
wine.

2518
02:38:16,255 --> 02:38:18,455
He struck his adversaries backward.

2519
02:38:19,395 --> 02:38:21,895
He put them to a perpetual reproach.

2520
02:38:22,335 --> 02:38:28,795
Moreover he rejected the tent of Joseph,
and didn’t choose the tribe of Ephraim, But

2521
02:38:28,835 --> 02:38:32,595
chose the tribe of Judah, Mount Zion which
he loved.

2522
02:38:33,895 --> 02:38:39,215
He built his sanctuary like the heights,
like the earth which he has established forever.

2523
02:38:40,395 --> 02:38:46,475
He also chose David his servant, and
took him from the sheepfolds; from following the

2524
02:38:46,515 --> 02:38:52,755
ewes that have their young, he brought him
to be the shepherd of Jacob, his people, and

2525
02:38:52,795 --> 02:38:54,235
Israel, his inheritance.

2526
02:38:55,575 --> 02:39:00,735
So he was their shepherd according to the
integrity of his heart, and guided them by

2527
02:39:00,775 --> 02:39:02,315
the skilfulness of his hands.

2528
02:39:03,635 --> 02:39:05,575
Psalm seventy-nine.

2529
02:39:05,615 --> 02:39:08,775
God, the nations have come into your
inheritance.

2530
02:39:09,735 --> 02:39:11,715
They have defiled your holy temple.

2531
02:39:12,635 --> 02:39:14,755
They have laid Jerusalem in heaps.

2532
02:39:15,275 --> 02:39:19,895
They have given the dead bodies of your servants
to be food for the birds of the sky,

2533
02:39:20,955 --> 02:39:23,735
the flesh of your saints to the animals of
the earth.

2534
02:39:24,355 --> 02:39:27,135
They have shed their blood like water
around Jerusalem.

2535
02:39:28,195 --> 02:39:29,855
There was no one to bury them.

2536
02:39:30,595 --> 02:39:36,215
We have become a reproach to our neighbours,
a scoffing and derision to those who are

2537
02:39:36,255 --> 02:39:37,155
around us.

2538
02:39:37,735 --> 02:39:38,835
How long, LORD?

2539
02:39:39,515 --> 02:39:40,855
Will you be angry forever?

2540
02:39:40,895 --> 02:39:43,835
Will your jealousy burn like fire?

2541
02:39:44,260 --> 02:39:49,640
Pour out your wrath on the nations that
don’t know you, on the kingdoms that don’t call

2542
02:39:49,680 --> 02:39:54,720
on your name, for they have devoured
Jacob, and destroyed his homeland.

2543
02:39:55,880 --> 02:39:59,320
Don’t hold the iniquities of our
forefathers against us.

2544
02:39:59,680 --> 02:40:04,600
Let your tender mercies speedily meet us,
for we are in desperate need.

2545
02:40:05,180 --> 02:40:09,640
Help us, God of our salvation, for the
glory of your name.

2546
02:40:10,740 --> 02:40:14,700
Deliver us, and forgive our sins, for your
name’s sake.

2547
02:40:15,940 --> 02:40:19,020
Why should the nations say, “Where is
their God?”

2548
02:40:19,060 --> 02:40:24,920
Let it be known amongst the nations,
before our eyes, that vengeance for your servants’

2549
02:40:25,200 --> 02:40:26,680
blood is being poured out.

2550
02:40:27,160 --> 02:40:29,760
Let the sighing of the prisoner come
before you.

2551
02:40:30,560 --> 02:40:35,420
According to the greatness of your power,
preserve those who are sentenced to death.

2552
02:40:35,460 --> 02:40:41,000
Pay back to our neighbours seven times
into their bosom their reproach with which they

2553
02:40:41,040 --> 02:40:42,280
have reproached you, Lord.

2554
02:40:42,720 --> 02:40:48,020
So we, your people and sheep of your
pasture, will give you thanks forever.

2555
02:40:49,100 --> 02:40:52,100
We will praise you forever, to all
generations.

2556
02:40:53,560 --> 02:40:55,020
Psalm eighty.

2557
02:40:55,060 --> 02:41:01,740
Hear us, Shepherd of Israel, you who lead
Joseph like a flock, you who

2558
02:41:01,780 --> 02:41:04,280
sit above the cherubim, shine out.

2559
02:41:04,320 --> 02:41:09,220
Before Ephraim, Benjamin, and Manasseh,
stir up your might!

2560
02:41:09,940 --> 02:41:10,980
Come to save us!

2561
02:41:11,680 --> 02:41:12,900
Turn us again, God.

2562
02:41:13,760 --> 02:41:17,020
Cause your face to shine, and we will be
saved.

2563
02:41:18,240 --> 02:41:23,580
LORD God of Armies, how long will you be
angry against the prayer of your people?

2564
02:41:24,280 --> 02:41:29,580
You have fed them with the bread of tears,
and given them tears to drink in large measure.

2565
02:41:30,220 --> 02:41:34,120
You make us a source of contention to our
neighbours.

2566
02:41:34,160 --> 02:41:36,240
Our enemies laugh amongst themselves.

2567
02:41:36,280 --> 02:41:38,480
Turn us again, God of Armies.

2568
02:41:39,280 --> 02:41:42,580
Cause your face to shine, and we will be
saved.

2569
02:41:43,740 --> 02:41:45,320
You brought a vine out of Egypt.

2570
02:41:46,000 --> 02:41:48,420
You drove out the nations, and planted it.

2571
02:41:49,080 --> 02:41:50,660
You cleared the ground for it.

2572
02:41:51,280 --> 02:41:53,660
It took deep root, and filled the land.

2573
02:41:54,580 --> 02:41:56,540
The mountains were covered with its
shadow.

2574
02:41:57,300 --> 02:41:59,420
Its boughs were like God’s cedars.

2575
02:41:59,680 --> 02:42:04,340
It sent out its branches to the sea, its
shoots to the River.

2576
02:42:05,400 --> 02:42:11,660
Why have you broken down its walls, so that
all those who pass by the way pluck it?

2577
02:42:12,620 --> 02:42:15,240
The boar out of the wood ravages it.

2578
02:42:16,120 --> 02:42:18,800
The wild animals of the field feed on it.

2579
02:42:19,180 --> 02:42:21,140
Turn again, we beg you, God of Armies.

2580
02:42:21,980 --> 02:42:28,520
Look down from heaven, and see, and visit
this vine, the stock which your right hand

2581
02:42:28,560 --> 02:42:32,360
planted, the branch that you made strong
for yourself.

2582
02:42:33,440 --> 02:42:34,680
It’s burnt with fire.

2583
02:42:35,420 --> 02:42:36,320
It’s cut down.

2584
02:42:36,900 --> 02:42:38,280
They perish at your rebuke.

2585
02:42:39,000 --> 02:42:44,740
Let your hand be on the man of your right
hand, on the son of man whom you made strong

2586
02:42:44,780 --> 02:42:45,680
for yourself.

2587
02:42:46,460 --> 02:42:48,500
So we will not turn away from you.

2588
02:42:49,480 --> 02:42:52,360
Revive us, and we will call on your name.

2589
02:42:53,060 --> 02:42:55,140
Turn us again, LORD God of Armies.

2590
02:42:55,600 --> 02:42:58,740
Cause your face to shine, and we will be
saved.

2591
02:43:00,080 --> 02:43:01,760
Psalm eighty-one.

2592
02:43:01,800 --> 02:43:03,900
Sing aloud to God, our strength!

2593
02:43:04,900 --> 02:43:07,640
Make a joyful shout to the God of Jacob!

2594
02:43:08,900 --> 02:43:14,620
Raise a song, and bring here the
tambourine, the pleasant lyre with the harp.

2595
02:43:14,740 --> 02:43:19,800
Blow the trumpet at the New Moon, at the
full moon, on our feast day.

2596
02:43:20,760 --> 02:43:25,320
For it is a statute for Israel, an
ordinance of the God of Jacob.

2597
02:43:26,020 --> 02:43:32,500
He appointed it in Joseph for a covenant,
when he went out over the land of Egypt, I

2598
02:43:32,540 --> 02:43:34,500
heard a language that I didn’t know.

2599
02:43:35,320 --> 02:43:37,640
“I removed his shoulder from the burden.

2600
02:43:38,520 --> 02:43:40,500
His hands were freed from the basket.

2601
02:43:40,540 --> 02:43:43,440
You called in trouble, and I delivered
you.

2602
02:43:44,340 --> 02:43:46,700
I answered you in the secret place of
thunder.

2603
02:43:47,400 --> 02:43:50,606
I tested you at the waters of Meribah.”

2604
02:43:50,646 --> 02:43:51,653
Selah.

2605
02:43:51,693 --> 02:43:57,600
“Hear, my people, and I will testify to
you, Israel, if you would listen to me!

2606
02:43:58,500 --> 02:44:03,760
There shall be no strange god in you,
neither shall you worship any foreign god.

2607
02:44:04,240 --> 02:44:08,800
I am the LORD, your God, who brought you
up out of the land of Egypt.

2608
02:44:09,280 --> 02:44:11,940
Open your mouth wide, and I will fill it.

2609
02:44:12,680 --> 02:44:15,160
But my people didn’t listen to my voice.

2610
02:44:16,560 --> 02:44:17,980
Israel desired none of me.

2611
02:44:18,261 --> 02:44:23,401
So I let them go after the stubbornness
of their hearts, that they might walk in their

2612
02:44:23,441 --> 02:44:24,861
own counsels.

2613
02:44:24,901 --> 02:44:30,181
Oh that my people would listen to me, that
Israel would walk in my ways!

2614
02:44:31,241 --> 02:44:35,741
I would soon subdue their enemies, and
turn my hand against their adversaries.

2615
02:44:36,661 --> 02:44:41,521
The haters of the LORD would cringe
before him, and their punishment would last forever.

2616
02:44:42,381 --> 02:44:45,741
But he would have also fed them with the
finest of the wheat.

2617
02:44:46,721 --> 02:44:49,501
I will satisfy you with honey out of the
rock.”

2618
02:44:50,661 --> 02:44:53,041
Psalm eighty-two.

2619
02:44:53,081 --> 02:44:54,781
God presides in the great assembly.

2620
02:44:55,761 --> 02:44:57,201
He judges amongst the gods.

2621
02:44:58,041 --> 02:45:02,401
“How long will you judge unjustly, and
show partiality to the wicked?”

2622
02:45:02,441 --> 02:45:04,441
Selah.

2623
02:45:04,481 --> 02:45:07,421
“Defend the weak, the poor, and the
fatherless.

2624
02:45:08,461 --> 02:45:10,501
Maintain the rights of the poor and
oppressed.

2625
02:45:10,541 --> 02:45:12,921
Rescue the weak and needy.

2626
02:45:13,741 --> 02:45:15,741
Deliver them out of the hand of the
wicked.”

2627
02:45:16,681 --> 02:45:19,121
They don’t know, neither do they
understand.

2628
02:45:20,101 --> 02:45:21,941
They walk back and forth in darkness.

2629
02:45:22,981 --> 02:45:25,321
All the foundations of the earth are
shaken.

2630
02:45:26,301 --> 02:45:30,721
I said, “You are gods, all of you are sons
of the Most High.

2631
02:45:31,501 --> 02:45:35,881
Nevertheless you shall die like men, and
fall like one of the rulers.”

2632
02:45:35,921 --> 02:45:41,041
Arise, God, judge the earth, for you
inherit all of the nations.

2633
02:45:41,861 --> 02:45:43,801
Psalm eighty-three.

2634
02:45:43,841 --> 02:45:45,481
God, don’t keep silent.

2635
02:45:46,361 --> 02:45:49,341
Don’t keep silent, and don’t be still,
God.

2636
02:45:50,121 --> 02:45:52,701
For, behold, your enemies are stirred up.

2637
02:45:53,401 --> 02:45:55,841
Those who hate you have lifted up their
heads.

2638
02:45:56,361 --> 02:45:58,641
They conspire with cunning against your
people.

2639
02:45:59,581 --> 02:46:01,481
They plot against your cherished ones.

2640
02:46:02,281 --> 02:46:08,501
“Come,” they say, “let’s destroy them as a
nation, that the name of Israel may be remembered

2641
02:46:08,541 --> 02:46:09,441
no more.”

2642
02:46:10,241 --> 02:46:12,921
For they have conspired together with one
mind.

2643
02:46:13,781 --> 02:46:15,781
They form an alliance against you.

2644
02:46:16,121 --> 02:46:23,081
The tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites;
Moab, and the Hagrites; Gebal, Ammon, and

2645
02:46:23,121 --> 02:46:29,681
Amalek; Philistia with the inhabitants of
Tyre; Assyria also is joined with

2646
02:46:29,721 --> 02:46:30,621
them.

2647
02:46:30,841 --> 02:46:32,621
They have helped the children of Lot.

2648
02:46:32,661 --> 02:46:33,561
Selah.

2649
02:46:34,646 --> 02:46:41,866
Do to them as you did to Midian, as to
Sisera, as to Jabin, at the river Kishon;

2650
02:46:41,906 --> 02:46:45,806
who perished at Endor, who became as dung
for the earth.

2651
02:46:46,306 --> 02:46:53,786
Make their nobles like Oreb and Zeeb, yes,
all their princes like Zebah and Zalmunna,

2652
02:46:53,826 --> 02:46:57,906
who said, “Let’s take possession of God’s
pasture lands.”

2653
02:46:58,766 --> 02:47:03,326
My God, make them like tumbleweed, like
chaff before the wind.

2654
02:47:04,116 --> 02:47:10,946
As the fire that burns the forest, as the
flame that sets the mountains on fire, so

2655
02:47:10,986 --> 02:47:14,946
pursue them with your tempest, and terrify
them with your storm.

2656
02:47:15,546 --> 02:47:19,906
Fill their faces with confusion, that they
may seek your name, LORD.

2657
02:47:20,526 --> 02:47:23,146
Let them be disappointed and dismayed
forever.

2658
02:47:23,986 --> 02:47:30,546
Yes, let them be confounded and perish;
that they may know that you alone, whose

2659
02:47:30,586 --> 02:47:34,406
name is the LORD, are the Most High over
all the earth.

2660
02:47:35,486 --> 02:47:36,946
Psalm eighty-four.

2661
02:47:36,986 --> 02:47:39,986
How lovely are your dwellings, LORD of
Armies!

2662
02:47:40,726 --> 02:47:44,606
My soul longs, and even faints for the
courts of the LORD.

2663
02:47:45,646 --> 02:47:49,026
My heart and my flesh cry out for the
living God.

2664
02:47:49,666 --> 02:47:56,506
Yes, the sparrow has found a home, and the
swallow a nest for herself, where she

2665
02:47:56,546 --> 02:48:02,386
may have her young, near your altars, LORD
of Armies, my King, and my God.

2666
02:48:03,006 --> 02:48:05,166
Blessed are those who dwell in your house.

2667
02:48:05,746 --> 02:48:07,366
They are always praising you.

2668
02:48:07,406 --> 02:48:09,486
Selah.

2669
02:48:09,526 --> 02:48:14,366
Blessed are those whose strength is in you,
who have set their hearts on a pilgrimage.

2670
02:48:14,886 --> 02:48:18,826
Passing through the valley of Weeping,
they make it a place of springs.

2671
02:48:19,426 --> 02:48:22,826
Yes, the autumn rain covers it with
blessings.

2672
02:48:23,686 --> 02:48:25,506
They go from strength to strength.

2673
02:48:26,406 --> 02:48:29,046
Every one of them appears before God in
Zion.

2674
02:48:30,146 --> 02:48:32,966
LORD, God of Armies, hear my prayer.

2675
02:48:34,006 --> 02:48:35,306
Listen, God of Jacob.

2676
02:48:35,346 --> 02:48:37,766
Selah.

2677
02:48:37,806 --> 02:48:41,146
Behold, God our shield, look at the face
of your anointed.

2678
02:48:41,746 --> 02:48:44,306
For a day in your courts is better than a
thousand.

2679
02:48:44,966 --> 02:48:50,306
I would rather be a doorkeeper in the house
of my God, than to dwell in the tents of

2680
02:48:50,346 --> 02:48:51,246
wickedness.

2681
02:48:51,686 --> 02:48:54,186
For the LORD God is a sun and a shield.

2682
02:48:54,986 --> 02:48:56,986
The LORD will give grace and glory.

2683
02:48:57,416 --> 02:49:01,756
He withholds no good thing from those who
walk blamelessly.

2684
02:49:02,336 --> 02:49:06,856
LORD of Armies, blessed is the man who
trusts in you.

2685
02:49:08,056 --> 02:49:11,036
Psalm eighty-five.

2686
02:49:11,076 --> 02:49:13,876
LORD, you have been favourable to your
land.

2687
02:49:14,396 --> 02:49:16,476
You have restored the fortunes of Jacob.

2688
02:49:17,536 --> 02:49:19,956
You have forgiven the iniquity of your
people.

2689
02:49:20,556 --> 02:49:22,436
You have covered all their sin.

2690
02:49:22,476 --> 02:49:24,376
Selah.

2691
02:49:24,416 --> 02:49:26,636
You have taken away all your wrath.

2692
02:49:27,516 --> 02:49:29,956
You have turned from the fierceness of
your anger.

2693
02:49:30,916 --> 02:49:36,816
Turn us, God of our salvation, and cause
your indignation towards us to cease.

2694
02:49:37,456 --> 02:49:39,076
Will you be angry with us forever?

2695
02:49:40,096 --> 02:49:42,656
Will you draw out your anger to all
generations?

2696
02:49:43,796 --> 02:49:47,796
Won’t you revive us again, that your
people may rejoice in you?

2697
02:49:48,496 --> 02:49:50,916
Show us your loving kindness, LORD.

2698
02:49:51,496 --> 02:49:52,776
Grant us your salvation.

2699
02:49:54,076 --> 02:50:00,276
I will hear what God, the LORD, will speak,
for he will speak peace to his people, his

2700
02:50:00,316 --> 02:50:03,496
saints; but let them not turn again to
folly.

2701
02:50:04,476 --> 02:50:09,916
Surely his salvation is near those who fear
him, that glory may dwell in our land.

2702
02:50:11,036 --> 02:50:12,596
Mercy and truth meet together.

2703
02:50:13,816 --> 02:50:16,176
Righteousness and peace have kissed each
other.

2704
02:50:16,896 --> 02:50:18,756
Truth springs out of the earth.

2705
02:50:19,136 --> 02:50:21,296
Righteousness has looked down from heaven.

2706
02:50:22,016 --> 02:50:25,216
Yes, the LORD will give that which is
good.

2707
02:50:25,896 --> 02:50:27,756
Our land will yield its increase.

2708
02:50:28,856 --> 02:50:33,056
Righteousness goes before him, And
prepares the way for his steps.

2709
02:50:34,476 --> 02:50:36,836
Psalm eighty-six.

2710
02:50:36,876 --> 02:50:40,776
Hear, LORD, and answer me, for I am poor
and needy.

2711
02:50:41,796 --> 02:50:44,556
Preserve my soul, for I am godly.

2712
02:50:45,416 --> 02:50:48,956
You, my God, save your servant who trusts
in you.

2713
02:50:49,536 --> 02:50:53,656
Be merciful to me, Lord, for I call to you
all day long.

2714
02:50:54,696 --> 02:51:00,756
Bring joy to the soul of your servant, for
to you, Lord, do I lift up my soul.

2715
02:51:01,216 --> 02:51:07,776
For you, Lord, are good, and ready to
forgive, abundant in loving kindness to all those

2716
02:51:07,816 --> 02:51:08,896
who call on you.

2717
02:51:10,096 --> 02:51:11,596
Hear, LORD, my prayer.

2718
02:51:12,216 --> 02:51:14,136
Listen to the voice of my petitions.

2719
02:51:15,276 --> 02:51:19,616
In the day of my trouble I will call on
you, for you will answer me.

2720
02:51:20,656 --> 02:51:26,136
There is no one like you amongst the gods,
Lord, nor any deeds like your deeds.

2721
02:51:26,581 --> 02:51:31,021
All nations you have made will come and
worship before you, Lord.

2722
02:51:32,081 --> 02:51:33,721
They shall glorify your name.

2723
02:51:34,821 --> 02:51:37,761
For you are great, and do wondrous things.

2724
02:51:38,621 --> 02:51:39,821
You are God alone.

2725
02:51:41,101 --> 02:51:42,481
Teach me your way, LORD.

2726
02:51:42,961 --> 02:51:44,381
I will walk in your truth.

2727
02:51:45,441 --> 02:51:48,061
Make my heart undivided to fear your name.

2728
02:51:48,701 --> 02:51:52,021
I will praise you, Lord my God, with my
whole heart.

2729
02:51:52,901 --> 02:51:56,441
I will glorify your name forever more.

2730
02:51:56,481 --> 02:51:59,261
For your loving kindness is great towards
me.

2731
02:52:00,201 --> 02:52:04,201
You have delivered my soul from the lowest
Sheol.

2732
02:52:04,241 --> 02:52:07,401
God, the proud have risen up against me.

2733
02:52:07,941 --> 02:52:13,801
A company of violent men have sought after
my soul, and they don’t hold regard for you

2734
02:52:13,841 --> 02:52:14,741
before them.

2735
02:52:15,381 --> 02:52:22,021
But you, Lord, are a merciful and gracious
God, slow to anger, and abundant in loving

2736
02:52:22,061 --> 02:52:23,201
kindness and truth.

2737
02:52:23,241 --> 02:52:25,941
Turn to me, and have mercy on me!

2738
02:52:26,781 --> 02:52:28,701
Give your strength to your servant.

2739
02:52:29,461 --> 02:52:30,801
Save the son of your servant.

2740
02:52:31,941 --> 02:52:38,281
Show me a sign of your goodness, that those
who hate me may see it, and be shamed, because

2741
02:52:38,321 --> 02:52:41,581
you, LORD, have helped me, and comforted
me.

2742
02:52:42,801 --> 02:52:44,421
Psalm eighty-seven.

2743
02:52:44,461 --> 02:52:46,681
His foundation is in the holy mountains.

2744
02:52:47,541 --> 02:52:51,781
The LORD loves the gates of Zion more than
all the dwellings of Jacob.

2745
02:52:52,641 --> 02:52:55,921
Glorious things are spoken about you, city
of God.

2746
02:52:55,961 --> 02:52:58,501
Selah.

2747
02:52:58,541 --> 02:53:02,841
I will record Rahab and Babylon amongst
those who acknowledge me.

2748
02:53:03,701 --> 02:53:10,321
Behold, Philistia, Tyre, and also
Ethiopia: “This one was born there.”

2749
02:53:10,821 --> 02:53:17,341
Yes, of Zion it will be said, “This one
and that one was born in her;” the Most High

2750
02:53:17,381 --> 02:53:19,241
himself will establish her.

2751
02:53:20,341 --> 02:53:25,861
The LORD will count, when he writes up the
peoples, “This one was born there.”

2752
02:53:25,901 --> 02:53:28,321
Selah.

2753
02:53:28,361 --> 02:53:33,881
Those who sing as well as those who dance
say, “All my springs are in you.”

2754
02:53:35,001 --> 02:53:36,841
Psalm eighty-eight.

2755
02:53:36,881 --> 02:53:42,261
LORD, the God of my salvation, I have
cried day and night before you.

2756
02:53:43,041 --> 02:53:45,381
Let my prayer enter into your presence.

2757
02:53:46,181 --> 02:53:47,721
Turn your ear to my cry.

2758
02:53:48,761 --> 02:53:50,541
For my soul is full of troubles.

2759
02:53:51,561 --> 02:53:53,541
My life draws near to Sheol.

2760
02:53:54,021 --> 02:53:57,061
I am counted amongst those who go down
into the pit.

2761
02:53:57,457 --> 02:54:04,297
I am like a man who has no help, set apart
amongst the dead, like the slain who

2762
02:54:04,337 --> 02:54:07,737
lie in the grave, whom you remember no
more.

2763
02:54:08,337 --> 02:54:10,357
They are cut off from your hand.

2764
02:54:11,197 --> 02:54:14,997
You have laid me in the lowest pit, in the
darkest depths.

2765
02:54:16,017 --> 02:54:18,077
Your wrath lies heavily on me.

2766
02:54:18,457 --> 02:54:20,617
You have afflicted me with all your waves.

2767
02:54:20,657 --> 02:54:22,617
Selah.

2768
02:54:22,657 --> 02:54:24,657
You have taken my friends from me.

2769
02:54:25,337 --> 02:54:27,637
You have made me an abomination to them.

2770
02:54:28,477 --> 02:54:31,357
I am confined, and I can’t escape.

2771
02:54:32,417 --> 02:54:34,157
My eyes are dim from grief.

2772
02:54:34,777 --> 02:54:36,497
I have called on you daily, LORD.

2773
02:54:37,337 --> 02:54:39,397
I have spread out my hands to you.

2774
02:54:40,277 --> 02:54:42,217
Do you show wonders to the dead?

2775
02:54:43,057 --> 02:54:45,917
Do the departed spirits rise up and praise
you?

2776
02:54:45,957 --> 02:54:47,717
Selah.

2777
02:54:47,757 --> 02:54:50,317
Is your loving kindness declared in the
grave?

2778
02:54:50,997 --> 02:54:52,677
Or your faithfulness in Destruction?

2779
02:54:53,917 --> 02:54:56,037
Are your wonders made known in the dark?

2780
02:54:56,677 --> 02:54:59,257
Or your righteousness in the land of
forgetfulness?

2781
02:55:00,317 --> 02:55:02,217
But to you, LORD, I have cried.

2782
02:55:02,257 --> 02:55:05,417
In the morning, my prayer comes before
you.

2783
02:55:06,277 --> 02:55:08,717
LORD, why do you reject my soul?

2784
02:55:09,377 --> 02:55:11,217
Why do you hide your face from me?

2785
02:55:12,057 --> 02:55:15,337
I am afflicted and ready to die from my
youth up.

2786
02:55:16,257 --> 02:55:19,017
While I suffer your terrors, I am
distracted.

2787
02:55:20,377 --> 02:55:22,517
Your fierce wrath has gone over me.

2788
02:55:23,277 --> 02:55:25,077
Your terrors have cut me off.

2789
02:55:25,537 --> 02:55:28,377
They came around me like water all day
long.

2790
02:55:29,177 --> 02:55:30,757
They completely engulfed me.

2791
02:55:31,297 --> 02:55:35,897
You have put lover and friend far from me,
and my friends into darkness.

2792
02:55:37,077 --> 02:55:39,637
Psalm eighty-nine.

2793
02:55:39,677 --> 02:55:42,577
I will sing of the loving kindness of the
LORD forever.

2794
02:55:43,277 --> 02:55:47,437
With my mouth, I will make known your
faithfulness to all generations.

2795
02:55:48,917 --> 02:55:52,217
I indeed declare, “Love stands firm
forever.

2796
02:55:53,077 --> 02:55:54,457
You established the heavens.

2797
02:55:55,177 --> 02:55:56,717
Your faithfulness is in them.”

2798
02:55:57,697 --> 02:56:04,357
“I have made a covenant with my chosen
one, I have sworn to David, my servant, ‘I

2799
02:56:04,397 --> 02:56:09,757
will establish your offspring forever, and
build up your throne to all generations.’”

2800
02:56:09,797 --> 02:56:12,257
Selah.

2801
02:56:12,297 --> 02:56:17,977
The heavens will praise your wonders, LORD,
your faithfulness also in the assembly of

2802
02:56:18,017 --> 02:56:18,917
the holy ones.

2803
02:56:19,717 --> 02:56:22,377
For who in the skies can be compared to
the LORD?

2804
02:56:22,750 --> 02:56:29,030
Who amongst the sons of the heavenly beings is
like the LORD, a very awesome God in the

2805
02:56:29,070 --> 02:56:34,450
council of the holy ones, to be feared
above all those who are around him?

2806
02:56:35,650 --> 02:56:40,050
LORD, God of Armies, who is a mighty one,
like you?

2807
02:56:40,430 --> 02:56:43,370
The LORD, your faithfulness is around you.

2808
02:56:44,250 --> 02:56:46,190
You rule the pride of the sea.

2809
02:56:46,630 --> 02:56:49,550
When its waves rise up, you calm them.

2810
02:56:50,450 --> 02:56:54,110
You have broken Rahab in pieces, like one
of the slain.

2811
02:56:54,990 --> 02:56:57,890
You have scattered your enemies with your
mighty arm.

2812
02:56:58,730 --> 02:56:59,790
The heavens are yours.

2813
02:57:00,470 --> 02:57:04,230
The earth also is yours, the world and its
fullness.

2814
02:57:04,890 --> 02:57:06,150
You have founded them.

2815
02:57:06,890 --> 02:57:09,390
You have created the north and the south.

2816
02:57:09,950 --> 02:57:12,450
Tabor and Hermon rejoice in your name.

2817
02:57:13,310 --> 02:57:14,450
You have a mighty arm.

2818
02:57:15,190 --> 02:57:18,550
Your hand is strong, and your right hand
is exalted.

2819
02:57:19,890 --> 02:57:23,230
Righteousness and justice are the
foundation of your throne.

2820
02:57:24,110 --> 02:57:27,130
Loving kindness and truth go before your
face.

2821
02:57:28,010 --> 02:57:30,770
Blessed are the people who learn to
acclaim you.

2822
02:57:31,250 --> 02:57:33,510
They walk in the light of your presence,
LORD.

2823
02:57:34,450 --> 02:57:36,690
In your name they rejoice all day.

2824
02:57:37,510 --> 02:57:39,850
In your righteousness, they are exalted.

2825
02:57:41,110 --> 02:57:43,010
For you are the glory of their strength.

2826
02:57:43,970 --> 02:57:46,630
In your favour, our horn will be exalted.

2827
02:57:47,230 --> 02:57:51,990
For our shield belongs to the LORD, our
king to the Holy One of Israel.

2828
02:57:52,830 --> 02:57:58,650
Then you spoke in vision to your saints,
and said, “I have given strength to the warrior.

2829
02:57:59,370 --> 02:58:01,970
I have exalted a young man from the
people.

2830
02:58:02,630 --> 02:58:04,770
I have found David, my servant.

2831
02:58:05,450 --> 02:58:10,630
I have anointed him with my holy oil, with
whom my hand shall be established.

2832
02:58:11,790 --> 02:58:13,890
My arm will also strengthen him.

2833
02:58:14,490 --> 02:58:16,090
No enemy will tax him.

2834
02:58:16,770 --> 02:58:18,770
No wicked man will oppress him.

2835
02:58:19,510 --> 02:58:24,850
I will beat down his adversaries before
him, and strike those who hate him.

2836
02:58:25,790 --> 02:58:29,630
But my faithfulness and my loving kindness
will be with him.

2837
02:58:30,290 --> 02:58:33,090
In my name, his horn will be exalted.

2838
02:58:34,050 --> 02:58:38,910
I will set his hand also on the sea, and
his right hand on the rivers.

2839
02:58:40,050 --> 02:58:46,230
He will call to me, ‘You are my Father, my
God, and the rock of my salvation!’

2840
02:58:46,686 --> 02:58:52,306
I will also appoint him my firstborn, the
highest of the kings of the earth.

2841
02:58:53,326 --> 02:58:57,546
I will keep my loving kindness for him
forever more.

2842
02:58:57,586 --> 02:59:00,146
My covenant will stand firm with him.

2843
02:59:00,906 --> 02:59:07,366
I will also make his offspring endure forever,
and his throne as the days of heaven.

2844
02:59:07,826 --> 02:59:14,386
If his children forsake my law, and don’t
walk in my ordinances; if they break my

2845
02:59:14,426 --> 02:59:20,426
statutes, and don’t keep my commandments;
then I will punish their sin with the rod,

2846
02:59:21,146 --> 02:59:22,546
and their iniquity with stripes.

2847
02:59:23,206 --> 02:59:28,766
But I will not completely take my
loving kindness from him, nor allow my faithfulness

2848
02:59:28,806 --> 02:59:29,706
to fail.

2849
02:59:30,126 --> 02:59:34,546
I will not break my covenant, nor alter
what my lips have uttered.

2850
02:59:35,546 --> 02:59:39,806
Once I have sworn by my holiness, I will
not lie to David.

2851
02:59:40,846 --> 02:59:45,886
His offspring will endure forever, his
throne like the sun before me.

2852
02:59:46,186 --> 02:59:50,826
It will be established forever like the
moon, the faithful witness in the sky.”

2853
02:59:50,866 --> 02:59:52,986
Selah.

2854
02:59:53,026 --> 02:59:55,046
But you have rejected and spurned.

2855
02:59:56,006 --> 02:59:57,986
You have been angry with your anointed.

2856
02:59:58,966 --> 03:00:01,386
You have renounced the covenant of your
servant.

2857
03:00:02,406 --> 03:00:04,586
You have defiled his crown in the dust.

2858
03:00:05,466 --> 03:00:07,606
You have broken down all his hedges.

2859
03:00:08,366 --> 03:00:10,426
You have brought his strongholds to ruin.

2860
03:00:11,086 --> 03:00:13,706
All who pass by the way rob him.

2861
03:00:14,306 --> 03:00:17,486
He has become a reproach to his
neighbours.

2862
03:00:17,526 --> 03:00:20,126
You have exalted the right hand of his
adversaries.

2863
03:00:21,226 --> 03:00:23,366
You have made all of his enemies rejoice.

2864
03:00:24,466 --> 03:00:30,126
Yes, you turn back the edge of his sword,
and haven’t supported him in battle.

2865
03:00:30,566 --> 03:00:34,726
You have ended his splendour, and thrown
his throne down to the ground.

2866
03:00:35,446 --> 03:00:37,446
You have shortened the days of his youth.

2867
03:00:38,426 --> 03:00:39,806
You have covered him with shame.

2868
03:00:39,846 --> 03:00:42,226
Selah.

2869
03:00:42,266 --> 03:00:43,586
How long, LORD?

2870
03:00:44,366 --> 03:00:46,046
Will you hide yourself forever?

2871
03:00:47,086 --> 03:00:48,966
Will your wrath burn like fire?

2872
03:00:49,886 --> 03:00:55,566
Remember how short my time is, for what
vanity you have created all the children of men!

2873
03:00:56,206 --> 03:01:02,126
What man is he who shall live and not see
death, who shall deliver his soul from the

2874
03:01:02,166 --> 03:01:02,766
power of Sheol?

2875
03:01:02,806 --> 03:01:03,706
Selah.

2876
03:01:05,314 --> 03:01:12,254
Lord, where are your former loving kindnesses,
which you swore to David in your faithfulness?

2877
03:01:12,974 --> 03:01:19,474
Remember, Lord, the reproach of your servants,
how I bear in my heart the taunts

2878
03:01:19,514 --> 03:01:25,654
of all the mighty peoples, With which your
enemies have mocked, LORD, with which they

2879
03:01:25,694 --> 03:01:28,394
have mocked the footsteps of your anointed
one.

2880
03:01:28,854 --> 03:01:31,334
Blessed be the LORD forever more.

2881
03:01:31,374 --> 03:01:32,994
Amen, and Amen.

2882
03:01:33,634 --> 03:01:35,694
First Peter, chapter one.

2883
03:01:35,734 --> 03:01:41,754
Peter, an apostle of Jesus Christ, to the
chosen ones who are living as foreigners in

2884
03:01:41,794 --> 03:01:48,874
the Dispersion in Pontus, Galatia,
Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia, according

2885
03:01:48,914 --> 03:01:54,974
to the foreknowledge of God the Father, in
sanctification of the Spirit, that you may

2886
03:01:55,014 --> 03:02:01,764
obey Jesus Christ and be sprinkled with his
blood: Grace to you and peace be multiplied.

2887
03:02:03,004 --> 03:02:09,084
Blessed be the God and Father of our
Lord Jesus Christ, who according to his great mercy

2888
03:02:09,124 --> 03:02:14,824
caused us to be born again to a
living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ

2889
03:02:14,864 --> 03:02:21,484
from the dead, to an incorruptible
and undefiled inheritance that doesn’t fade away,

2890
03:02:21,524 --> 03:02:28,004
reserved in Heaven for you, who by the
power of God are guarded through faith for a

2891
03:02:28,044 --> 03:02:31,064
salvation ready to be revealed in the last
time.

2892
03:02:32,184 --> 03:02:38,244
In this you greatly rejoice, though now for
a little while, if need be, you have been

2893
03:02:38,284 --> 03:02:43,744
grieved in various trials, that the proof
of your faith, which is more precious than

2894
03:02:43,784 --> 03:02:50,384
gold that perishes, even though it is
tested by fire, may be found to result

2895
03:02:50,424 --> 03:02:57,144
in praise, glory, and honour at the
revelation of Jesus Christ— whom, not

2896
03:02:57,184 --> 03:02:58,784
having known, you love.

2897
03:02:59,544 --> 03:03:06,524
In him, though now you don’t see him,
yet believing, you rejoice greatly with joy that

2898
03:03:06,564 --> 03:03:13,564
is unspeakable and full of glory, receiving
the result of your faith, the salvation of

2899
03:03:13,604 --> 03:03:14,004
your souls.

2900
03:03:14,044 --> 03:03:19,104
Concerning this salvation, the prophets
sought and searched diligently.

2901
03:03:19,693 --> 03:03:25,633
They prophesied of the grace that would come
to you, searching for who or what kind of

2902
03:03:25,673 --> 03:03:31,993
time the Spirit of Christ which was in
them pointed to when he predicted the sufferings

2903
03:03:32,033 --> 03:03:35,053
of Christ and the glories that would
follow them.

2904
03:03:35,633 --> 03:03:42,233
To them it was revealed that they served
not themselves, but you, in these things, which

2905
03:03:42,273 --> 03:03:46,833
now have been announced to you through those
who preached the Good News to you by the

2906
03:03:46,873 --> 03:03:52,393
Holy Spirit sent out from heaven; which
things angels desire to look into.

2907
03:03:52,733 --> 03:03:55,073
Therefore prepare your minds for action.

2908
03:03:55,793 --> 03:04:01,293
Be sober, and set your hope fully on the
grace that will be brought to you at the revelation

2909
03:04:01,333 --> 03:04:07,873
of Jesus Christ— as children of
obedience, not conforming yourselves according to your

2910
03:04:07,913 --> 03:04:15,753
former lusts

2911
03:04:15,793 --> 03:04:16,093
as in your ignorance, but just as he who
called you is holy, you yourselves also be holy

2912
03:04:16,133 --> 03:04:22,193
in all of your behaviour, because it is
written, “You shall be holy, for I am holy.”

2913
03:04:23,373 --> 03:04:29,053
If you call on him as Father, who
without respect of persons judges according to each

2914
03:04:29,093 --> 03:04:35,293
man’s work, pass the time of your
living as foreigners here in reverent fear, knowing

2915
03:04:35,333 --> 03:04:41,793
that you were redeemed, not with corruptible
things like silver or gold, from the useless

2916
03:04:41,833 --> 03:04:48,233
way of life handed down from your fathers,
but with precious blood, as of a lamb without

2917
03:04:48,273 --> 03:04:54,233
blemish or spot, the blood of Christ, who
was foreknown indeed before the foundation

2918
03:04:54,273 --> 03:05:00,893
of the world, but was revealed in this
last age for your sake, who through him are

2919
03:05:00,933 --> 03:05:07,413
believers in God, who raised him from the
dead and gave him glory, so that your

2920
03:05:07,453 --> 03:05:09,573
faith and hope might be in God.

2921
03:05:09,932 --> 03:05:15,452
Seeing you have purified your souls in
your obedience to the truth through the Spirit

2922
03:05:15,492 --> 03:05:22,052
in sincere brotherly affection, love one
another from the heart fervently, having

2923
03:05:22,092 --> 03:05:28,692
been born again, not of corruptible seed,
but of incorruptible, through the word of God,

2924
03:05:28,732 --> 03:05:31,172
which lives and remains forever.

2925
03:05:32,133 --> 03:05:38,672
For, “All flesh is like grass, and all of
man’s glory like the flower in the grass.

2926
03:05:38,713 --> 03:05:45,332
The grass withers, and its flower falls;
but the Lord’s word endures forever.”

2927
03:05:46,432 --> 03:05:49,912
This is the word of Good News which was
preached to you.

2928
03:05:50,793 --> 03:05:52,932
First Peter, chapter two.

2929
03:05:52,973 --> 03:05:59,632
Putting away therefore all wickedness, all
deceit, hypocrisies, envies, and all

2930
03:05:59,672 --> 03:06:06,212
evil speaking, as newborn babies, long for
the pure spiritual milk, that with

2931
03:06:06,252 --> 03:06:10,553
it you may grow, if indeed you have tasted
that the Lord is gracious.

2932
03:06:11,293 --> 03:06:18,473
Come to him, a living stone, rejected
indeed by men, but chosen by God, precious.

2933
03:06:19,652 --> 03:06:25,932
You also as living stones are built up
as a spiritual house, to be a holy priesthood,

2934
03:06:26,633 --> 03:06:32,033
to offer up spiritual sacrifices,
acceptable to God through Jesus Christ.

2935
03:06:32,613 --> 03:06:39,912
Because it is contained in Scripture, “Behold,
I lay in Zion a chief cornerstone, chosen

2936
03:06:39,953 --> 03:06:40,852
and precious.

2937
03:06:41,793 --> 03:06:44,572
He who believes in him will not be
disappointed.”

2938
03:06:45,332 --> 03:06:51,472
For you who believe therefore is the
honour, but for those who are disobedient, “The

2939
03:06:51,512 --> 03:06:57,852
stone which the builders rejected has
become the chief cornerstone,” and, “a stumbling

2940
03:06:57,892 --> 03:06:59,832
stone and a rock of offence.”

2941
03:06:59,873 --> 03:07:05,613
For they stumble at the word, being
disobedient, to which also they were appointed.

2942
03:07:06,312 --> 03:07:12,792
But you are a chosen race, a royal
priesthood, a holy nation, a people for God’s

2943
03:07:12,832 --> 03:07:18,292
own possession, that you may proclaim the excellence
of him who called you out of darkness

2944
03:07:18,332 --> 03:07:20,373
into his marvellous light.

2945
03:07:20,873 --> 03:07:27,772
In the past, you were not a people, but
now are God’s people, who had not obtained mercy,

2946
03:07:27,812 --> 03:07:29,973
but now have obtained mercy.

2947
03:07:30,479 --> 03:07:37,219
Beloved, I beg you as foreigners and
pilgrims to abstain from fleshly lusts

2948
03:07:37,259 --> 03:07:43,659
which war against the soul, having good
behaviour amongst the nations, so in that of

2949
03:07:43,699 --> 03:07:50,139
which they speak against you as evildoers, they
may see your good works and glorify God

2950
03:07:50,179 --> 03:07:51,399
in the day of visitation.

2951
03:07:52,179 --> 03:07:58,579
Therefore subject yourselves to every ordinance of
man for the Lord’s sake: whether to

2952
03:07:58,619 --> 03:08:05,219
the king, as supreme, or to governors, as
sent by him for vengeance on evildoers

2953
03:08:05,259 --> 03:08:07,679
and for praise to those who do well.

2954
03:08:08,259 --> 03:08:13,659
For this is the will of God, that
by well-doing you should put to silence the ignorance

2955
03:08:13,699 --> 03:08:14,839
of foolish men.

2956
03:08:15,559 --> 03:08:22,359
Live as free people, yet not using your
freedom for a cloak of wickedness, but as bondservants

2957
03:08:22,399 --> 03:08:22,999
of God.

2958
03:08:23,039 --> 03:08:24,359
Honour all men.

2959
03:08:24,799 --> 03:08:25,839
Love the brotherhood.

2960
03:08:26,379 --> 03:08:27,059
Fear God.

2961
03:08:27,099 --> 03:08:28,619
Honour the king.

2962
03:08:29,259 --> 03:08:35,859
Servants, be in subjection to your masters
with all respect, not only to the good

2963
03:08:35,899 --> 03:08:38,379
and gentle, but also to the wicked.

2964
03:08:39,259 --> 03:08:45,439
For it is commendable if someone
endures pain, suffering unjustly, because of conscience

2965
03:08:45,479 --> 03:08:46,379
towards God.

2966
03:08:46,739 --> 03:08:51,979
For what glory is it if, when you sin, you
patiently endure beating?

2967
03:08:52,719 --> 03:08:58,499
But if when you do well, you
patiently endure suffering, this is commendable with God.

2968
03:08:59,319 --> 03:09:05,099
For you were called to this, because Christ
also suffered for us, leaving you an example,

2969
03:09:05,139 --> 03:09:11,359
that you should follow his steps, who didn’t
sin, “neither was deceit found in his mouth.”

2970
03:09:12,119 --> 03:09:14,439
When he was cursed, he didn’t curse back.

2971
03:09:15,219 --> 03:09:20,879
When he suffered, he didn’t threaten, but
committed himself to him who judges righteously.

2972
03:09:21,839 --> 03:09:28,959
He himself bore our sins in his body on
the tree, that we, having died to sins, might

2973
03:09:28,999 --> 03:09:30,199
live to righteousness.

2974
03:09:31,419 --> 03:09:33,099
You were healed by his wounds.

2975
03:09:33,839 --> 03:09:39,979
For you were going astray like sheep; but
now you have returned to the Shepherd and Overseer

2976
03:09:40,019 --> 03:09:40,919
of your souls.

2977
03:09:42,019 --> 03:09:42,979
First Peter, chapter three.

2978
03:09:43,778 --> 03:09:50,498
In the same way, wives, be in subjection
to your own husbands, so that, even

2979
03:09:50,538 --> 03:09:56,738
if any don’t obey the Word, they may be
won by the behaviour of their wives without a

2980
03:09:56,778 --> 03:10:00,138
word, seeing your pure behaviour in fear.

2981
03:10:00,738 --> 03:10:06,098
Let your beauty come not from the outward
adorning of braiding your hair, and of wearing

2982
03:10:06,138 --> 03:10:12,378
gold ornaments or of putting on fine clothing,
but from the hidden person of the heart,

2983
03:10:12,918 --> 03:10:19,098
in the incorruptible adornment of a gentle
and quiet spirit, which is very precious in

2984
03:10:19,138 --> 03:10:20,038
God’s sight.

2985
03:10:20,458 --> 03:10:26,318
For this is how in the past the holy women
who hoped in God also adorned themselves,

2986
03:10:27,238 --> 03:10:29,318
being in subjection to their own husbands.

2987
03:10:30,598 --> 03:10:37,118
So Sarah obeyed Abraham, calling him lord,
whose children you now are if you do well

2988
03:10:37,158 --> 03:10:39,838
and are not put in fear by any terror.

2989
03:10:40,298 --> 03:10:46,898
You husbands, in the same way, live
with your wives according to knowledge, giving honour

2990
03:10:46,938 --> 03:10:53,038
to the woman as to the weaker vessel, as
also being joint heirs of the grace of life,

2991
03:10:53,938 --> 03:10:55,638
that your prayers may not be hindered.

2992
03:10:56,458 --> 03:11:03,798
Finally, all of you be
like-minded, compassionate, loving as brothers, tenderhearted,

2993
03:11:03,838 --> 03:11:10,798
courteous, not rendering evil for evil or
insult for insult; but instead blessing,

2994
03:11:11,518 --> 03:11:15,798
knowing that you were called to this, that
you may inherit a blessing.

2995
03:11:16,438 --> 03:11:23,078
For, “He who would love life and see good
days, let him keep his tongue from evil

2996
03:11:23,118 --> 03:11:26,378
and his lips from speaking deceit.

2997
03:11:26,418 --> 03:11:29,058
Let him turn away from evil and do good.

2998
03:11:29,858 --> 03:11:31,978
Let him seek peace and pursue it.

2999
03:11:32,798 --> 03:11:38,198
For the eyes of the Lord are on the
righteous, and his ears open to their prayer; but

3000
03:11:38,238 --> 03:11:41,118
the face of the Lord is against those who
do evil.”

3001
03:11:41,958 --> 03:11:46,758
Now who will harm you if you become
imitators of that which is good?

3002
03:11:47,198 --> 03:11:54,458
But even if you should suffer for
righteousness’ sake, you are

3003
03:11:54,498 --> 03:11:54,798
blessed.

3004
03:11:54,838 --> 03:11:55,598
“Don’t fear what they fear, neither be
troubled.”

3005
03:11:55,638 --> 03:11:57,978
But sanctify the Lord God in your hearts.

3006
03:11:58,440 --> 03:12:03,900
Always be ready to give an answer to
everyone who asks you a reason concerning the hope

3007
03:12:03,940 --> 03:12:09,060
that is in you, with humility and fear,
having a good conscience.

3008
03:12:09,820 --> 03:12:16,540
Thus, while you are spoken against as
evildoers, they may be disappointed who curse your

3009
03:12:16,580 --> 03:12:18,120
good way of life in Christ.

3010
03:12:18,800 --> 03:12:25,000
For it is better, if it is God’s will,
that you suffer for doing what is right than for

3011
03:12:25,040 --> 03:12:25,940
doing evil.

3012
03:12:26,440 --> 03:12:32,920
Because Christ also suffered for sins
once, the righteous for the unrighteous, that

3013
03:12:32,960 --> 03:12:38,940
he might bring you to God, being put to
death in the flesh, but made alive in the Spirit,

3014
03:12:39,340 --> 03:12:45,200
in whom he also went and preached to
the spirits in prison, who before were disobedient

3015
03:12:45,700 --> 03:12:50,380
when God waited patiently in the days of
Noah while the ship was being built.

3016
03:12:51,260 --> 03:12:56,700
In it, few, that is, eight souls, were
saved through water.

3017
03:12:57,620 --> 03:13:04,080
This is a symbol of baptism, which now
saves you—not the putting away of the filth of

3018
03:13:04,120 --> 03:13:10,040
the flesh, but the answer of a
good conscience towards God—through the resurrection of

3019
03:13:10,080 --> 03:13:16,600
Jesus Christ, who is at the right hand of
God, having gone into heaven, angels and

3020
03:13:16,640 --> 03:13:19,580
authorities and powers being made subject
to him.

3021
03:13:19,620 --> 03:13:22,740
First Peter, chapter four.

3022
03:13:22,780 --> 03:13:29,180
Therefore, since Christ suffered for us in
the flesh, arm yourselves also with the same

3023
03:13:29,220 --> 03:13:35,780
mind; for he who has suffered in the flesh
has ceased from sin, that you no longer should

3024
03:13:35,820 --> 03:13:41,040
live the rest of your time in the flesh for
the lusts of men, but for the will of God.

3025
03:13:41,620 --> 03:13:47,560
For we have spent enough of our past
time doing the desire of the Gentiles, and having

3026
03:13:47,600 --> 03:13:54,660
walked in lewdness, lusts, drunken
binges, orgies, carousings, and abominable idolatries.

3027
03:13:55,640 --> 03:14:01,660
They think it is strange that you don’t run
with them into the same excess of riot, speaking

3028
03:14:01,700 --> 03:14:02,620
evil of you.

3029
03:14:03,160 --> 03:14:07,220
They will give account to him who is ready
to judge the living and the dead.

3030
03:14:07,588 --> 03:14:13,568
For to this end the Good News was preached
even to the dead, that they might be judged

3031
03:14:13,608 --> 03:14:18,568
indeed as men in the flesh, but live as to
God in the spirit.

3032
03:14:19,728 --> 03:14:21,608
But the end of all things is near.

3033
03:14:22,568 --> 03:14:27,928
Therefore be of sound mind,
self-controlled, and sober in prayer.

3034
03:14:28,608 --> 03:14:34,808
And above all things be earnest in your
love amongst yourselves, for love covers a multitude

3035
03:14:34,848 --> 03:14:35,748
of sins.

3036
03:14:36,708 --> 03:14:39,408
Be hospitable to one another without
grumbling.

3037
03:14:39,768 --> 03:14:46,408
As each has received a gift, employ it in
serving one another, as good managers of

3038
03:14:46,448 --> 03:14:48,808
the grace of God in its various forms.

3039
03:14:49,608 --> 03:14:54,048
If anyone speaks, let it be as it were the
very words of God.

3040
03:14:54,888 --> 03:15:01,528
If anyone serves, let it be as of
the strength which God supplies, that in all things

3041
03:15:01,568 --> 03:15:07,428
God may be glorified through Jesus Christ,
to whom belong the glory and the dominion

3042
03:15:07,468 --> 03:15:08,828
forever and ever.

3043
03:15:09,268 --> 03:15:10,168
Amen.

3044
03:15:10,368 --> 03:15:15,948
Beloved, don’t be astonished at the fiery
trial which has come upon you to test you,

3045
03:15:16,408 --> 03:15:18,708
as though a strange thing happened to you.

3046
03:15:19,348 --> 03:15:25,108
But because you are partakers of
Christ’s sufferings, rejoice, that at the revelation

3047
03:15:25,148 --> 03:15:28,988
of his glory you also may rejoice with
exceeding joy.

3048
03:15:29,768 --> 03:15:35,188
If you are insulted for the name of
Christ, you are blessed, because the Spirit of glory

3049
03:15:35,228 --> 03:15:37,308
and of God rests on you.

3050
03:15:38,168 --> 03:15:42,588
On their part he is blasphemed, but on
your part he is glorified.

3051
03:15:42,988 --> 03:15:49,308
But let none of you suffer as a murderer, or
a thief, or an evil doer, or a meddler in

3052
03:15:49,348 --> 03:15:50,308
other men’s matters.

3053
03:15:51,108 --> 03:15:57,208
But if one of you suffers for being a
Christian, let him not be ashamed; but let him

3054
03:15:57,248 --> 03:15:59,088
glorify God in this matter.

3055
03:15:59,508 --> 03:16:04,148
For the time has come for judgement to
begin with the household of God.

3056
03:16:04,948 --> 03:16:10,588
If it begins first with us, what will happen
to those who don’t obey the Good News of

3057
03:16:10,628 --> 03:16:11,528
God?

3058
03:16:11,588 --> 03:16:16,968
“If it is hard for the righteous to be
saved, what will happen to the ungodly and the

3059
03:16:17,008 --> 03:16:17,443
sinner?”

3060
03:16:17,483 --> 03:16:24,063
Therefore let them also who suffer according to
the will of God in doing good entrust

3061
03:16:24,103 --> 03:16:27,623
their souls to him, as to a faithful
Creator.

3062
03:16:27,663 --> 03:16:31,403
First Peter, chapter five.

3063
03:16:31,443 --> 03:16:37,903
Therefore I exhort the elders amongst you, as
a fellow elder and a witness of the sufferings

3064
03:16:37,943 --> 03:16:44,463
of Christ, and who will also share in the
glory that will be revealed: shepherd

3065
03:16:44,503 --> 03:16:51,363
the flock of God which is amongst
you, exercising the oversight, not under compulsion,

3066
03:16:52,083 --> 03:16:58,703
but voluntarily; not for dishonest gain,
but willingly; not as lording it over

3067
03:16:58,743 --> 03:17:03,583
those entrusted to you, but making
yourselves examples to the flock.

3068
03:17:04,323 --> 03:17:10,323
When the chief Shepherd is revealed, you
will receive the crown of glory that doesn’t

3069
03:17:10,363 --> 03:17:11,263
fade away.

3070
03:17:11,963 --> 03:17:15,823
Likewise, you younger ones, be subject to
the elder.

3071
03:17:16,703 --> 03:17:23,103
Yes, all of you clothe yourselves with
humility and subject yourselves to one another;

3072
03:17:23,823 --> 03:17:28,343
for “God resists the proud, but gives
grace to the humble.”

3073
03:17:29,143 --> 03:17:34,923
Humble yourselves therefore under the mighty hand of
God, that he may exalt you in due

3074
03:17:34,963 --> 03:17:40,283
time, casting all your worries on him,
because he cares for you.

3075
03:17:40,323 --> 03:17:44,343
Be sober and self-controlled.

3076
03:17:44,383 --> 03:17:45,283
Be watchful.

3077
03:17:45,383 --> 03:17:51,943
Your adversary, the devil, walks around
like a roaring lion, seeking whom he

3078
03:17:51,983 --> 03:17:52,883
may devour.

3079
03:17:53,623 --> 03:17:59,003
Withstand him steadfast in your faith, knowing
that your brothers who are in the world

3080
03:17:59,043 --> 03:18:01,863
are undergoing the same sufferings.

3081
03:18:02,743 --> 03:18:09,663
But may the God of all grace, who called
you to his eternal glory by Christ Jesus, after

3082
03:18:09,703 --> 03:18:15,883
you have suffered a little while, perfect,
establish, strengthen, and settle you.

3083
03:18:16,483 --> 03:18:19,903
To him be the glory and the power forever
and ever.

3084
03:18:20,623 --> 03:18:21,523
Amen.

3085
03:18:21,723 --> 03:18:28,423
Through Silvanus, our faithful brother, as I
consider him, I have written to you briefly,

3086
03:18:29,383 --> 03:18:34,943
exhorting and testifying that this is the
true grace of God in which you stand.

3087
03:18:35,543 --> 03:18:40,163
She who is in Babylon, chosen together
with you, greets you.

3088
03:18:40,763 --> 03:18:42,283
So does Mark, my son.

3089
03:18:43,163 --> 03:18:45,563
Greet one another with a kiss of love.

3090
03:18:45,954 --> 03:18:49,494
Peace be to all of you who are in Christ
Jesus.

3091
03:18:50,374 --> 03:18:51,274
Amen.

3092
03:18:52,074 --> 03:18:54,774
James, chapter one.

3093
03:18:54,814 --> 03:19:01,494
James, a servant of God and of the Lord
Jesus Christ, to the twelve

3094
03:19:01,534 --> 03:19:05,254
tribes which are in the Dispersion:
Greetings.

3095
03:19:05,294 --> 03:19:12,114
Count it all joy, my brothers, when you
fall into various temptations, knowing

3096
03:19:12,154 --> 03:19:15,094
that the testing of your faith produces
endurance.

3097
03:19:15,994 --> 03:19:22,334
Let endurance have its perfect work, that
you may be perfect and complete, lacking in

3098
03:19:22,374 --> 03:19:23,214
nothing.

3099
03:19:23,254 --> 03:19:29,974
But if any of you lacks wisdom, let him
ask of God, who gives to all liberally and

3100
03:19:30,014 --> 03:19:33,194
without reproach, and it will be given to
him.

3101
03:19:33,794 --> 03:19:40,454
But let him ask in faith, without any
doubting, for he who doubts is like a wave

3102
03:19:40,494 --> 03:19:43,654
of the sea, driven by the wind and tossed.

3103
03:19:44,174 --> 03:19:48,414
For that man shouldn’t think that he will
receive anything from the Lord.

3104
03:19:49,854 --> 03:19:53,854
He is a double-minded man, unstable in all
his ways.

3105
03:19:54,934 --> 03:20:01,374
Let the brother in humble circumstances glory
in his high position; and the rich, in

3106
03:20:01,414 --> 03:20:06,834
that he is made humble, because like the
flower in the grass, he will pass away.

3107
03:20:07,494 --> 03:20:13,874
For the sun arises with the scorching wind
and withers the grass; and the flower in it

3108
03:20:13,914 --> 03:20:17,114
falls, and the beauty of its appearance
perishes.

3109
03:20:18,254 --> 03:20:21,454
So the rich man will also fade away in his
pursuits.

3110
03:20:22,294 --> 03:20:28,954
Blessed is a person who endures temptation, for
when he has been approved, he will receive

3111
03:20:28,994 --> 03:20:33,554
the crown of life which the Lord promised
to those who love him.

3112
03:20:34,614 --> 03:20:41,254
Let no man say when he is tempted, “I am
tempted by God,” for God can’t

3113
03:20:41,294 --> 03:20:45,194
be tempted by evil, and he himself tempts
no one.

3114
03:20:45,794 --> 03:20:50,994
But each one is tempted when he is drawn
away by his own lust and enticed.

3115
03:20:51,934 --> 03:20:55,794
Then the lust, when it has conceived,
bears sin.

3116
03:20:56,834 --> 03:21:00,554
The sin, when it is full grown, produces
death.

3117
03:21:01,514 --> 03:21:03,754
Don’t be deceived, my beloved brothers.

3118
03:21:04,574 --> 03:21:11,314
Every good gift and every perfect gift is
from above, coming down from the Father

3119
03:21:11,354 --> 03:21:16,234
of lights, with whom can be no variation
nor turning shadow.

3120
03:21:16,634 --> 03:21:23,314
Of his own will he gave birth to us by the
word of truth, that we should be a kind of

3121
03:21:23,354 --> 03:21:24,854
first fruits of his creatures.

3122
03:21:25,974 --> 03:21:32,814
So, then, my beloved brothers, let every
man be swift to hear, slow

3123
03:21:32,854 --> 03:21:39,714
to speak, and slow to anger; for the
anger of man doesn’t produce the righteousness of

3124
03:21:39,754 --> 03:21:40,654
God.

3125
03:21:40,754 --> 03:21:47,434
Therefore, putting away all filthiness and
overflowing of wickedness, receive with

3126
03:21:47,474 --> 03:21:51,894
humility the implanted word, which is able
to save your souls.

3127
03:21:52,994 --> 03:21:58,354
But be doers of the word, and not only
hearers, deluding your own selves.

3128
03:21:59,194 --> 03:22:09,514
For if anyone is a hearer of the word and
not

3129
03:22:09,554 --> 03:22:10,357
a doer, he is like a man looking at
his natural face in a mirror; for he sees himself,

3130
03:22:10,397 --> 03:22:13,574
and goes away, and immediately forgets
what kind of man he was.

3131
03:22:14,154 --> 03:22:20,274
But he who looks into the perfect law
of freedom and continues, not being a hearer who

3132
03:22:20,314 --> 03:22:26,074
forgets but a doer of the work, this man
will be blessed in what he does.

3133
03:22:26,634 --> 03:22:32,054
If anyone amongst you thinks himself to
be religious while he doesn’t bridle his tongue,

3134
03:22:32,714 --> 03:22:36,614
but deceives his heart, this man’s
religion is worthless.

3135
03:22:37,394 --> 03:22:44,394
Pure religion and undefiled before our God
and Father is this: to visit the fatherless

3136
03:22:44,434 --> 03:22:49,834
and widows in their affliction, and to
keep oneself unstained by the world.

3137
03:22:50,994 --> 03:22:53,244
James, chapter two.

3138
03:22:53,284 --> 03:22:59,334
My brothers, don’t hold the faith of
our glorious Lord Jesus Christ with partiality.

3139
03:22:59,374 --> 03:23:05,914
For if a man with a gold ring, in fine
clothing, comes into your synagogue, and a

3140
03:23:05,954 --> 03:23:12,094
poor man in filthy clothing also comes in,
and you pay special attention to him who wears

3141
03:23:12,134 --> 03:23:19,254
the fine clothing and say, “Sit here in a
good place;” and you tell the poor man, “Stand

3142
03:23:19,294 --> 03:23:26,234
there,” or “Sit by my footstool”
haven’t you shown partiality amongst yourselves, and

3143
03:23:26,274 --> 03:23:28,194
become judges with evil thoughts?

3144
03:23:29,374 --> 03:23:30,874
Listen, my beloved brothers.

3145
03:23:31,383 --> 03:23:37,283
Didn’t God choose those who are poor in this
world to be rich in faith and heirs of the

3146
03:23:37,323 --> 03:23:39,843
Kingdom which he promised to those who
love him?

3147
03:23:40,783 --> 03:23:42,843
But you have dishonoured the poor man.

3148
03:23:43,663 --> 03:23:47,903
Don’t the rich oppress you and personally
drag you before the courts?

3149
03:23:48,743 --> 03:23:52,343
Don’t they blaspheme the honourable name
by which you are called?

3150
03:23:53,243 --> 03:23:59,583
However, if you fulfil the royal law
according to the Scripture, “You shall love your

3151
03:23:59,623 --> 03:24:02,043
neighbour as yourself,” you do well.

3152
03:24:02,963 --> 03:24:09,603
But if you show partiality, you commit
sin, being convicted by the law as transgressors.

3153
03:24:09,943 --> 03:24:15,903
For whoever keeps the whole law, and yet
stumbles in one point, he has become guilty

3154
03:24:15,943 --> 03:24:16,843
of all.

3155
03:24:17,453 --> 03:24:22,843
For he who said, “Do not commit adultery,”
also said, “Do not commit murder.”

3156
03:24:23,343 --> 03:24:28,803
Now if you do not commit adultery but
do murder, you have become a transgressor of the

3157
03:24:28,843 --> 03:24:29,743
law.

3158
03:24:29,783 --> 03:24:34,663
So speak and so do as men who are to be
judged by the law of freedom.

3159
03:24:35,683 --> 03:24:39,463
For judgement is without mercy to him who
has shown no mercy.

3160
03:24:40,623 --> 03:24:43,143
Mercy triumphs over judgement.

3161
03:24:43,183 --> 03:24:48,803
What good is it, my brothers, if a man
says he has faith, but has no works?

3162
03:24:49,623 --> 03:24:50,883
Can faith save him?

3163
03:24:51,343 --> 03:24:57,423
And if a brother or sister is naked and in
lack of daily food, and one of you tells them,

3164
03:24:57,683 --> 03:24:58,583
“Go in peace.

3165
03:24:59,023 --> 03:25:04,803
Be warmed and filled;” yet you didn’t give
them the things the body needs, what good

3166
03:25:04,843 --> 03:25:05,743
is it?

3167
03:25:06,163 --> 03:25:10,383
Even so faith, if it has no works, is dead
in itself.

3168
03:25:10,423 --> 03:25:15,763
Yes, a man will say, “You have faith, and
I have works.”

3169
03:25:16,643 --> 03:25:22,023
Show me your faith without works, and I
will show you my faith by my works.

3170
03:25:23,003 --> 03:25:24,863
You believe that God is one.

3171
03:25:25,743 --> 03:25:26,643
You do well.

3172
03:25:26,923 --> 03:25:29,083
The demons also believe—and shudder.

3173
03:25:30,303 --> 03:25:34,843
But do you want to know, vain man, that
faith apart from works is dead?

3174
03:25:34,883 --> 03:25:41,483
Wasn’t Abraham our father justified by works, in
that he offered up Isaac his son on

3175
03:25:41,523 --> 03:25:42,423
the altar?

3176
03:25:43,103 --> 03:25:48,103
You see that faith worked with his works,
and by works faith was perfected.

3177
03:25:48,645 --> 03:25:54,430
So the Scripture was fulfilled which says,
“Abraham believed God, and it was accounted

3178
03:25:54,470 --> 03:26:00,232
to him as righteousness,” and he was
called the friend of God.

3179
03:26:00,272 --> 03:26:07,001
You see then that by works a man is
justified, and not only by

3180
03:26:07,041 --> 03:26:07,484
faith.

3181
03:26:07,524 --> 03:26:14,253
In the same way, wasn’t Rahab the
prostitute also justified by works when she

3182
03:26:14,293 --> 03:26:18,605
received the messengers and sent them out
another way?

3183
03:26:18,645 --> 03:26:25,445
For as the body apart from the spirit is
dead, even so faith apart from works is dead.

3184
03:26:26,305 --> 03:26:28,665
James, chapter three.

3185
03:26:28,705 --> 03:26:35,325
Let not many of you be teachers, my
brothers, knowing that we will receive heavier judgement.

3186
03:26:35,365 --> 03:26:37,285
For we all stumble in many things.

3187
03:26:38,025 --> 03:26:44,185
Anyone who doesn’t stumble in word is a
perfect person, able to bridle the whole body

3188
03:26:44,225 --> 03:26:45,125
also.

3189
03:26:45,445 --> 03:26:52,205
Indeed, we put bits into the horses’ mouths so
that they may obey us, and we guide their

3190
03:26:52,245 --> 03:26:53,145
whole body.

3191
03:26:53,865 --> 03:27:00,405
Behold, the ships also, though they are so
big and are driven by fierce winds, are yet

3192
03:27:00,445 --> 03:27:04,505
guided by a very small rudder, wherever
the pilot desires.

3193
03:27:05,325 --> 03:27:09,365
So the tongue is also a little member, and
boasts great things.

3194
03:27:10,165 --> 03:27:13,605
See how a small fire can spread to a large
forest!

3195
03:27:14,545 --> 03:27:15,905
And the tongue is a fire.

3196
03:27:16,845 --> 03:27:22,205
The world of iniquity amongst our members
is the tongue, which defiles the whole body,

3197
03:27:22,245 --> 03:27:27,485
and sets on fire the course of nature, and
is set on fire by Gehenna.

3198
03:27:27,945 --> 03:27:34,445
For every kind of animal, bird, creeping
thing, and sea creature is tamed, and

3199
03:27:34,485 --> 03:27:38,985
has been tamed by mankind; but nobody can
tame the tongue.

3200
03:27:40,145 --> 03:27:43,345
It is a restless evil, full of deadly
poison.

3201
03:27:44,385 --> 03:27:50,465
With it we bless our God and Father, and with
it we curse men who are made in the image

3202
03:27:50,505 --> 03:27:51,405
of God.

3203
03:27:51,745 --> 03:27:54,245
Out of the same mouth comes blessing and
cursing.

3204
03:27:55,425 --> 03:27:58,585
My brothers, these things ought not to be
so.

3205
03:27:59,485 --> 03:28:03,565
Does a spring send out from the same
opening fresh and bitter water?

3206
03:28:04,365 --> 03:28:08,985
Can a fig tree, my brothers, yield olives,
or a vine figs?

3207
03:28:09,725 --> 03:28:13,405
Thus no spring yields both salt water and
fresh water.

3208
03:28:13,733 --> 03:28:16,593
Who is wise and understanding amongst you?

3209
03:28:17,593 --> 03:28:22,953
Let him show by his good conduct that his
deeds are done in gentleness of wisdom.

3210
03:28:23,933 --> 03:28:30,513
But if you have bitter jealousy and selfish
ambition in your heart, don’t boast and don’t

3211
03:28:30,553 --> 03:28:31,673
lie against the truth.

3212
03:28:32,393 --> 03:28:38,913
This wisdom is not that which comes down
from above, but is earthly, sensual, and

3213
03:28:38,953 --> 03:28:39,853
demonic.

3214
03:28:40,533 --> 03:28:46,593
For where jealousy and selfish ambition are,
there is confusion and every evil deed.

3215
03:28:47,213 --> 03:28:54,813
But the wisdom that is from above
is first pure, then peaceful, gentle, reasonable, full

3216
03:28:54,853 --> 03:28:59,893
of mercy and good fruits, without
partiality, and without hypocrisy.

3217
03:29:00,553 --> 03:29:05,293
Now the fruit of righteousness is sown in
peace by those who make peace.

3218
03:29:06,233 --> 03:29:08,573
James, chapter four.

3219
03:29:08,613 --> 03:29:11,473
Where do wars and fightings amongst you
come from?

3220
03:29:12,373 --> 03:29:15,593
Don’t they come from your pleasures that
war in your members?

3221
03:29:16,753 --> 03:29:18,533
You lust, and don’t have.

3222
03:29:19,273 --> 03:29:21,673
You murder and covet, and can’t obtain.

3223
03:29:22,813 --> 03:29:24,013
You fight and make war.

3224
03:29:24,833 --> 03:29:26,933
You don’t have, because you don’t ask.

3225
03:29:27,453 --> 03:29:33,413
You ask, and don’t receive, because you ask
with wrong motives, so that you may spend

3226
03:29:33,453 --> 03:29:34,353
it on your pleasures.

3227
03:29:35,553 --> 03:29:40,613
You adulterers and adulteresses, don’t you know
that friendship with the world is hostility

3228
03:29:40,653 --> 03:29:41,553
towards God?

3229
03:29:42,053 --> 03:29:47,133
Whoever therefore wants to be a friend of
the world makes himself an enemy of God.

3230
03:29:47,833 --> 03:29:53,433
Or do you think that the Scripture says in
vain, “The Spirit who lives in us yearns jealously”?

3231
03:29:54,193 --> 03:29:55,453
But he gives more grace.

3232
03:29:56,153 --> 03:30:01,573
Therefore it says, “God resists the proud,
but gives grace to the humble.”

3233
03:30:02,693 --> 03:30:04,473
Be subject therefore to God.

3234
03:30:04,913 --> 03:30:07,633
Resist the devil, and he will flee from
you.

3235
03:30:08,193 --> 03:30:11,093
Draw near to God, and he will draw near to
you.

3236
03:30:12,073 --> 03:30:13,493
Cleanse your hands, you sinners.

3237
03:30:14,313 --> 03:30:17,493
Purify your hearts, you double-minded.

3238
03:30:17,533 --> 03:30:19,293
Lament, mourn, and weep.

3239
03:30:19,893 --> 03:30:23,613
Let your laughter be turned to mourning
and your joy to gloom.

3240
03:30:24,193 --> 03:30:28,233
Humble yourselves in the sight of the
Lord, and he will exalt you.

3241
03:30:28,873 --> 03:30:30,913
Don’t speak against one another, brothers.

3242
03:30:31,442 --> 03:30:37,902
He who speaks against a brother and judges
his brother, speaks against the law and

3243
03:30:37,942 --> 03:30:39,002
judges the law.

3244
03:30:39,702 --> 03:30:44,822
But if you judge the law, you are not a
doer of the law but a judge.

3245
03:30:45,362 --> 03:30:49,682
Only one is the lawgiver, who is able to
save and to destroy.

3246
03:30:50,602 --> 03:30:52,662
But who are you to judge another?

3247
03:30:53,362 --> 03:30:59,842
Come now, you who say, “Today or tomorrow
let’s go into this city and

3248
03:30:59,882 --> 03:31:03,482
spend a year there, trade, and make a
profit.”

3249
03:31:04,542 --> 03:31:07,542
Yet you don’t know what your life will be
like tomorrow.

3250
03:31:07,582 --> 03:31:09,182
For what is your life?

3251
03:31:10,142 --> 03:31:15,382
For you are a vapour that appears for a
little time and then vanishes away.

3252
03:31:16,222 --> 03:31:22,522
For you ought to say, “If the Lord wills,
we will both live, and do this or that.”

3253
03:31:23,542 --> 03:31:25,702
But now you glory in your boasting.

3254
03:31:26,662 --> 03:31:28,382
All such boasting is evil.

3255
03:31:28,422 --> 03:31:34,382
To him therefore who knows to do good and
doesn’t do it, to him it is sin.

3256
03:31:35,402 --> 03:31:37,722
James, chapter five.

3257
03:31:37,762 --> 03:31:42,942
Come now, you rich, weep and howl for your
miseries that are coming on you.

3258
03:31:43,702 --> 03:31:48,202
Your riches are corrupted and your
garments are moth-eaten.

3259
03:31:48,242 --> 03:31:54,022
Your gold and your silver are corroded, and
their corrosion will be for a testimony against

3260
03:31:54,062 --> 03:31:57,022
you and will eat your flesh like fire.

3261
03:31:57,702 --> 03:32:00,242
You have laid up your treasure in the last
days.

3262
03:32:01,182 --> 03:32:06,962
Behold, the wages of the labourers who mowed
your fields, which you have kept back by

3263
03:32:07,002 --> 03:32:13,202
fraud, cry out; and the cries of those who
reaped have entered into the ears of the Lord

3264
03:32:13,242 --> 03:32:13,722
of Armies.

3265
03:32:13,762 --> 03:32:17,862
You have lived in luxury on the earth, and
taken your pleasure.

3266
03:32:18,722 --> 03:32:21,722
You have nourished your hearts as in a day
of slaughter.

3267
03:32:22,682 --> 03:32:26,162
You have condemned and you have murdered
the righteous one.

3268
03:32:27,362 --> 03:32:28,682
He doesn’t resist you.

3269
03:32:29,642 --> 03:32:33,322
Be patient therefore, brothers, until the
coming of the Lord.

3270
03:32:33,982 --> 03:32:40,142
Behold, the farmer waits for the precious
fruit of the earth, being patient over it,

3271
03:32:40,182 --> 03:32:44,522
until it receives the early and late rain.

3272
03:32:44,562 --> 03:32:45,942
You also be patient.

3273
03:32:46,842 --> 03:32:50,462
Establish your hearts, for the coming of
the Lord is at hand.

3274
03:32:50,786 --> 03:32:55,406
Don’t grumble, brothers, against one
another, so that you won’t be judged.

3275
03:32:56,726 --> 03:32:59,626
Behold, the judge stands at the door.

3276
03:33:00,726 --> 03:33:06,946
Take, brothers, for an example of suffering
and of perseverance, the prophets who spoke

3277
03:33:06,986 --> 03:33:08,326
in the name of the Lord.

3278
03:33:09,306 --> 03:33:12,026
Behold, we call them blessed who endured.

3279
03:33:12,866 --> 03:33:18,645
You have heard of the perseverance of Job
and have seen the Lord in the outcome, and

3280
03:33:18,686 --> 03:33:21,226
how the Lord is full of compassion and
mercy.

3281
03:33:22,426 --> 03:33:29,385
But above all things, my brothers, don’t
swear— not by heaven, or by the earth, or

3282
03:33:29,426 --> 03:33:35,905
by any other oath; but let your “yes” be
“yes”, and your “no”, “no”, so that

3283
03:33:35,946 --> 03:33:37,466
you don’t fall into hypocrisy.

3284
03:33:38,466 --> 03:33:40,346
Is any amongst you suffering?

3285
03:33:41,106 --> 03:33:42,006
Let him pray.

3286
03:33:42,706 --> 03:33:43,606
Is any cheerful?

3287
03:33:44,346 --> 03:33:45,346
Let him sing praises.

3288
03:33:46,406 --> 03:33:47,646
Is any amongst you sick?

3289
03:33:48,266 --> 03:33:54,405
Let him call for the elders of the
assembly, and let them pray over him, anointing him

3290
03:33:54,446 --> 03:34:00,366
with oil in the name of the Lord; and the
prayer of faith will heal him who is sick,

3291
03:34:01,066 --> 03:34:02,586
and the Lord will raise him up.

3292
03:34:03,346 --> 03:34:06,626
If he has committed sins, he will be
forgiven.

3293
03:34:07,426 --> 03:34:12,646
Confess your sins to one another and pray
for one another, that you may be healed.

3294
03:34:13,886 --> 03:34:18,046
The insistent prayer of a righteous person
is powerfully effective.

3295
03:34:19,006 --> 03:34:24,806
Elijah was a man with a nature like ours,
and he prayed earnestly that it might not rain,

3296
03:34:25,306 --> 03:34:29,026
and it didn’t rain on the earth for three
years and six months.

3297
03:34:29,666 --> 03:34:35,166
He prayed again, and the sky gave rain,
and the earth produced its fruit.

3298
03:34:35,786 --> 03:34:42,026
Brothers, if any amongst you wanders from the
truth and someone turns him back, let him

3299
03:34:42,066 --> 03:34:47,706
know that he who turns a sinner from the
error of his way will save a soul from death

3300
03:34:48,306 --> 03:34:50,146
and will cover a multitude of sins.

